    "calculator": "Unlabelled",
    "questionText": "Applecross SHS Semester 1, 2018 Section 2 Mathematics Methods Unit 1 5 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS SECTION AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF. Question 11 (6 marks) A thin pole stands vertically in the middle of a level playing ground. From point 𝐴 on the ground, the angle of elevation to the top of the pole, 𝑇, is 18º. From point 𝐵, also on the ground but 5.35 metres further from the foot of the pole than 𝐴, the angle of elevation to the top of the pole is 15º. (a) Draw a sketch to represent this information. (1 mark) (b) Showing use of trigonometry, determine the height of the pole. (5 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN002-112-4 Question 11 (6 marks) A thin pole stands vertically in the middle of a level playing ground. From point 𝐴 on the ground, the angle of elevation to the top of the pole, 𝑇, is 18º. From point 𝐵, also on the ground but 5.35 metres further from the foot of the pole than 𝐴, the angle of elevation to the top of the pole is 15º. (a) Draw a sketch to represent this information. (1 mark) (b) Showing use of trigonometry, determine the height of the post. (5 marks) Solution Specific behaviours ✓ sketch with right-angle, two given angles and distance AB Solution 𝐴𝑇 sin15 = 5.35 sin 3 ⇒𝐴𝑇= 26.46 ℎ= 26.46 × sin 18 = 8.18 Specific behaviours ✓ angle 𝐵𝑇𝐴 ✓ equation using sine rule ✓ solves for AT ✓ use of trig in right triangle ✓ determines h",
