    "questionText": "Applecross SHS Semester 1, 2018 Section 2 Mathematics Methods Unit 1 6 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS SECTION AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF. Question 12 (7 marks) Let 𝑓(𝑥) = 4 3 −𝑥 and 𝑔(𝑥) = 1 𝑥+ 𝑝+ 𝑞, where 𝑝 and 𝑞 are constants. The graph of 𝑦= 𝑔(𝑥) is shown below. (a) Sketch the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) on the axes above. (3 marks) (b) Determine the values of 𝑝 and 𝑞. (2 marks) (c) Solve the equation 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑔(𝑥), giving your solution(s) to one decimal place. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN002-112-4 Question 12 (7 marks) Let 𝑓(𝑥) = 4 3 −𝑥 and 𝑔(𝑥) = 1 𝑥+ 𝑝+ 𝑞, where 𝑝 and 𝑞 are constants. The graph of 𝑦= 𝑔(𝑥) is shown below. (a) Sketch the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) on the axes above. (3 marks) (b) Determine the values of 𝑝 and 𝑞. (2 marks) (c) Solve the equation 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑔(𝑥), giving your solution(s) to one decimal place. (2 marks) Solution See graph Specific behaviours ✓ asymptotes ✓ y-intercept ✓ accuracy [i.e. thu' at least 3 of (-1,1), (1,2), (2,4), (4,-4) or (7,-1)] Solution 𝑝= 2, 𝑞= −3 Specific behaviours ✓ value of 𝑝 ✓ value of 𝑞 Solution 𝑥= −1.7, 𝑥= 4.4 Specific behaviours ✓ one solution ✓ second solution (Rounding for guidance only but penalise answers given as coordinates)",
