    "questionText": "Applecross SHS Semester 1, 2018 Section 2 Mathematics Methods Unit 1 8 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS SECTION AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF. Question 14 (10 marks) A logo with triangular outline 𝐴𝐵𝐶 contains a shaded segment bounded by the straight line 𝑃𝑀 and the circular arc 𝑃𝑀 with centre 𝐵 and radius 𝐵𝑀= 18 cm, as shown below. Given that ∠𝐴𝐵𝐶= 5𝜋 12, ∠𝐵𝐶𝐴= 2∠𝐵𝐴𝐶 and 𝑀 is the midpoint of 𝐵𝐶, determine (a) the size of ∠𝐴𝐵𝐶 in degrees. (1 mark) (b) the area of the shaded segment. (2 marks) (c) the perimeter of the shaded segment. (3 marks) Applecross SHS Semester 1, 2018 Section 2 Mathematics Methods Unit 1 9 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS SECTION AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF. (d) the area of triangle 𝐴𝐵𝐶. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN002-112-4 Question 14 (10 marks) A logo with triangular outline 𝐴𝐵𝐶 contains a shaded segment bounded by the straight line 𝑃𝑀 and the circular arc 𝑃𝑀 with centre 𝐵 and radius 𝐵𝑀= 18 cm, as shown below. Given that ∠𝐴𝐵𝐶= 5𝜋 12, ∠𝐵𝐶𝐴= 2∠𝐵𝐴𝐶 and 𝑀 is the midpoint of 𝐵𝐶, determine (a) the size of ∠𝐴𝐵𝐶 in degrees. (1 mark) (b) the area of the shaded segment. (2 marks) (c) the perimeter of the shaded segment. (3 marks) Solution 𝐴= 1 2 (18)2 (5𝜋 12 −sin(5𝜋 12)) ≈55.6 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates substitution into segment area formula ✓ evaluates area Solution 𝑃𝑀𝑎𝑟𝑐= 18 × 5𝜋 12 = 15𝜋 2 ≈23.56 𝑏= √182 + 182 −2(18)(18) cos 75 ≈21.92 Perimeter = 23.56 + 21.92 ≈45.5 cm Specific behaviours ✓ calculates arc length ✓ indicates use of cosine rule to find 𝑃𝑀 ✓ evaluates 𝑃𝑀 and states perimeter Solution 5𝜋 12 × 180 𝜋 = 75° Specific behaviours ✓ converts angle",
