    "questionText": "Applecross SHS Semester 1, 2018 Section 2 Mathematics Methods Unit 1 11 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS SECTION AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF. Question 16 (6 marks) (a) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) is shown in bold below. The graphs of 𝑦= −𝑓(𝑥), 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥+ 𝑝) and 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) + 𝑞 are also shown, where 𝑝 and 𝑞 are constants. Clearly label the remaining graphs with 𝑦= −𝑓(𝑥), 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥+ 𝑝) or 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) + 𝑞. (3 marks) (b) The one-to-one relation 𝑦= 7 −3𝑥 has domain and range given by {𝑥: 𝑥= −2, 3, 𝑎} and {𝑦: 𝑦= −8, −2, 𝑏} respectively. Determine the values of constants 𝑎 and 𝑏. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN002-112-4 Question 16 (6 marks) (a) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) is shown in bold below. The graphs of 𝑦= −𝑓(𝑥), 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥+ 𝑝) and 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) + 𝑞 are also shown, where 𝑝 and 𝑞 are constants. Clearly label the remaining graphs with 𝑦= −𝑓(𝑥), 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥+ 𝑝) or 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) + 𝑞. (3 marks) (b) The one-to-one relation 𝑦= 7 −3𝑥 has domain and range given by {𝑥: 𝑥= −2, 3, 𝑎} and {𝑦: 𝑦= −8, −2, 𝑏} respectively. Determine the values of constants 𝑎 and 𝑏. (3 marks) Solution See graph Specific behaviours ✓✓✓ each correct label Solution 𝑥= 3, 𝑦= −2 𝑥= −2, 𝑦= 13 = 𝑏 𝑥= 𝑎, 𝑦= 7 −3𝑎= −8 ⇒𝑎= 5 Specific behaviours ✓ value of 𝑏 ✓ indicates 𝑎 is mapped onto −8 ✓ solves for value of 𝑎",
