    "questionText": "Applecross SHS Semester 1, 2020 Section 2 Mathematics Methods Unit 1&2 3 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS SECTION AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF. Section Two: Calculator-assumed 65% (98 Marks) This section has thirteen questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 9 (5 marks) Shape 𝐴𝑂𝐵𝐶𝐷𝐴 below consists of sector 𝐵𝑂𝐶 of circle centre 𝑂 joined to sector 𝐷𝑂𝐴 of a different circle, also centre 𝑂. 𝐴𝐵 is a line of length 65 cm, arc 𝐴𝐷 is 12 cm long and ∠𝐴𝑂𝐷= 0.32 radians. (a) Determine the length 𝑂𝐴. (2 marks) (b) Determine the area of the shape. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 3 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN002-152-4 Section Two: Calculator-assumed 65% (98 Marks) This section has thirteen questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 9 (5 marks) Shape 𝐴𝑂𝐵𝐶𝐷𝐴 below consists of sector 𝐵𝑂𝐶 of circle centre 𝑂 joined to sector 𝐷𝑂𝐴 of a different circle, also centre 𝑂. 𝐴𝐵 is a straight line of length 65 cm, arc 𝐴𝐷 is 12 cm long and ∠𝐴𝑂𝐷= 0.32 radians. (a) Determine the length 𝑂𝐴. (2 marks) (b) Determine the area of the shape. (3 marks) Solution Let 𝑂𝐴= 𝑅 so that 0.32𝑅= 12 𝑅= 37.5 cm Specific behaviours ✓ correct use of arc length ✓ correct length Solution 𝐴𝐷𝑂𝐴= 1 2 × 37.52 × 0.32 = 225 Let 𝑂𝐵= 𝑟 𝑟= 65 −37.5 = 27.5 𝐴𝐵𝑂𝐶= 1 2 × 27.52(𝜋−0.32) = 1067 Area = 225 + 1067 = 1 292 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ area of sector 𝐷𝑂𝐴 ✓ radius and angle of sector 𝐵𝑂𝐶 ✓ area of shape",
    "questionImage": "generated/resource-previews/docx-pdf-cache-year-11-mathematics-methods-section-2-semeste-p003-question-b416d96868.jpg",
