    "calculator": "Unlabelled",
    "questionText": "Applecross SHS Semester 1, 2020 Section 2 Mathematics Methods Unit 1&2 7 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS SECTION AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF. Question 13 (6 marks) The graph 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥), where 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 𝑐 has a turning point at (2, −7). (a) State the equation of the line of symmetry for the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥). (1 mark) (b) Determine the value of the constant 𝑏 and the value of the constant 𝑐. (3 marks) (c) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) is translated 3 units to the left and 2 units upwards. Determine the equation of the resulting curve. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN002-152-4 Question 13 (6 marks) The graph 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥), where 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 𝑐 has a turning point at (2, −7). (a) State the equation of the line of symmetry for the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥). (1 mark) (b) Determine the value of the constant 𝑏 and the value of the constant 𝑐. (3 marks) (c) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) is translated 3 units to the left and 2 units upwards. Determine the equation of the resulting curve. (2 marks) Solution 𝑥= 2 Specific behaviours ✓ correct equation Solution 𝑓(𝑥) = (𝑥−2)2 −7 = 𝑥2 −4𝑥+ 4 −7 𝑏= −4 𝑐= −3 Specific behaviours ✓ writes 𝑓(𝑥) in squared form ✓ value of 𝑏 ✓ value of 𝑐 Solution New turning point at (2 −3, −7 + 2) = (−1, −5). Equation is 𝑦= (𝑥+ 1)2 −5 = 𝑥2 + 2𝑥−4 Specific behaviours ✓ identifies new turning point ✓ correct equation (either form)",
