    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions SN018-132-1 Question 8 (7 marks) (a) Evaluate sin(39𝜋 4 ). (2 marks) (b) 𝐴 is an acute angle and 𝐵 is an obtuse angle such that cos 𝐴= 1 3 and sin 𝐵= 2 3. (i) Show that sin 𝐴= 2√2 3 and determine the value of cos 𝐵. (3 marks) (ii) Determine the value of sin(𝐴+ 𝐵) as a single fraction. (2 marks) Mathematics Department Year 11 Mathematics Methods Semester 1 Examination, 2019 Question/Answer Booklet MATHEMATICS METHODS UNIT 1 Section Two: Calculator Assumed Student Name: _____________________________________________ Time allowed for this section Reading time before commencing work: ten minutes Working time: one hundred minutes Materials required/recommended for this section To be provided by the supervisor This Question/Answer booklet Formula sheet (retained from Section One) To be provided by the candidate Standard items: pens (blue/black preferred), pencils (including coloured), sharpener, correction fluid/tape, eraser, ruler, highlighters Special items: drawing instruments, templates, notes on one unfolded sheet of A4 paper, and up to three calculators approved for use in this examination Important note to candidates No other items may be taken into the examination room. It is your responsibility to ensure that you do not have any unauthorised material. If you have any unauthorised material with you, hand it to the supervisor before reading any further. Fix student label here",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions SN018-132-3 Question 8 (7 marks) (a) Evaluate sinቀ39𝜋𝜋 4 ቁ. (2 marks) (b) 𝐴𝐴 is an acute angle and 𝐵𝐵 is an obtuse angle such that cos 𝐴𝐴= 1 3 and sin 𝐵𝐵= 2 3. (i) Show that sin 𝐴𝐴= 2√2 3 and determine the value of cos 𝐵𝐵. (3 marks) (ii) Determine the value of sin(𝐴𝐴+ 𝐵𝐵) as a single fraction. (2 marks) Solution sin(𝐴𝐴+ 𝐵𝐵) = 2√2 3 × ቆ−√5 3 ቇ+ 1 3 × 2 3 = 2 −2√10 9 Specific behaviours  substitutes correctly  correct value as single fraction Solution sin39𝜋𝜋 4 = sin (39 −32)𝜋𝜋 4 = sin7𝜋𝜋 4 sin 7𝜋𝜋 4 = −sin𝜋𝜋 4 = −1 √2 = −√2 2 Specific behaviours  reduces angle  exact value Solution sin2 𝐴𝐴= 1 −൬1 3൰ 2 = 8 9 ⇒sin𝐴𝐴= √8 3 = 2√2 3 cos2 𝐵𝐵= 1 −൬2 3൰ 2 = 5 9 cos 𝐵𝐵= −√5 3 Specific behaviours  indicates how to obtain sin2 𝐴𝐴  obtains cos2 𝐵𝐵  correct value of cos 𝐵𝐵 If right triangles are used, then: uses Pythagoras’ to show value of sin 𝐴𝐴 obtains the absolute value of cos 𝐵𝐵  correct value of cos 𝐵𝐵",
