    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 3 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-2 Section Two: Calculator-assumed 65% (98 Marks) This section has fourteen (14) questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 9 (4 marks) (a) The points 𝐴𝐴 and 𝐵𝐵 have coordinates (7, −2) and (−3, 6) respectively. If 𝐴𝐴 is the midpoint of 𝐵𝐵 and 𝐶𝐶, determine the coordinates of 𝐶𝐶. (2 marks) (b) The points 𝐷𝐷 and 𝐸𝐸 have coordinates (−2𝑝𝑝, 𝑞𝑞) and (3𝑞𝑞, −2𝑝𝑝) respectively, where 𝑝𝑝 and 𝑞𝑞 are constants. Determine the value of 𝑝𝑝 and the value of 𝑞𝑞 if the midpoint of 𝐷𝐷 and 𝐸𝐸 is at (11, −7). (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 3 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-8 Section Two: Calculator-assumed 65% (98 Marks) This section has fourteen (14) questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 9 (4 marks) (a) The points 𝐴𝐴 and 𝐵𝐵 have coordinates (7, −2) and (−3, 6) respectively. If 𝐴𝐴 is the midpoint of 𝐵𝐵 and 𝐶𝐶, determine the coordinates of 𝐶𝐶. (2 marks) (b) The points 𝐷𝐷 and 𝐸𝐸 have coordinates (−2𝑝𝑝, 𝑞𝑞) and (3𝑞𝑞, −2𝑝𝑝) respectively, where 𝑝𝑝 and 𝑞𝑞 are constants. Determine the value of 𝑝𝑝 and the value of 𝑞𝑞 if the midpoint of 𝐷𝐷 and 𝐸𝐸 is at (11, −7). (2 marks) Solution If 𝐶𝐶(𝑥𝑥, 𝑦𝑦) then −3 + 𝑥𝑥 2 = 7 ⇒𝑥𝑥= 17 and 6 + 𝑦𝑦 2 = −2 ⇒𝑦𝑦= −10 𝐶𝐶(17, −10) Specific behaviours  writes equations for midpoints or uses horizontal and vertical distance between points  obtains the correct coordinates of 𝐶𝐶 Solution −2𝑝𝑝+ 3𝑞𝑞 2 = 11 and 𝑞𝑞−2𝑝𝑝 2 = −7 Solve simultaneously CAS to get 𝑝𝑝= 16, 𝑞𝑞= 18 Specific behaviours  value of 𝑝𝑝  value of 𝑞𝑞",
