    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 6 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-2 Question 11 (7 marks) Line 𝐿𝐿 has equation 𝑥𝑥 5 + 𝑦𝑦 3 = 1. (a) State the coordinates of the point where 𝐿𝐿 intersects the 𝑥𝑥-axis. (1 mark) (b) State, with justification, if 𝐿𝐿 is parallel to the line with equation 𝑦𝑦= 0.6𝑥𝑥+ 4. (2 marks) (c) Determine the equation of line 𝑃𝑃 that is perpendicular to 𝐿𝐿 and passes through the point with coordinates (30, 19). (2 marks) (d) Determine the coordinates of the point of intersection of 𝐿𝐿 and 𝑃𝑃. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN018-132-8 Question 11 (7 marks) Line 𝐿𝐿 has equation 𝑥𝑥 5 + 𝑦𝑦 3 = 1. (a) State the coordinates of the point where 𝐿𝐿 intersects the 𝑥𝑥-axis. (1 mark) (b) State, with justification, if 𝐿𝐿 is parallel to the line with equation 𝑦𝑦= 0.6𝑥𝑥+ 4. (2 marks) (c) Determine the equation of line 𝑃𝑃 that is perpendicular to 𝐿𝐿 and passes through the point with coordinates (30, 19). (2 marks) (d) Determine the coordinates of the point of intersection of 𝐿𝐿 and 𝑃𝑃. (2 marks) Solution 𝑦𝑦= 3 −3 5 𝑥𝑥 𝐿𝐿 is not parallel to this line as gradients are different: − 3 5 ≠0.6. Specific behaviours  indicates gradient of 𝐿𝐿  states not parallel, comparing gradients Solution 𝑦𝑦= 0 ⇒𝑥𝑥= 5 At (5, 0) Specific behaviours  correct coordinates (no marks if not listed as coordinates) Solution 𝑦𝑦−19 = 5 3 (𝑥𝑥−30) Specific behaviours  indicates perpendicular gradient  correct equation Solution 𝑃𝑃: 𝑦𝑦= 5 3 𝑥𝑥−31 5 3 𝑥𝑥−31 = 3 −3 5 𝑥𝑥⇒34 15 𝑥𝑥= 34 ⇒𝑥𝑥= 15 𝑦𝑦= 5 3 (15) −31 = −6 Intersect at (15, −6) Specific behaviours  equates equations and solves for 𝑥𝑥  correct coordinates Award 2 marks if just the correct answer is listed.",
