    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-2 Question 12 (8 marks) (a) The variables 𝑄𝑄 and 𝑣𝑣 are directly proportional and when 𝑣𝑣= 40, 𝑄𝑄= 10. (i) Determine an equation for the relationship between 𝑄𝑄 and 𝑣𝑣. (2 marks) (ii) State the value of 𝑄𝑄 when 𝑣𝑣= 80. (1 mark) (b) The time, 𝑡𝑡 minutes, that a car takes to travel 250 m at a constant speed of 𝑠𝑠 kmh-1 is given by the formula 𝑡𝑡= 𝑘𝑘 𝑠𝑠 . (i) Determine the value of the constant 𝑘𝑘, given that when 𝑠𝑠= 15, 𝑡𝑡= 60. (1 mark) (ii) Determine the value of 𝑡𝑡 when 𝑠𝑠= 10. (1 mark) (iii) On the axes below, draw a graph to show how 𝑡𝑡 varies with 𝑠𝑠. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-8 Question 12 (8 marks) (a) The variables 𝑄𝑄 and 𝑣𝑣 are directly proportional and when 𝑣𝑣= 40, 𝑄𝑄= 10. (i) Determine an equation for the relationship between 𝑄𝑄 and 𝑣𝑣. (2 marks) (ii) State the value of 𝑄𝑄 when 𝑣𝑣= 80. (1 mark) (b) The time, 𝑡𝑡 minutes, that a car takes to travel 250 m at a constant speed of 𝑠𝑠 kmh-1 is given by the formula 𝑡𝑡= 𝑘𝑘 𝑠𝑠 . (i) Determine the value of the constant 𝑘𝑘, given that when 𝑠𝑠= 15, 𝑡𝑡= 60. (1 mark) (ii) Determine the value of 𝑡𝑡 when 𝑠𝑠= 10. (1 mark) (iii) On the axes below, draw a graph to show how 𝑡𝑡 varies with 𝑠𝑠. (3 marks) Solution 𝑄𝑄= 𝑚𝑚𝑚𝑚, 𝑚𝑚= 10 40 = 0.25 ⇒𝑄𝑄= 0.25𝑣𝑣 Specific behaviours  uses correct linear relationship  calculates the proportion constant Solution 𝑄𝑄= 0.25(80) = 20 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution 𝑡𝑡= 900 ÷ 10 = 90 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution 60 = 𝑘𝑘 15 ⇒𝑘𝑘= 900 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution See graph. Key points: (10, 90), (15, 60), (30, 30), (60, 15), (90, 10) Specific behaviours  plots at least 2 key points  plots all key points  smooth curve v = 4Q is also correct and is to be awarded full marks",
