    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 8 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-2 Question 13 (8 marks) The graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) is shown below where 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = 𝑎𝑎 𝑏𝑏−𝑥𝑥 . (a) State the value of the constant 𝑎𝑎 and the value of the constant 𝑏𝑏. (3 marks) (b) The hyperbola shown above has two asymptotes. State their equations. (2 marks) (c) Describe how to transform the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) to obtain the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥+ 1) and state the domain and range of the transformed function. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN018-132-8 Question 13 (8 marks) The graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) is shown below where 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = 𝑎𝑎 𝑏𝑏−𝑥𝑥 . (a) State the value of the constant 𝑎𝑎 and the value of the constant 𝑏𝑏. (3 marks) (b) The hyperbola shown above has two asymptotes. State their equations. (2 marks) (c) Describe how to transform the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) to obtain the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥+ 1) and state the domain and range of the transformed function. (3 marks) Solution 𝑥𝑥= 2, 𝑦𝑦= 0 Specific behaviours  vertical asymptote  horizontal asymptote Solution Translate the graph 1 unit to left. Domain: 𝑥𝑥≠1 Range: 𝑦𝑦≠0 Specific behaviours  transformation  domain  range Solution 𝑏𝑏= 2 Using (3, 4) ⇒4 = 𝑎𝑎÷ (2 −3) ⇒𝑎𝑎= −4 Specific behaviours  value of 𝑏𝑏  uses point on curve  value of 𝑎𝑎",
