    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-2 Question 14 (8 marks) (a) Convert, giving an exact answer (i) 40° to radians. (1 mark) (ii) 0.2 radians to degrees. (1 mark) (b) Calculate, to the nearest degree, the acute angle between the line 𝑦𝑦= 4.5𝑥𝑥+ 2 and the line 𝑦𝑦= 1.5𝑥𝑥−3. (3 marks) (c) The sides adjacent to the right-angle in a right triangle have lengths 36 cm and 77 cm. If the smallest angle in the triangle is 𝛼𝛼, then determine an exact value for (i) tan 𝛼𝛼. (1 mark) (ii) cos(90° −𝛼𝛼). (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-8 Question 14 (8 marks) (a) Convert, giving an exact answer (i) 40° to radians. (1 mark) (ii) 0.2 radians to degrees. (1 mark) (b) Calculate, to the nearest degree, the acute angle between the line 𝑦𝑦= 4.5𝑥𝑥+ 2 and the line 𝑦𝑦= 1.5𝑥𝑥−3. (3 marks) (c) The sides adjacent to the right-angle in a right triangle have lengths 36 cm and 77 cm. If the smallest angle in the triangle is 𝛼𝛼, then determine an exact value for (i) tan 𝛼𝛼. (1 mark) (ii) cos(90° −𝛼𝛼). (2 marks) Solution 2𝜋𝜋 9 Specific behaviours  exact value Solution 36 𝜋𝜋 Specific behaviours  exact value Solution 𝜃𝜃1 = tan−1 4.5 = 77.5 𝜃𝜃2 = tan−1 1.5 = 56.3 𝜃𝜃2 −𝜃𝜃1 = 21° Specific behaviours  indicates use of tan−1 𝑚𝑚  one correct angle with 𝑥𝑥-axis  correct angle between lines Solution tan 𝛼𝛼= 36 77 Specific behaviours  correct ratio Solution ඥ362 + 772 = 85 cos(90° −𝛼𝛼) = 36 85 Specific behaviours  calculates length of hypotenuse  correct ratio",
