    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-2 Question 16 (7 marks) In shape 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂 below, ∠𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 117° and 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴, 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 are diameters of the circle with centre 𝑂𝑂 and radius 42 cm. (a) Calculate the perimeter of 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂. (4 marks) (b) Calculate the area of 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-8 Question 16 (7 marks) In shape 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂 below, ∠𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 117° and 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴, 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 are diameters of the circle with centre 𝑂𝑂 and radius 42 cm. (a) Calculate the perimeter of 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂. (4 marks) (b) Calculate the area of 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂. (3 marks) Solution 117° = 13𝜋𝜋 20 , 𝜋𝜋−13𝜋𝜋 20 = 7𝜋𝜋 20 = 63° 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴, 𝐷𝐷𝐷𝐷: 42 × 13𝜋𝜋 20 = 273𝜋𝜋 10 ≈85.765 𝐵𝐵𝐶𝐶2 = 422 + 422 −2(42)(42) cos 63 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵≈43.9 𝑃𝑃𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇= 2(42) + 2(85.765) + 43.9 ≈299 cm Specific behaviours  indicates length of arc 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴  indicates use of cosine rule for 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵  correct length 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵  correct total perimeter Solution 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴+ 𝐷𝐷𝐷𝐷𝐷𝐷: 2 × 1 2 × 422 × 13𝜋𝜋 20 = 5733𝜋𝜋 5 ≈3602 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵: 1 2 (42)(42) sin 63 ≈786 𝐴𝐴𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇𝑇= 3602 + 786 = 4 388 cm2 Specific behaviours  sector area 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴  triangle area 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵  correct total area",
