    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 12 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-2 Question 17 (7 marks) A small mass, attached to the bottom of a spring, oscillated up and down. The distance, 𝑑𝑑 cm, of the mass from the top of the spring after 𝑡𝑡 seconds can be modelled by 𝑑𝑑= 45 + 35 sin൬3𝜋𝜋𝜋𝜋 4 ൰ (a) Sketch the graph of 𝑑𝑑 against 𝑡𝑡 on the axes below for 0 ≤𝑡𝑡≤3. (3 marks) (b) Mark on your graph point 𝑀𝑀, where the mass is 40 cm from the top of the spring and moving downwards. (1 mark) (c) Determine (i) the maximum distance of the mass from the top of the spring. (1 mark) (ii) the time taken for the mass to first return to its initial position. (1 mark) (iii) the distance moved by the weight between 𝑡𝑡= 1 and 𝑡𝑡= 2. (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN018-132-8 Question 17 (7 marks) A small mass, attached to the bottom of a spring, oscillated up and down. The distance, 𝑑𝑑 cm, of the mass from the top of the spring after 𝑡𝑡 seconds can be modelled by 𝑑𝑑= 45 + 35 sin൬3𝜋𝜋𝜋𝜋 4 ൰ (a) Sketch the graph on the axes below for 0 ≤𝑡𝑡≤3. (3 marks) (b) Mark on your graph point 𝑀𝑀, where the mass is 40 cm from the top of the spring and moving downwards. (1 mark) (c) Determine (i) the maximum distance of the mass from the top of the spring. (1 mark) (ii) the time taken for the mass to first return to its initial position. (1 mark) (iii) the distance moved by the mass between 𝑡𝑡= 1 and 𝑡𝑡= 2. (1 mark) Solution 80 cm Specific behaviours  correct distance Solution 𝑑𝑑(1) −𝑑𝑑(2) = 69.75 −10 = 59.75 cm Specific behaviours  correct distance Solution 𝑡𝑡= 4 3 = 1. 3ത s Specific behaviours  correct time Solutions (a), (b) See graph Specific behaviours  𝑦𝑦-intercept and (3, 70)  max and min  single smooth curve  accurately locates 𝑀𝑀",
