    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-2 Question 18 (8 marks) (a) The equation of the axis of symmetry for the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 2𝑥𝑥2 + 8𝑥𝑥+ 5 is 𝑥𝑥= 𝑚𝑚. Determine the value of 𝑚𝑚, using a method that does not refer to the graph of the parabola. (2 marks) (b) A parabola with equation 𝑦𝑦= 𝑎𝑎𝑥𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑏𝑏𝑏+ 𝑐𝑐 has a turning point at (4, −5) and passes through the point (2, −17). Determine the value of 𝑎𝑎, the value of 𝑏𝑏 and the value of 𝑐𝑐. (3 marks) (c) Determine the value of the discriminant for the quadratic equation 4𝑥𝑥2 −28𝑥𝑥+ 47 = 0 and use it to explain how many solutions the equation (𝑥𝑥+ 3)(4𝑥𝑥2 −28𝑥𝑥+ 47) = 0 will have. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-8 Question 18 (8 marks) (a) The equation of the axis of symmetry for the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 2𝑥𝑥2 + 8𝑥𝑥+ 5 is 𝑥𝑥= 𝑚𝑚. Determine the value of 𝑚𝑚, using a method that does not refer to the graph of the parabola. (2 marks) (b) A parabola with equation 𝑦𝑦= 𝑎𝑎𝑥𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑏𝑏𝑏+ 𝑐𝑐 has a turning point at (4, −5) and passes through the point (2, −17). Determine the value of 𝑎𝑎, the value of 𝑏𝑏 and the value of 𝑐𝑐. (3 marks) (c) Determine the value of the discriminant for the quadratic equation 4𝑥𝑥2 −28𝑥𝑥+ 47 = 0 and use it to explain how many solutions the equation (𝑥𝑥+ 3)(4𝑥𝑥2 −28𝑥𝑥+ 47) = 0 will have. (3 marks) Solution 𝑥𝑥= − 8 2 × 2 = −2 𝑚𝑚= −2 𝑦𝑦= 2(𝑥𝑥+ 2)2 + 𝑐𝑐 ∴𝑚𝑚= −2 Specific behaviours  uses 𝑥𝑥= −𝑏𝑏÷ (2𝑎𝑎) or partially completes the square  value of 𝑚𝑚 Solution 𝑑𝑑= (−28)2 −4(4)(47) = 32 When 𝑑𝑑> 0, quadratic will have two solutions. Hence equation will have three solutions - one from the linear factor and two from the quadratic factor. Specific behaviours  value of discriminant  uses discriminant to say quadratic will have two solutions  explains why equation has three solutions Solution 𝑦𝑦= 𝑎𝑎(𝑥𝑥−4)2 −5 −17 = 𝑎𝑎(2 −4)2 −5 ⇒𝑎𝑎= −",
