    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 14 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-2 Question 19 (6 marks) Let 𝑝𝑝= cos 130° and 𝑞𝑞= sin 35°. Give your answers to the following in terms of 𝑝𝑝 and/or 𝑞𝑞. (a) Write down an expression for (i) sin 145°. (1 mark) (ii) cos 50°. (1 mark) (b) Determine an expression for cos 145°. (3 marks) (c) Hence, determine an expression for tan 145°. (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN018-132-8 Question 19 (6 marks) Let 𝑝𝑝= cos 130° and 𝑞𝑞= sin 35°. Give your answers to the following in terms of 𝑝𝑝 and/or 𝑞𝑞. (a) Write down an expression for (i) sin 145°. (1 mark) (ii) cos 50°. (1 mark) (b) Determine an expression for cos 145°. (3 marks) (c) Determine an expression for tan 145°. (1 mark) Solution sin145° = sin 35° = 𝑞𝑞 Specific behaviours  correct expression Solution cos 50° = −cos 130° = −𝑝𝑝 Specific behaviours  correct expression Solution tan 145° = sin 145° cos 145° = − 𝑞𝑞 ඥ1 −𝑞𝑞2 Specific behaviours  correct expression Solution cos2 145° + sin2 145° = 1 cos2 145° = 1 −𝑞𝑞2 cos 145° = ±ඥ1 −𝑞𝑞2 but cos 145° < 0 ⇒cos 145° = −ඥ1 −𝑞𝑞2 Specific behaviours  indicates use of sin2 𝜃𝜃+ cos2 𝜃𝜃= 1  expression for cos2 145°  correct expression",
