    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-2 Question 20 (9 marks) (a) Without evaluating, show that: (3 marks) cos 15° cos 65° + sin 15° sin65° = sin 140° (b) Simplify sin(𝐴𝐴+ 𝐵𝐵) cos 𝐵𝐵−cos(𝐴𝐴+ 𝐵𝐵) sin(𝐵𝐵). (2 marks) (c) (i) Show that √2sin(𝑥𝑥+ 45°) = sin 𝑥𝑥 + cos 𝑥𝑥 (2 marks) (ii) Hence, show that the exact value of sin 75° = (1+ √3) 2√2 (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-8 Question 20 (9 marks) (a) Show, using one or more identities from the formula sheet and without using the value of any trigonometric term, that (3 marks) cos 15° cos 65° + sin 15° sin65° = sin140° (b) Simplify sin(𝐴𝐴+ 𝐵𝐵) cos 𝐵𝐵−cos(𝐴𝐴+ 𝐵𝐵) sin(𝐵𝐵). (2 marks) (c) (i) Show that √2sin(𝑥𝑥+ 45°) = sin 𝑥𝑥 + cos 𝑥𝑥 (2 marks) (ii) Hence, show that the exact value of sin 75° = (1+ √3) 2√2 (2 marks) Solution sin(𝐴𝐴+ 𝐵𝐵) cos 𝐵𝐵−cos(𝐴𝐴+ 𝐵𝐵) sin(𝐵𝐵) = sin(𝐴𝐴+ 𝐵𝐵−𝐵𝐵) = sin𝐴𝐴 Specific behaviours  indicates use of difference identity  correct result Solution cos 15° cos 65° + sin15° sin65° = cos(65° −15°) = cos 50° = sin(90° + 50°) = sin 140° Specific behaviours  shows uses of difference identity  reduces LHS to cos 50°  shows use of relationships between trigonometric ratios to obtain result Solution =  correctly expands LHS  concludes correctly Solution = Therefore sin 75° = (1+ √3) 2√2 Specific behaviours  substitutes x = 30 into expression in (c) (i)  uses exact values to obtain correct conclusion",
