    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 16 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN018-132-2 Question 21 (8 marks) (a) The circle shown has centre 𝑂𝑂 and diameter 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 of length 50 cm. Determine the shaded area given that 2 × ∠𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 3 × ∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵. (4 marks) (b) A sector of a circle has a perimeter of 112 cm and an area of 735 cm2. Determine all possible values for the radius of the circle. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED SN018-132-8 Question 21 (8 marks) (a) The circle shown has centre 𝑂𝑂 and diameter 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 of length 50 cm. Determine the shaded area given that 2 × ∠𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 3 × ∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵. (4 marks) (b) A sector of a circle has a perimeter of 112 cm and an area of 735 cm2. Determine all possible values for the radius of the circle. (4 marks) Solution 2𝑟𝑟+ 𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟= 112 1 2𝑟𝑟2𝜃𝜃= 735 Solving simultaneously gives 𝑟𝑟= 21, 𝜃𝜃= 10 3 or 𝑟𝑟= 35, 𝜃𝜃= 6 5 Hence 𝑟𝑟= 21 or 𝑟𝑟= 35 cm Specific behaviours  equation for perimeter  equation for area  solution of equations  states both values of 𝑟𝑟 Solution ∠𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 3 2∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 ∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵+ 3 2∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 𝜋𝜋⇒ ∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 2𝜋𝜋 5 = 72° 𝐴𝐴= 1 2(25)2 ቀ2𝜋𝜋 5 −sin 2𝜋𝜋 5 ቁ = 95.5 cm2 Specific behaviours  equation using angles  correct angle for segment  substitutes correctly into formula  correct area",
