    "calculator": "Calculator-free",
    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 8 (8 marks) Solve the following equations for 𝑥𝑥. (a) 𝑥𝑥2 + 20𝑥𝑥−21 = 0. (2 marks) (b) (𝑥𝑥−1)2 −4 = 2𝑥𝑥−3. (3 marks) (c) 𝑥𝑥3 −2𝑥𝑥2 −11𝑥𝑥+ 12 = 0. (3 marks) © 2020 WA Exam Papers. Christ Church Grammar School has a non-exclusive licence to copy and communicate this document for non-commercial, educational use within the school. No other copying, communication or use is permitted without the express written permission of WA Exam Papers. SN018-152-5.",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions Question 8 (8 marks) Solve the following equations for 𝑥𝑥. (a) 𝑥𝑥2 + 20𝑥𝑥−21 = 0. (2 marks) (b) (𝑥𝑥−1)2 −4 = 2𝑥𝑥−3. (3 marks) (c) 𝑥𝑥3 −2𝑥𝑥2 −11𝑥𝑥+ 12 = 0. (3 marks) Solution 𝑥𝑥2 −2𝑥𝑥+ 1 −4 = 2𝑥𝑥−3 𝑥𝑥2 −4𝑥𝑥= 0 𝑥𝑥(𝑥𝑥−4) = 0 𝑥𝑥= 0, 𝑥𝑥= 4 Specific behaviours  expands and equates to zero  factorises  states both solutions Solution 𝑥𝑥3 −2𝑥𝑥2 −11𝑥𝑥+ 12|𝑥𝑥=1 = 13 −13 = 0 𝑥𝑥3 −2𝑥𝑥2 −11𝑥𝑥+ 12 = (𝑥𝑥−1)(𝑥𝑥2 −𝑥𝑥−12) = (𝑥𝑥−1)(𝑥𝑥+ 3)(𝑥𝑥−4) 𝑥𝑥= −3, 𝑥𝑥= 1, 𝑥𝑥= 4 Specific behaviours  indicates linear factor  factorises  states all solutions Solution 𝑥𝑥2 + 20𝑥𝑥−21 = (𝑥𝑥−1)(𝑥𝑥+ 21) Hence 𝑥𝑥= 1, 𝑥𝑥= −21. Specific behaviours  factorises  states both solutions",
