    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page Question 11 (8 marks) The height ℎ metres of a particle above level ground is defined as a function of time 𝑡𝑡 seconds as follows: ℎ(𝑡𝑡) = 68.75 + 15𝑡𝑡−5𝑡𝑡2, 0 ≤𝑡𝑡≤5.5 . (a) Determine the height of the particle when (i) 𝑡𝑡= 0. (1 mark) (ii) 𝑡𝑡= 4.5. (1 mark) (b) Determine the maximum height reached by the particle and the time it reached this height. (2 marks) (c) Determine the time(s) that the particle was at a height of 75 m. (2 marks) (d) State the range of the function ℎ(𝑡𝑡) for the given domain. (2 marks) Solution Range of ℎ: 0 ≤ℎ≤80 Or Accept {ℎ∈ℝ: 0 ≤ℎ≤80} Specific behaviours  upper limit  lower limit, correct inequality Note: no penalty for just writing inequality in this context. Solution From graph of ℎ(𝑡𝑡): ℎ= 75 when 𝑡𝑡= 0.5 s, 2.5 s Specific behaviours  one time  both times Solution From graph of ℎ(𝑡𝑡): Maximum height: ℎ= 80 m when 𝑡𝑡= 1.5 s. Specific behaviours  correct height  correct time Solution ℎ(0) = 68.75 m ℎ(4.5) = 35 m Specific behaviours  (i) correct  (ii) correct",
