    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 12 (6 marks) The graph 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥), where 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = 𝑥𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑏𝑏𝑏+ 𝑐𝑐 has a turning point at (−2, −1). (a) State the equation of the line of symmetry for the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥). (1 mark) (b) Determine the value of the constant 𝑏𝑏 and the value of the constant 𝑐𝑐. (3 marks) (c) The graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) is translated 3 units to the right and 5 units upwards. Determine the equation of the resulting curve. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page Question 12 (6 marks) The graph 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥), where 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = 𝑥𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑏𝑏𝑏+ 𝑐𝑐 has a turning point at (−2, −1). (a) State the equation of the line of symmetry for the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥). (1 mark) (b) Determine the value of the constant 𝑏𝑏 and the value of the constant 𝑐𝑐. (3 marks) (c) The graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) is translated 3 units to the right and 5 units upwards. Determine the equation of the resulting curve. (2 marks) Solution 𝑥𝑥= −2 Specific behaviours  correct equation Solution 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = (𝑥𝑥+ 2)2 −1 = 𝑥𝑥2 + 4𝑥𝑥+ 4 −1 𝑏𝑏= 4 𝑐𝑐= 3 Specific behaviours  writes 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) in squared form  value of 𝑏𝑏  value of 𝑐𝑐 Solution New turning point at (−2 + 3, −1 + 5) = (1, 4). Equation is 𝑦𝑦= (𝑥𝑥−1)2 + 4 = 𝑥𝑥2 −2𝑥𝑥+ 5 Specific behaviours  identifies new turning point  correct equation (either form)",
