    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page Question 18 (8 marks) (a) Determine the area of triangle 𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃 when ∠𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃= 32°, ∠𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃= 114° and 𝑃𝑃𝑃𝑃= 37 cm. (4 marks) (b) The area of triangle 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 is 75 cm2, ∠𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 30° and 3𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 4𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 as shown in the diagram. Determine the length of 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴. (4 marks) Solution 1 2 (4𝑥𝑥)(3𝑥𝑥) sin(30°) = 75 𝑥𝑥= 5 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴2 = 152 + 202 −2(15)(20) cos(30°) 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴= 10.27 cm Specific behaviours  area equation  value of 𝑥𝑥  cosine rule  length of 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 Solution 𝑞𝑞 sin32° = 37 sin 114° ⇒𝑞𝑞= 21.46 Area = 1 2 (37)(21.46) sin(34°) = 222 cm2 Specific behaviours  sketch of triangle or evidence of correct values used in rule  correct use of sine rule  length of second side  correct area",
