    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 19 (5 marks) The graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) is shown, where 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = 𝑎𝑎 𝑥𝑥+ 𝑏𝑏+ 𝑐𝑐 and 𝑎𝑎, 𝑏𝑏 and 𝑐𝑐 are constants. (a) Determine the value of 𝑎𝑎, the value of 𝑏𝑏 and the value of 𝑐𝑐. (3 marks) (b) State the domain and range of 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥). (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page Question 15 (7 marks) Let 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = √12 −2𝑥𝑥−2 and 𝑔𝑔(𝑥𝑥) = 16 + 𝑥𝑥. (a) Evaluate 𝑓𝑓(−2) −𝑔𝑔(−2). (2 marks) (b) State the domain of 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥). (2 marks) (c) State the range of 𝑔𝑔(𝑥𝑥). (1 mark) (d) Determine the coordinates of the point(s) of intersection of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) and 𝑦𝑦= 𝑔𝑔(𝑥𝑥). (2 marks) Solution Using graph/CAS: (−12, 4) Specific behaviours  𝑥𝑥-coordinate  𝑦𝑦-coordinate Solution 𝑓𝑓(−2) −𝑔𝑔(−2) = √16 −2 −(16 −2) = 2 −14 = −12 Specific behaviours  evaluates 𝑓𝑓 correctly  correct value Solution 12 −2𝑥𝑥≥0 −2𝑥𝑥≥−12 𝑥𝑥≤6 Domain: {𝑥𝑥∈ℝ: 𝑥𝑥≤6} Specific behaviours  correct inequality  correct notation Note: penalise for incorrect notation and make a note so not penalised in question 19 as well. Solution 𝑦𝑦∈ℝ Specific behaviours  correct range (symbols or words) Alternative Solution Draws sketch/graph 𝑥𝑥≤6 Domain: {𝑥𝑥∈ℝ: 𝑥𝑥≤6} Specific behaviours  correct inequality  correct notation Note: penalise for incorrect notation and make a note so not penalised in question 19 as well.",
