    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page Question 20 (8 marks) The graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑎𝑎+ 𝑏𝑏cos(𝑥𝑥+ 𝑐𝑐) is drawn below, where 𝑎𝑎, 𝑏𝑏 and 𝑐𝑐 are positive constants. (a) Determine the value of 𝑎𝑎, the value of 𝑏𝑏 and the value of 𝑐𝑐, where 𝑐𝑐< 𝜋𝜋. (3 marks) (b) On the same axes, draw the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑎𝑎+ 𝑏𝑏 2 cos(𝑥𝑥−𝑐𝑐). (3 marks) (c) Solve 𝑏𝑏cos(𝑥𝑥+ 𝑐𝑐) = 𝑏𝑏 2 cos(𝑥𝑥−𝑐𝑐) for −𝜋𝜋≤𝑥𝑥≤𝜋𝜋. (2 marks) Solution 𝑎𝑎= 1.5, 𝑏𝑏= 3, 𝑐𝑐= 𝜋𝜋 6 Specific behaviours  value of 𝑎𝑎  value of 𝑏𝑏  value of 𝑐𝑐 Solution Using intersection of graphs: 𝑥𝑥= −5𝜋𝜋 6 , 𝑥𝑥= 𝜋𝜋 6 OR 𝑥𝑥= −2.6180, 𝑥𝑥= 0.5236 Specific behaviours  a correct solution, anywhere  two solutions as given (as exact values or decimals; decimals to at least 2 decimal places) Solution (b) See graph Specific behaviours  both maxima  both minima  smooth curve",
