    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of questions DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 22 (5 marks) (a) A box of chocolates contains nine different chocolates. Determine the number of different selections that can be made when (i) two chocolates are chosen from the box. (1 mark) (ii) one, two or three chocolates are chosen from the box. (2 marks) (b) (i) Determine the value of 𝑟𝑟 if ቀ9 3ቁ= ቀ9 𝑟𝑟ቁ (1 mark) (ii) Explain how Pascal’s triangle can be used to find the solution to part (i). (1 mark) © 2020 WA Exam Papers. Christ Church Grammar School has a non-exclusive licence to copy and communicate this document for non-commercial, educational use within the school. No other copying, communication or use is permitted without the express written permission of WA Exam Papers. SN018-152-6.",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of questions Question 22 (5 marks) (a) A box of chocolates contains nine different chocolates. Determine the number of different selections that can be made when (i) two chocolates are chosen from the box. (1 mark) (ii) one, two or three chocolates are chosen from the box. (2 marks) (b) (i) Determine the value of 𝑟𝑟 if ቀ9 3ቁ= ቀ9 𝑟𝑟ቁ (1 mark) (ii) Explain how Pascal’s triangle can be used to find the solution to part (i). (1 mark) Solution ቀ9 2ቁ= 36 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution ቀ9 1ቁ+ ቀ9 2ቁ+ ቀ9 3ቁ= 9 + 36 + 84 = 129 Specific behaviours  correct selects 1, 2 and 3 chocolates  correct total value Solution ቀ9 3ቁ= ቀ9 𝑟𝑟ቁthen 𝑟𝑟= 6 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution The values in Pascal’s triangle are symmetrical so ቀ9 6ቁ is the same value as ቀ9 3ቁ, just starting from the other side of Pascal’s triangle. Specific behaviours  valid explanation",
