    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions SN044-132-1 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 8 (7 marks) (a) Evaluate sin (39𝜋 4 ). (2 marks) (b) 𝐴 is an acute angle and 𝐵 is an obtuse angle such that cos 𝐴= 1 3 and sin 𝐵= 2 3. (i) Show that sin𝐴= 2√2 3 and determine the value of cos𝐵. (3 marks) (ii) Determine the value of sin(𝐴+ 𝐵) as a single fraction. (2 marks) © 2019 WA Exam Papers. John Wollaston Anglican Community School has a non- exclusive licence to copy and communicate this document for non-commercial, educational use within the school. No other copying, communication or use is permitted without the express written permission of WA Exam Papers. SN044-132-1.",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions SN044-132-2 Question 8 (7 marks) (a) Evaluate sin (39𝜋 4 ). (2 marks) (b) 𝐴 is an acute angle and 𝐵 is an obtuse angle such that cos 𝐴= 1 3 and sin 𝐵= 2 3. (i) Show that sin𝐴= 2√2 3 and determine the value of cos𝐵. (3 marks) (ii) Determine the value of sin(𝐴+ 𝐵) as a single fraction. (2 marks) Solution sin(𝐴+ 𝐵) = 2√2 3 × (−√5 3 ) + 1 3 × 2 3 = 2 −2√10 9 Specific behaviours ✓ substitutes correctly ✓ correct value as single fraction Solution sin 39𝜋 4 = sin(39 −32)𝜋 4 = sin 7𝜋 4 sin7𝜋 4 = −sin 𝜋 4 = −1 √2 = −√2 2 Specific behaviours ✓ reduces angle ✓ exact value Solution sin2 𝐴= 1 −(1 3) 2 = 8 9 ⇒sin 𝐴= √8 3 = 2√2 3 cos2 𝐵= 1 −(2 3) 2 = 5 9 cos 𝐵= −√5 3 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates how to obtain sin2 𝐴 ✓ obtains cos2 𝐵 ✓ correct value of cos𝐵",
