    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN044-132-3 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 10 (8 marks) A positive integer less than 10 is chosen at random. The outcome sets for events 𝐵, 𝐶 and 𝐷 are 𝐵= {1, 4, 9}, 𝐶= {1, 6, 9} and 𝐷= {5, 6, 7}. (a) List the following sets: (i) 𝐶∩𝐷. (1 mark) (ii) 𝐵∪𝐶∪𝐷. (2 marks) (iii) (𝐵′ ∩𝐶′)′. (1 mark) (b) Determine (i) n(𝐶∩𝐷′). (1 mark) (ii) 𝑃(𝐵∩D). (1 mark) (iii) 𝑃(𝐵′|(𝐶∪𝐷)). (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN044-132-4 Question 10 (8 marks) A positive integer less than 10 is chosen at random. The outcome sets for events 𝐵, 𝐶 and 𝐷 are 𝐵= {1, 4, 9}, 𝐶= {1, 6, 9} and 𝐷= {5, 6, 7}. (a) List the following sets: (i) 𝐶∩𝐷. (1 mark) (ii) 𝐵∪𝐶∪𝐷. (2 marks) (iii) (𝐵′ ∩𝐶′)′. (1 mark) (b) Determine (i) n(𝐶∩𝐷′). (1 mark) (ii) 𝑃(𝐵∩D). (1 mark) (iii) 𝑃(𝐵′|(𝐶∪𝐷)). (2 marks) Solution 𝐶∩𝐷= {6} Specific behaviours ✓ correct set Solution 𝐵∪𝐶∪𝐷= {1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9} Specific behaviours ✓ correct set ✓ uses curly braces to define set Solution (𝐵′ ∩𝐶′)′ = 𝐵∪𝐶= {1, 4, 6, 9} Specific behaviours ✓ correct set Solution 𝐶∩𝐷′ = {1, 9} ⇒𝑛(𝐶∩𝐷′) = 2 Specific behaviours ✓ correct number Solution 𝐵∩D = { } ⇒𝑃(𝐵∩D) = 0 Specific behaviours ✓ correct probability Solution 𝑃= 3 5 Specific behaviours ✓ denominator ✓ numerator",
