    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN044-132-3 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 11 (8 marks) In an experiment, the sound intensity, 𝑆, can be modelled by 𝑆(𝑥) = 3.6 −2.4𝑥+ 1.5𝑥2 −0.2𝑥3, where 𝑥 is the distance from the sound source in metres and 0 ≤𝑥≤6. (a) Determine 𝑆 when 𝑥= 3. (1 mark) (b) Draw the graph of 𝑦= 𝑆(𝑥) on the axes below. (4 marks) (c) Determine the equation of the straight line 𝐿 that passes through the 𝑥-intercept and the 𝑦- intercept of the graph of 𝑦= 𝑆(𝑥). (2 marks) (d) Determine the coordinates of the point of intersection of 𝐿 with the graph of 𝑦= 𝑆(𝑥) where 𝑥> 0 and 𝑦> 0. (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN044-132-4 Question 11 (8 marks) In an experiment, the sound intensity, 𝑆, can be modelled by 𝑆(𝑥) = 3.6 −2.4𝑥+ 1.5𝑥2 −0.2𝑥3, where 𝑥 is the distance from the sound source in metres and 0 ≤𝑥≤6. (a) Determine 𝑆 when 𝑥= 3. (1 mark) (b) Draw the graph of 𝑦= 𝑆(𝑥) on the axes below. (4 marks) (c) Determine the equation of the straight line 𝐿 that passes through the 𝑥-intercept and the 𝑦- intercept of the graph of 𝑦= 𝑆(𝑥). (2 marks) (d) Determine the coordinates of the point of intersection of 𝐿 with the graph of 𝑦= 𝑆(𝑥) where 𝑥> 0 and 𝑦> 0. (1 mark) Solution 𝑆(3) = 4.5 Specific behaviours ✓ correct value Solution (1.5, 2.7) Specific behaviours ✓ correct coordinates Solution (0, 3.6) & (6, 0) ⇒𝑚= −3.6 ÷ 6 = −0.6 𝑦= −0.6𝑥+ 3.6 Specific behaviours ✓ gradient ✓ 𝑦-intercept and equation Solution See graph Specific behaviours ✓ intercepts ✓ accurate maximum ✓ accurate minimum ✓ smooth curve",
