    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN044-132-3 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 16 (8 marks) A small weight, attached to the bottom of a spring, oscillated up and down. The distance, 𝑑 cm, of the weight from the top of the spring after 𝑡 seconds can be modelled by 𝑑= 45 + 35 sin (3𝜋𝑡 4 ) (a) Sketch the graph on the axes below for 0 ≤𝑡≤3. (4 marks) (b) Mark on your graph point 𝑀, where the weight is 40 cm from the top of the spring and moving downwards. (1 mark) (c) Determine (i) the maximum distance of the weight from the top of the spring. (1 mark) (ii) the time taken for the weight to first return to its initial position. (1 mark) (iii) the distance moved by the weight between 𝑡= 1 and 𝑡= 2. (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN044-132-4 Question 16 (8 marks) A small weight, attached to the bottom of a spring, oscillated up and down. The distance, 𝑑 cm, of the weight from the top of the spring after 𝑡 seconds can be modelled by 𝑑= 45 + 35 sin (3𝜋𝑡 4 ) (a) Sketch the graph on the axes below for 0 ≤𝑡≤3. (4 marks) (b) Mark on your graph point 𝑀, where the weight is 40 cm from the top of the spring and moving downwards. (1 mark) (c) Determine (i) the maximum distance of the weight from the top of the spring. (1 mark) (ii) the time taken for the weight to first return to its initial position. (1 mark) (iii) the distance moved by the weight between 𝑡= 1 and 𝑡= 2. (1 mark) Solution 80 cm Specific behaviours ✓ correct distance Solution 𝑑(1) −𝑑(2) = 69.75 −10 = 59.75 cm Specific behaviours ✓ correct distance Solution 𝑡= 4 3 = 1. 3̅ s Specific behaviours ✓ correct time Solutions (a), (b) See graph Specific behaviours ✓ 𝑦-intercept and (3, 70) ✓ max and min ✓ inflection pt ~(1.3, 45) ✓ single smooth curve ✓ accurately locates 𝑀",
