    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN044-132-3 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 17 (7 marks) An examination consisted of two papers, one of which was much harder than the other. 15% of candidates gained a distinction in the first paper (event 𝐴) and 5% gained a distinction in the second paper (event 𝐵) whilst 82% did not gain a distinction in either paper. (a) Determine the probability that a randomly chosen candidate (i) gained a distinction in both papers. (2 marks) (ii) gained a distinction in one paper but not the other. (2 marks) (iii) gained a distinction in the first paper given that they gained a distinction in the second. (1 mark) (b) State, with justification, whether events 𝐴 and 𝐵 are independent. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN044-132-4 Question 17 (7 marks) An examination consisted of two papers, one of which was much harder than the other. 15% of candidates gained a distinction in the first paper (event 𝐴) and 5% gained a distinction in the second paper (event 𝐵) whilst 82% did not gain a distinction in either paper. (a) Determine the probability that a randomly chosen candidate (i) gained a distinction in both papers. (2 marks) (ii) gained a distinction in one paper but not the other. (2 marks) (iii) gained a distinction in the first paper given that they gained a distinction in the second. (1 mark) (b) State, with justification, whether events 𝐴 and 𝐵 are independent. (2 marks) Solution Events are NOT independent since 𝑃(𝐴) = 0.15 and 𝑃(𝐴|𝐵) = 0.4 and so it can be seen that 𝑃(𝐴) ≠𝑃(𝐴|𝐵). Specific behaviours ✓ states not independent ✓ justification Solution 𝑃(𝐴∪𝐵) = 1 −0.82 = 0.18 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) = 0.15 + 0.05 −0.18 = 0.02 Specific behaviours ✓ calculates 𝑃(𝐴∪𝐵) ✓ correct probability Solution 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵̅) + 𝑃(𝐴̅ ∩𝐵) = (0.15 −0.02) + (0.05 −0.02) = 0.16 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates correct method ✓ correct probability Solution 𝑃(𝐴|𝐵) = 0.02 0.05 = 0.4 Specific ",
