    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN044-132-3 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 20 (8 marks) A shelf held a collection of 18 different books, of which 7 were cookbooks, 3 were dictionaries and the rest were travel guides. A random selection of 5 books is to be made from the shelf. (a) Determine the number of ways (i) this can be done. (2 marks) (ii) a selection can be made that will not contain any dictionaries. (2 marks) (b) Determine the probability that (i) the selection will only contain cookbooks. (2 marks) (ii) the selection will contain exactly one cookbook given that it does not contain any dictionaries. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN044-132-4 Question 20 (8 marks) A shelf held a collection of 18 different books, of which 7 were cookbooks, 3 were dictionaries and the rest were travel guides. A random selection of 5 books is to be made from the shelf. (a) Determine the number of ways (i) this can be done. (2 marks) (ii) a selection can be made that will not contain any dictionaries. (2 marks) (b) Determine the probability that (i) the selection will only contain cookbooks. (2 marks) (ii) the selection will contain exactly one cookbook given that it does not contain any dictionaries. (2 marks) Solution (7 5) × (3 0) × (8 0) = 21 𝑃= 21 8568 = 1 408 ≈0.00245 Specific behaviours ✓ correct number for selection ✓ correct probability (no need to simplify) Solution (7 1) × (8 4) × (3 0) = 490 𝑃= 490 3003 = 70 429 ≈0.16317 Specific behaviours ✓ correct number for selection ✓ correct probability (no need to simplify) Solution (15 5 ) × (3 0) = 3 003 Specific behaviours ✓ correct number to choose from ✓ correct number Solution (18 5 ) = 8 568 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates use of combinations ✓ correct number",
