    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 METHODS UNIT 1 End of questions SN044-132-3 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 21 (8 marks) (a) The circle shown has centre 𝑂 and diameter 𝐴𝐶 of length 50 cm. Determine the shaded area given that 2 × ∠𝐴𝑂𝐵= 3 × ∠𝐵𝑂𝐶. (4 marks) (b) A sector of a circle has a perimeter of 112 cm and an area of 735 cm2. Determine the radius of the circle. (4 marks) © 2019 WA Exam Papers. John Wollaston Anglican Community School has a non- exclusive licence to copy and communicate this document for non-commercial, educational use within the school. No other copying, communication or use is permitted without the express written permission of WA Exam Papers. SN044-132-3.",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 METHODS UNIT 1 End of questions SN044-132-4 Question 21 (8 marks) (a) The circle shown has centre 𝑂 and diameter 𝐴𝐶 of length 50 cm. Determine the shaded area given that 2 × ∠𝐴𝑂𝐵= 3 × ∠𝐵𝑂𝐶. (4 marks) (b) A sector of a circle has a perimeter of 112 cm and an area of 735 cm2. Determine the radius of the circle. (4 marks) Solution 2𝑟+ 𝑟𝜃= 112 1 2𝑟2𝜃= 735 Solving simultaneously gives 𝑟= 21, 𝜃= 10 3 or 𝑟= 35, 𝜃= 6 5 Hence 𝑟= 21 or 𝑟= 35 cm Specific behaviours ✓ equation for perimeter ✓ equation for area ✓ solution of equations ✓ states both values of 𝑟 Solution ∠𝐴𝑂𝐵= 3 2∠𝐵𝑂𝐶 ∠𝐵𝑂𝐶+ 3 2∠𝐵𝑂𝐶= 𝜋⇒ ∠𝐵𝑂𝐶= 2𝜋 5 = 72° 𝐴= 1 2(25)2 (2𝜋 5 −sin 2𝜋 5 ) = 95.5 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ equation using angles ✓ correct angle for segment ✓ substitutes correctly into formula ✓ correct area",
