    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN044-152-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 10 (8 marks) The height ℎ metres of a particle above level ground is defined as a function of time 𝑡 seconds as follows: ℎ(𝑡) = 68.75 + 15𝑡−5𝑡2, 0 ≤𝑡≤5.5 . (a) Determine the height of the particle when (i) 𝑡= 0. (1 mark) (ii) 𝑡= 4.5. (1 mark) (b) Determine the maximum height reached by the particle and the time it reached this height. (2 marks) (c) Determine the time(s) that the particle was at a height of 75 m. (2 marks) (d) State the range of the function ℎ(𝑡) for the given domain. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN044-152-4 Question 10 (8 marks) The height ℎ metres of a particle above level ground is defined as a function of time 𝑡 seconds as follows: ℎ(𝑡) = 68.75 + 15𝑡−5𝑡2, 0 ≤𝑡≤5.5 . (a) Determine the height of the particle when (i) 𝑡= 0. (1 mark) (ii) 𝑡= 4.5. (1 mark) (b) Determine the maximum height reached by the particle and the time it reached this height. (2 marks) (c) Determine the time(s) that the particle was at a height of 75 m. (2 marks) (d) State the range of the function ℎ(𝑡) for the given domain. (2 marks) Solution Range of ℎ: 0 ≤ℎ≤80 Specific behaviours ✓ upper limit ✓ lower limit, correct inequality Solution From graph of ℎ(𝑡): ℎ= 75 when 𝑡= 0.5 s, 2.5 s Specific behaviours ✓ one time ✓ both times Solution From graph of ℎ(𝑡): Maximum height: ℎ= 80 m when 𝑡= 1.5 s. Specific behaviours ✓ correct height ✓ correct time Solution ℎ(0) = 68.75 m ℎ(4.5) = 35 m Specific behaviours ✓ (i) correct ✓ (ii) correct",
