    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN044-152-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 11 (6 marks) Two events are such that 𝑃(𝑋) = 0.2, 𝑃(𝑌) = 0.5 and 𝑃(𝑌|𝑋) = 0.1. Determine the probability that (a) both events occur. (2 marks) (b) at least one event occurs. (2 marks) (c) neither event occurs. (1 mark) (d) 𝑋 occurs given that 𝑌 has occurred. (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN044-152-4 Question 11 (6 marks) Two events are such that 𝑃(𝑋) = 0.2, 𝑃(𝑌) = 0.5 and 𝑃(𝑌|𝑋) = 0.1. Determine the probability that (a) both events occur. (2 marks) (b) at least one event occurs. (2 marks) (c) neither event occurs. (1 mark) (d) 𝑋 occurs given that 𝑌 has occurred. (1 mark) Solution 𝑃(𝑋|𝑌) = 𝑃(𝑋∩𝑌) 𝑃(𝑌) = 0.02 0.5 = 0.04 Specific behaviours ✓ correct probability Solution 𝑃(𝑋̅ ∩𝑌̅) = 1 −𝑃(𝑋∪𝑌) = 1 −0.68 = 0.32 Specific behaviours ✓ correct probability Solution 𝑃(𝑋∪𝑌) = 𝑃(𝑋) + 𝑃(𝑌) −𝑃(𝑋∩𝑌) = 0.2 + 0.5 −0.02 = 0.68 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates use of rule ✓ correct probability Solution 𝑃(𝑌|𝑋) = 𝑃(𝑋∩𝑌) 𝑃(𝑋) ⇒𝑃(𝑋∩𝑌) = 0.2 × 0.1 = 0.02 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates use of conditional formula ✓ correct probability",
