    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN044-152-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 12 (8 marks) The height above ground level, ℎ m, of a seat on a steadily rotating Ferris wheel 𝑡 minutes after the wheel begins to move is given by ℎ= 21.5 −18.5 cos (𝜋𝑡 6 + 𝜋 3). (a) Determine the initial height of the seat. (1 mark) (b) Graph the height of the seat against time on the axes below. (4 marks) (c) Determine (i) the maximum height above ground reached by the seat. (1 mark) (ii) the time taken, to the nearest second, for the seat to first reach a height of 4 m above ground level. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN044-152-4 Question 12 (8 marks) The height above ground level, ℎ m, of a seat on a steadily rotating Ferris wheel 𝑡 minutes after the wheel begins to move is given by ℎ= 21.5 −18.5 cos (𝜋𝑡 6 + 𝜋 3). (a) Determine the initial height of the seat. (1 mark) (b) Graph the height of the seat against time on the axes below. (4 marks) (c) Determine (i) the maximum height above ground reached by the seat. (1 mark) (ii) the time taken, to the nearest second, for the seat to first reach a height of 4 m above ground level. (2 marks) 6 12 18 24 10 20 30 40 50 Solution ℎ(0) = 12.25 m Specific behaviours ✓ correct height Solution ℎ= 4 ⇒𝑡= 9.37 0.37 × 60 = 22 𝑡= 9 m 22 s (562 s) Specific behaviours ✓ time as decimal ✓ time to nearest second Solution ℎ𝑀𝐴𝑋= 40 m Specific behaviours ✓ correct height Solution See graph Specific behaviours ✓ (0, 12) and (24, 12) ✓ correct maximums ✓ correct minimums ✓ smooth curve",
