    "questionText": "CALCULATOR ASSUMED 11 MATHEMATICS METHODS UNIT 1 Question 15 {1.1.13} (5 marks) An online company that sells onesies has modelled their expected number of daily sales (S) against the average daily temperature (T) in ℃. Their model has S as inversely proportional to √2𝑇+ 16 for −5 ≤𝑇≤30. On a 10℃ day in August they sold 20 onesies. a) Determine the relationship between S and T. (3 marks) b) Determine the number of expected sales tomorrow if the average forecasted temperature is 29. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR ASSUMED 11 MATHEMATICS METHODS UNIT 1 Question 15 {1.1.13} (5 marks) An online company that sells onesies has modelled their expected number of daily sales (S) against the average daily temperature (T) in ℃. Their model has S as inversely proportional to √2𝑇+ 16 for −5 ≤𝑇≤30. On a 10℃ day in August they sold 20 onesies. a) Determine the relationship between S and T. (3 marks) Solution 𝑆∝ 1 √2𝑇+ 16 ⇒𝑆= 𝑘 √2𝑇+ 16 20 = 𝑘 √2 × 10 + 16 ⇒𝑘= 120 𝑆= 120 √2𝑇+ 16 Specific behaviours ✓ constructs equation for S ✓ determines k ✓ determines relationship between S and T b) Determine the number of expected sales tomorrow if the average forecasted temperature is 29. (2 marks) Solution 𝑆= 120 √2 × 29 + 16 = 13.9 (1 𝑑. 𝑝) Hence, the number of expected sales is 14 Specific behaviours ✓ substitutes 𝑇= 29 ✓ states the number of expected sales as an integer",
