    "questionText": "CALCULATOR ASSUMED 12 MATHEMATICS METHODS UNIT 1 Question 16 {1.1.14} (10 marks) a) State all the asymptotes on each graph below then determine each equation of the rectangular hyperbola: i) (3 marks) ii) (3 marks) b) Complete the table below. (4 marks) Curve x-intercept y-intercept Asymptote parallel to the x-axis y-axis 𝑦= 6 𝑥−2 −3 𝑦= −9 𝑥+ 3",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR ASSUMED 12 MATHEMATICS METHODS UNIT 1 Question 16 {1.1.14} (10 marks) a) State all the asymptotes on each graph below then determine each equation of the rectangular hyperbola: i) (3 marks) ii) (3 marks) b) Complete the table below. c) (4 marks) Solution Curve x-intercept y-intercept Asymptote parallel to the x-axis y-axis 𝑦= 6 𝑥−2 −3 (4, 0) (0, −6) 𝑦= −3 𝑥= 2 𝑦= −9 𝑥+ 3 None (0, −3) 𝑦= 0 𝑥= −3 Specific behaviours ✓ correct x-intercepts ✓ correct y-intercepts ✓ correct horizontal asymptotes ✓ correct vertical asymptotes Solution 𝑦= 𝑘 𝑥−3 + 2 𝑘 0 −3 + 2 = 4 ⇒𝑘= −6 𝑦= −6 𝑥−3 + 2 Specific behaviours ✓ states asymptotes 𝑥= 3 & 𝑦= 2 ✓ substitutes point and solves ✓ states equation Solution 𝑦= 𝑘 𝑥+ 1 𝑘 0 + 1 = 3 ⇒𝑘= 3 𝑦= 3 𝑥+ 1 Specific behaviours ✓ states asymptotes 𝑥= −1 & 𝑦= 0 ✓ substitutes point and solves ✓ states equation",
