    "questionText": "3 Section Two: Calculator-assumed 67% (94 Marks) This section has twelve questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 8 (2,4 = 6 marks) Four points have coordinates 𝐴(−11, 7), 𝐵(4, −3), 𝐶(7, 9) and 𝐷(𝑠, 𝑡). (a) If 𝐵 is the midpoint of 𝐴 and 𝐷, determine the coordinates of point 𝐷. (2 marks) (b) Determine the equation of the line that is perpendicular to 𝐴𝐵 and that passes through 𝐶 in the form 𝑎𝑥+ 𝑏𝑦+ 𝑐= 0, where 𝑎, 𝑏 and 𝑐 are integers and 𝑎> 0. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 3 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page Section Two: Calculator-assumed 67% (94 Marks) This section has twelve questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 8 (6 marks) Four points have coordinates 𝐴(−11, 7), 𝐵(4, −3), 𝐶(7, 9) and 𝐷(𝑠, 𝑡). (a) If 𝐵 is the midpoint of 𝐴 and 𝐷, determine the value of the constant 𝑠 and the value of the constant 𝑡. (2 marks) (b) Determine the equation of the line that is perpendicular to 𝐴𝐵 and that passes through 𝐶 in the form 𝑎𝑥+ 𝑏𝑦+ 𝑐= 0, where 𝑎, 𝑏 and 𝑐 are integers and 𝑎> 0. (4 marks) Solution 𝑚𝐴𝐵= −3 −7 4 −(−11) = −2 3 , 𝑚𝑃𝐸𝑅𝑃= −1 ÷ −2 3 = 3 2 𝑦−9 = 3 2 (𝑥−7) 2𝑦−18 = 3𝑥−21 3𝑥−2𝑦−3 = 0 Specific behaviours ✓ slope of 𝐴𝐵 ✓ slope of perpendicular line ✓ correct equation of line, any form ✓ correct equation of line in required form Solution −11 + 𝑠 2 = 4 →𝑠= 19 7 + 𝑡 2 = −3 →𝑡= −13 Specific behaviours ✓ value of 𝑠 ✓ value of 𝑡",
