    "questionText": "13 Question 18 (4,4, = 8 marks) (a) The graph of the quadratic function 2 ( ) ( ) f x a x b c = + + has roots at 𝑥= −1 and 𝑥= 9 and the range of 𝑓(𝑥) is 𝑦≥−50. Use an algebraic method to determine 𝑓(0). (4 marks) (b) The area of square 𝐵 is 303.5 cm2 greater than twice the area of square 𝐴, (i.e 2 2 2 303.5 B A = + cm2 ) and the difference in the perimeters of the two squares is 50 cm, Determine the least possible area of square 𝐴, the smaller of the squares and show all steps of your working. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "Question 18 (8 marks) (a) The graph of the quadratic function 2 ( ) ( ) f x a x b c = + + has roots at 𝑥= −1 and 𝑥= 9 and the range of 𝑓(𝑥) is 𝑦≥−50. Use an algebraic method to determine 𝑓(0). (4 marks) (b) The area of square 𝐵 is 303.5 cm2 greater than twice the area of square 𝐴, (i.e 2 2 2 303.5 B A = + cm2 ) and the difference in the perimeters of the two squares is 50cm, Determine the least possible area of square 𝐴, the smaller of the squares and show all steps of your working. Solution 4𝐵= 4𝐴+ 50 𝐵= 𝐴+ 12.5 Hence (𝐴+ 12.5)2 = 2𝐴2 + 303.5 𝐴= 19 2 = 9.5, 𝐴= 31 2 = 15.5 Least area when 𝐴= 9.5: 𝐴𝐴= 9.52 = 361 4 = 90.25 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ equation for difference in perimeter or states difference in sides ✓ forms quadratic equation ✓ solves quadratic equation (accept if only 9.5 given, but warn) or solves equations simultaneously ✓ states least area (do not award if TP used) Solution Axis of symmetry is midway between roots (−1 + 9) ÷ 2 = 4 and so turning point at (4, −50). 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑎(𝑥−4)2 −50 Using a root, 𝑓(9) = 0 = 𝑎(9 −4)2 −50 →𝑎= 2. Hence 𝑓(0) = 2(0 −4)2 −50 = −18. Specific behaviours ✓ uses range and symmetry to identify turning point or for 𝑎(𝑥+ 1)(𝑥−9), 𝑎(𝑥−ℎ)2 −50 or",
