    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-112-2 Question 12 (8 marks) (a) Determine the equation of the axis of symmetry for the graph of 𝑦= 4𝑥2 −20𝑥−51. (2 marks) (b) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 27 passes through the points (3, 6) and (−4, −57). Determine the values of the constants 𝑎 and 𝑏. (3 marks) (c) Determine the value(s) of 𝑚 for which the graph of 𝑦= 𝑥2 −4𝑥+ 𝑚 has no real roots. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-112-4 Question 12 (8 marks) (a) Determine the equation of the axis of symmetry for the graph of 𝑦= 4𝑥2 −20𝑥−51. (2 marks) (b) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 27 passes through the points (3, 6) and (−4, −57). Determine the values of the constants 𝑎 and 𝑏. (3 marks) (c) Determine the value(s) of 𝑚 for which the graph of 𝑦= 𝑥2 −4𝑥+ 𝑚 Has no real roots. (3 marks) Solution ∆= 16 −4 × 1 × 𝑚 ∆< 0 𝑤ℎ𝑒𝑛 𝑚> 4 Specific behaviours  indicates use of ∆ correct substitution  𝑚> 4 Solution 6 = (3)2𝑎+ 3𝑏+ 27 6 = 9𝑎+ 3𝑏+ 27 −57 = (−4)2𝑎−4𝑏+ 27 −57 = 16𝑎−4𝑏+ 27 Solve simultaneously using CAS 𝑎= −4, 𝑏= 5 Specific behaviours  substitutes in both points  solves for 𝑎  solves for 𝑏 Solution 𝑥= −𝑏 2𝑎= −−20 2 × 4 = 2.5 𝑥= 2.5 Specific behaviours  indicates use of formula  correct equation",
