    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-112-2 Question 16 (8 marks) Let 𝑓(𝑥) = 4 3 −𝑥 and 𝑔(𝑥) = 1 𝑥+ 𝑝+ 𝑞, where 𝑝 and 𝑞 are constants. The graph of 𝑦= 𝑔(𝑥) is shown below. (a) Sketch the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) on the axes above. Clearly label the asymptotes and y-intercept(s). (3 marks) (b) Determine the values of 𝑝 and 𝑞. (2 marks) (c) Solve the equation 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑔(𝑥), giving your solution(s) to one decimal place. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-112-4 Question 16 (8 marks) Let 𝑓(𝑥) = 4 3 −𝑥 and 𝑔(𝑥) = 1 𝑥+ 𝑝+ 𝑞, where 𝑝 and 𝑞 are constants. The graph of 𝑦= 𝑔(𝑥) is shown below. (a) Sketch the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) on the axes above. (3 marks) (b) Determine the values of 𝑝 and 𝑞. (2 marks) (c) Solve the equation 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑔(𝑥), giving your solution(s) to one decimal place. (3 marks) Solution See graph Specific behaviours  asymptotes  y-intercept  accuracy [i.e. at least 3 of (-1,1), (1,2), (2,4), (4,-4) or (7,-1)] Solution 𝑝= 2, 𝑞= −3 Specific behaviours  value of 𝑝  value of 𝑞 Solution 4 3 −𝑥= 1 𝑥+ 2 −3 𝑥= −1.7, 𝑥= 4.4 Specific behaviours constructs equality  one solution  second solution (Rounding for guidance only but penalise answers given as coordinates -1 mark)",
