    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-112-2 Question 20 (6 marks) (a) Part of the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) is shown below, where 𝑓(𝑥) = −2(𝑥−𝑏)3 + 𝑐, and 𝑏 and 𝑐 are constants. (i) State the degree of 𝑓(𝑥). (1 mark) (ii) Determine the value of 𝑏. (1 mark) (iii) Determine 𝑓(0). (2 marks) (b) Another function is given by 𝑔(𝑥) = −𝑓(𝑥+ 8). Describe the transformation that maps the graph 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) onto 𝑦= 𝑔(𝑥). (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-112-4 Question 20 (6 marks) (a) Part of the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) is shown below, where 𝑓(𝑥) = −2(𝑥−𝑏)3 + 𝑐, and 𝑏 and 𝑐 are constants. (i) State the degree of 𝑓(𝑥). (1 mark) (ii) Determine the value of 𝑏. (1 mark) (iii) Determine 𝑓(0). (2 marks) (b) Another function is given by 𝑔(𝑥) = −𝑓(𝑥+ 8). Describe how to obtain the graph of 𝑦= 𝑔(𝑥) from the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥). (2 marks) Solution 𝑏= 4 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution Translate graph 8 units to the left. Reflection about the x-axis Specific behaviours  correct translation  correct reflection Solution 𝑓(𝑥) = −2(𝑥−4)3 + 2 𝑓(0) = −2(−4)3 + 2 = 130 Specific behaviours  indicates value of 𝑐  evaluates Solution 3 Specific behaviours  correct degree",
