    "answerText": "Question 11 (9 marks) A positive integer less than 12 is chosen at random. The outcome sets for events 𝐴, 𝐵 and 𝐶 are 𝐴= {3, 4, 5, 6}, 𝐵= {1, 3, 5, 7} and 𝐶= {2, 6, 10}. (a) List the following sets: (i) 𝐴∩𝐵. (1 mark) (ii) 𝐴∪𝐵∪𝐶. (2 marks) (iii) 𝐴∩(𝐵∪𝐶). (2 mark) (b) Determine (i) n(𝐵∩𝐶′). (1 mark) (ii) 𝑃(𝐵∩C). (1 mark) (iii) 𝑃(𝐴′|(𝐵∪𝐶)). (2 marks) Solution 𝐴∩𝐵= {3, 5} Specific behaviours ✓ correct set Solution 𝐴∪𝐵∪𝐶= {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 10} Specific behaviours ✓ correct set ✓ uses curly braces to define set Solution 𝐵∪𝐶= {1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7, 10} 𝐴∩(𝐵∪𝐶)= {3, 5, 6}, Specific behaviours ✓ correct 𝐵∪𝐶 ✓ correct answer Solution 4 Specific behaviours ✓ correct number Solution 𝐵∩C = { } ⇒𝑃(𝐵∩C) = 0 Specific behaviours ✓ correct probability Solution 𝑃= 4 7 Specific behaviours ✓ denominator ✓ numerator",
