    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNIT 1 SN085-132-2 Question 17 (8 marks) (a) The variables 𝑃 and 𝑤 are directly proportional and when 𝑤= 30, 𝑃= 6. (i) Determine an equation for the relationship between 𝑃 and 𝑤. (2 marks) (ii) State the value of 𝑃 when 𝑤= 10. (1 mark) (b) The time, 𝑡 minutes, that a car takes to travel 500 m at a constant speed of 𝑠 kmh-1 is given by the formula 𝑡= 𝑘 𝑠 . (i) Determine the value of the constant 𝑘, given that when 𝑠= 30, 𝑡= 60. (1 mark) (ii) Determine the value of 𝑡 when 𝑠= 20. (1 mark) (iii) On the axes below, draw a graph to show how 𝑠 varies with 𝑡. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "Question 17 (8 marks) (a) The variables 𝑃 and 𝑤 are directly proportional and when 𝑤= 30, 𝑃= 6. (i) Determine an equation for the relationship between 𝑃 and 𝑤. (2 marks) (ii) State the value of 𝑃 when 𝑤= 10. (1 mark) (b) The time, 𝑡 minutes, that a car takes to travel 500 m at a constant speed of 𝑠 kmh-1 is given by the formula 𝑡= 𝑘 𝑠 . (i) Determine the value of the constant 𝑘, given that when 𝑠= 30, 𝑡= 60. (1 mark) (ii) Determine the value of 𝑡 when 𝑠= 20. (1 mark) (iii) On the axes below, draw a graph to show how 𝑠 varies with 𝑡. (3 marks) Question 17 (8 marks) Solution 𝑃= 𝑚𝑤, 𝑚= 6 30 = 0.2 ⇒𝑃= 0.2𝑤 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates use of line through origin ✓ correct relationship Solution 𝑃= 0.2(10) = 2 Specific behaviours ✓ correct value Solution 𝑡= 1800 ÷ 20 = 90 Specific behaviours ✓ correct value Solution 60 = 𝑘 30 ⇒𝑘= 1800 Specific behaviours ✓ correct value Solution See graph. Key points: (10, 180), (20, 90), (30, 60), (60, 30), (90, 20) Specific behaviours ✓ plots at least 2 key points ✓ plots all key points ✓ smooth curve",
