    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNIT 1 SN085-132-2 Question 19 (8 marks) (a) The equation of the axis of symmetry for the graph of 𝑦= 2𝑥2 + 8𝑥+ 5 is 𝑥= 𝑚. Determine the value of 𝑚, using a method that does not refer to the graph of the parabola. (2 marks) (b) A parabola with equation 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 𝑐 has a turning point at (4, −5) and passes through the point (2, −17). Determine the value of 𝑎, the value of 𝑏 and the value of 𝑐. (3 marks) (c) Determine the value of the discriminant for the quadratic equation 4𝑥2 −28𝑥+ 47 = 0 and use it to explain how many solutions the equation (𝑥+ 3)(4𝑥2 −28𝑥+ 47) = 0 will have. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "Question 19 (8 marks) (a) The equation of the axis of symmetry for the graph of 𝑦= 2𝑥2 + 8𝑥+ 5 is 𝑥= 𝑚. Determine the value of 𝑚, using a method that does not refer to the graph of the parabola. (2 marks) (b) A parabola with equation 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 𝑐 has a turning point at (4, −5) and passes through the point (2, −17). Determine the value of 𝑎, the value of 𝑏 and the value of 𝑐. (3 marks) (c) Determine the value of the discriminant for the quadratic equation 4𝑥2 −28𝑥+ 47 = 0 and use it to explain how many solutions the equation (𝑥+ 3)(4𝑥2 −28𝑥+ 47) = 0 will have. (3 marks) Solution 𝑥= − 8 2 × 2 = −2 𝑚= −2 𝑦= 2(𝑥+ 2)2 + 𝑐 ∴𝑚= −2 Specific behaviours ✓ uses 𝑥= −𝑏÷ (2𝑎) or partially completes the square ✓ value of 𝑚 Solution 𝑑= (−28)2 −4(4)(47) = 32 When 𝑑> 0, quadratic will have two solutions. Hence equation will have three solutions - one from the linear factor and two from the quadratic factor. Specific behaviours ✓ value of discriminant ✓ uses discriminant to say quadratic will have two solutions ✓ explains why equation has three solutions Solution 𝑦= 𝑎(𝑥−4)2 −5 −17 = 𝑎(2 −4)2 −5 ⇒𝑎= −3 𝑦= −3(𝑥−4)2 −5 = −3𝑥2 + 24𝑥−53 𝑎= −3, 𝑏= 24, 𝑐= −53 Specific behaviours ✓ correctly writes in turn",
