    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED SN085-132-2 Question 20 (8 marks) (a) The circle shown has centre 𝑂 and diameter 𝐴𝐶 of length 80 cm. Determine the shaded area given that 3 × ∠𝐴𝑂𝐵= 5 × ∠𝐵𝑂𝐶. (4 marks) (b) A sector of a circle has a perimeter of 84 cm and an area of 360 cm2. Determine the radius of the circle. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "Question 20 (8 marks) (a) The circle shown has centre 𝑂 and diameter 𝐴𝐶 of length 80 cm. Determine the shaded area given that 3 × ∠𝐴𝑂𝐵= 5 × ∠𝐵𝑂𝐶. (4 marks) (b) A sector of a circle has a perimeter of 84 cm and an area of 360 cm2. Determine the radius of the circle. (4 marks) Solution ∠𝐵𝑂𝐶= 3 5∠𝐴𝑂𝐵 ∠𝐴𝑂𝐵+ 3 5∠𝐴𝑂𝐵= 𝜋⇒ ∠𝐴𝑂𝐵= 5𝜋 8 = 112.5° 𝐴= 1 2(40)2 (5𝜋 8 −sin 5𝜋 8 ) = 832 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ equation using angles ✓ correct angle for segment ✓ substitutes correctly into formula ✓ correct area Solution 2𝑟+ 𝑟𝜃= 84 1 2𝑟2𝜃= 360 Solving simultaneously gives 𝑟= 12, 𝜃= 5 or 𝑟= 30, 𝜃= 4 5 Hence 𝑟= 12 or 𝑟= 30 cm Specific behaviours ✓ equation for perimeter ✓ equation for area ✓ solution of equations ✓ states both values of 𝑟",
