    "questionText": "See next page Question 19 (7 marks) (a) Three aircraft, marked, Z, U and W, are flying in a triangular formation at an air show, at the same speed and altitude. Aircraft Z is 8.25 m from aircraft U which is 6.5 m from aircraft W. The angle WZU formed is 48°. Determine what distance aircraft W is from aircraft Z? (3 marks) (b) Determine the area of triangle 𝑃𝑄𝑅 when ∠𝑃𝑄𝑅= 32°, ∠𝑃𝑅𝑄= 114° and 𝑃𝑄= 37 cm. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "See next page Question 19 (7 marks) (a) Three aircraft, marked, Z, U and W, are flying in a triangular formation at an air show, at the same speed and altitude. Aircraft Z is 8.25 m from aircraft U which is 6.5 m from aircraft W. The angle WZU formed is 48°. Determine what distance aircraft W is from aircraft Z? (3 marks) Solution Soln 1 x = 7.68 m x = 3.36 m Aircraft W could be 7.68 m or 3.36 m from aircraft Z Or Soln 2 Solve 2 2 2 6.5 8.25 2. .(8.25)cos48 x x     3.36 x m  or 7.68m Specific behaviours   sine rule and both solns   cos rule and first x value   second x value or second soln   cos rule   first x value   second x value Only one correct solution 2/3",
