    "questionText": "See next page Question 20 (8 marks) A polynomial of degree 3 passes through the points with coordinates (0, 9), (−1, 0), (3, 0) and (1.5, 0). (a) Determine the equation of the polynomial. State in expanded form (3 marks) (b) Draw the graph of the polynomial on the axes below, indicating and labelling key features (4 marks) (c) Determine the coordinates of the point where concavity changes. (1 mark) Give your answer to an accuracy of 4 decimal places.",
    "answerText": "See next page Question 20 (8 marks) A polynomial of degree 3 passes through the points with coordinates (0, 9), (−1, 0), (3, 0) and (1.5, 0). (a) Determine the equation of the polynomial. State in expanded form. (3 marks) Solution Using roots: 𝑦= 𝑎(𝑥+ 1)(𝑥−3)(𝑥−1.5) Use 4th point: 𝑥= 0 ⇒9 = 𝑎(1)(−3)(−1.5) 𝑎= 2 Expand: 𝑦= 2(𝑥+ 1)(𝑥−3)(𝑥−1.5) = 2𝑥3 −7𝑥2 + 9 Specific behaviours   factored form using roots   substitutes fourth point and determines correct value of 𝑎   correct expanded form (b) Draw the graph of the polynomial on the axes below, indicating and labelling key features (4 marks) (c) Determine the coordinates of the point where concavity changes. (1 mark) Give your answer to an accuracy of 4 decimal places. Alt Solution Using roots: 𝑦= 𝑏(𝑥+ 1)(𝑥−3)(2𝑥−3) Use 4th point: 𝑥= 0 ⇒9 = 𝑏(1)(−3)(−3) 𝑏= 1 Expand: 𝑦= (𝑥+ 1)(𝑥−3)(2𝑥−3) = 2𝑥3 −7𝑥2 + 9 Specific behaviours   factored form using roots   substitutes fourth point and determines correct value of 𝑏   correct expanded form Solution See graph Specific behaviours   all roots   labelled maximum   labelled minimum   smooth curve Solution (1.6667,2.6481) Specific behaviours   correct answer",
