    "calculator": "Unlabelled",
    "questionText": "Question 24 (8 marks) The height above ground level, ℎ m, of a seat on a steadily rotating Ferris wheel 𝑡 minutes after the wheel begins to move is given by ℎ= 17.5 + 15.5 cos (𝜋𝑡 6 −𝜋 3). (a) Determine the initial height of the seat. (1 mark) (b) Graph the height of the seat against time on the axes below. (4 marks) (c) Determine (i) the maximum height above ground reached by the seat. (1 mark) (ii) the time taken, to the nearest second, for the seat to first reach a height of 7 m above ground level. (2 marks) See next page Additional working space Question number(s): …………………… Additional working space Question number(s): ……………………",
    "answerText": "See next page Question 24 (8 marks) The height above ground level, ℎ m, of a seat on a steadily rotating Ferris wheel 𝑡 minutes after the wheel begins to move is given by ℎ= 17.5 + 15.5 cos (𝜋𝑡 6 −𝜋 3). (a) Determine the initial height of the seat. (1 marks) Solution ℎ(0) = 25.25 m Specific behaviours   correct height (b) Graph the height of the seat against time on the axes below. (4 marks) (c) Determine (i) the maximum height above ground reached by the seat. (1 mark) Solution  ℎ𝑀𝐴𝑋= 33 m Specific behaviours   correct height (ii) the time taken, to the nearest second, for the seat to first reach a height of 7 m above ground level. (2 marks) Solution  ℎ= 7 ⇒𝑡= 6.42  0.42 × 60 = 25  𝑡= 6 m 25 s (385 s) Specific behaviours   time as decimal   time to nearest second Solution  See graph Specific behaviours   (0, 25) and (24, 25)   correct maximums   correct minimums   smooth curve",
