    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-172-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 19 (7 marks) The equation of a parabola is 𝑦= 1 4(𝑥2 −6𝑥+ 15). (a) Sketch the parabola on the axes below. (3 marks) All parabolas have a focal point and a directrix. For a parabola with equation 𝑦= 𝑎(𝑥−𝑝)2 + 𝑞, the focal point is at (𝑝, 𝑞+ 1 4𝑎) and the equation of the directrix is 𝑦= 𝑞−1 4𝑎, where 𝑎, 𝑝 and 𝑞 are constants. (b) Determine the focal point and directrix for this parabola and add them, with labels, to your sketch above. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 14 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-172-8 Question 19 (7 marks) The equation of a parabola is 𝑦= 1 4(𝑥2 −6𝑥+ 15). (a) Sketch the parabola on the axes below. (3 marks) All parabolas have a focal point and a directrix. For a parabola with equation 𝑦= 𝑎(𝑥−𝑝)2 + 𝑞, the focal point is at (𝑝, 𝑞+ 1 4𝑎) and the equation of the directrix is 𝑦= 𝑞−1 4𝑎, where 𝑎, 𝑝 and 𝑞 are constants. (b) Determine the focal point and directrix for this parabola and add them, with labels, to your sketch above. (4 marks) Solution From graph, turning point at (3, 1.5). Hence 𝑎= 1 4 , 𝑝= 3, 𝑞= 1.5 Focal point: (3, 2.5) and directrix: 𝑦= 0.5. Specific behaviours  indicates turning point  indicates values of all constants  plots focus  draws directrix Solution See graph Specific behaviours  correct turning point  correct 𝑦-intercept  smooth symmetrical curve",
