    "answerText": "See next page Question 20 (7 marks) The diagram shows sector 𝑂𝑀𝑁 of a circle centre 𝑂 of radius 29 cm and 𝛼= 68°. Circle 𝐶 is inside the sector and just touches 𝑂𝑀, 𝑂𝑁 and arc 𝑀𝑁. (a) Determine the area of sector 𝑂𝑀𝑁. (2 marks) (b) Show that the radius of circle 𝐶 is 10.4 cm, correct to one decimal place. (3 marks) Solution Extend sector sides to form isosceles triangle: 𝑃𝑁′ = 29 tan (68° 2 ) = 19.56 cm 𝑟= 19.56 tan (56° 2 ) = 10.4 cm Specific behaviours  forms isosceles triangle, shows angles  calculates 𝑃𝑁′  calculates radius (c) Determine the area of the shaded region, inside sector 𝑂𝑀𝑁 but outside circle 𝐶. (2 marks) Solution 𝐴𝐶= 𝜋(10.4)2 ≈340 Shaded area = 499 −340 = 159 cm2 Specific behaviours  calculates area of circle  calculates shaded area, with units NB: Answer only ok Solution 𝐴= 68° 360° × 𝜋(29)2 = 14297𝜋 90 ≈499 cm2 Specific behaviours  indicates suitable method  calculates area Alternate Solution 2 2 2 2 29 ( ) tan34 r y r y x r r x       CAS solve: 10.4 r cm  Specific behaviours  forms triangle OCQ  sets up three equations to solve simultaneously  calculates radius r x y Q",
