    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-192-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 9 (8 marks) A calculator is used to randomly generate a whole number between 4 and 12 inclusive. Event 𝐴 occurs when the number is odd, event 𝐵 occurs when the number is prime and event 𝐶 occurs when the number is less than 9. (a) Determine the ordered set of all possible outcomes for the event (i) 𝐶 (1 mark) (ii) 𝐴∪𝐶. (1 mark) (iii) 𝐴̅ ∩𝐵̅ ∩𝐶̅. (2 marks) (b) Determine (i) 𝑃(𝐵∩𝐶). (2 marks) (ii) 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵∪𝐶 ̅̅̅̅̅̅̅). (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-192-4 Question 9 (8 marks) A calculator is used to randomly generate a whole number between 4 and 12 inclusive. Event 𝐴 occurs when the number is odd, event 𝐵 occurs when the number is prime and event 𝐶 occurs when the number is less than 9. (a) Determine the ordered set of all possible outcomes for the event (i) 𝐶 (1 mark) (ii) 𝐴∪𝐶. (1 mark) Solution 𝐴∪𝐶= {4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 11 } Specific behaviours  correct ordered list (iii) 𝐴̅ ∩𝐵̅ ∩𝐶̅. (2 marks) (b) Determine (i) 𝑃(𝐵∩𝐶). (2 marks) (ii) 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵∪𝐶 ̅̅̅̅̅̅̅). (2 marks) Solution Odd numbers that are not prime and more than eight: 𝐴∩𝐵∪𝐶 ̅̅̅̅̅̅̅ = {9} 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵∪𝐶 ̅̅̅̅̅̅̅) = 1 9 Specific behaviours  identifies subset  correct probability Solution Primes that are no more than 8: 𝐵∩𝐶= {5, 7} 𝑃(𝐵∩𝐶) = n(𝐵∩𝐶) n(𝑈) = 2 9 Specific behaviours  identifies subset  correct probability Solution Numbers that are in none of the sets: 𝐴̅ ∩𝐵̅ ∩𝐶̅ = {10, 12} Specific behaviours  appropriate working ie list relevant sets  correct ordered list Solution 𝐶 = {4, 5, 6, 7, 8 } Specific behaviours  correct ordered list (penalise lack of curly brackets once in whole question)",
