    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-192-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 11 (10 marks) The time of sunrise, 𝑡 hours after midnight, on the 𝑛th day of the year in Esperance is closely modelled by 𝑡= 6.27 −1.71 sin(0.0172𝑛+ 2.083). (a) Use the model to calculate, in hours and minutes, the time of sunrise on 5th February, rounding to the nearest minute. (2 marks) (b) Graph 𝑡 as a function of 𝑛 on the axes below for 0 ≤𝑛≤365. (4 marks) (c) Jill lives in Esperance and is woken by her alarm clock at 6: 12 am every day. How many days will she have woken after sunrise in a year of 365 days? (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-192-4 Question 11 (10 marks) The time of sunrise, 𝑡 hours after midnight, on the 𝑛th day of the year in Esperance is closely modelled by 𝑡= 6.27 −1.71 sin(0.0172𝑛+ 2.083). (a) Use the model to calculate, in hours and minutes, the time of sunrise on 5 February rounding to the nearest minute. (2 marks) (b) Graph 𝑡 as a function of 𝑛 on the axes below for 0 ≤𝑛≤365. (4 marks) (c) Jill lives in Esperance and is woken by her alarm clock at 6: 12 am every day. How many days will she have woken up after sunrise in a year of 365 days? (4 marks) Solution 𝑛= 31 + 5 = 36, 𝑡(36) = 5.543 = 5: 33 am Specific behaviours  correct value of 𝑛  correct time in hours and minutes rounded correctly Solution See graph Specific behaviours  endpoints  maximum  minimum  smooth curve Solution 6: 12 am →6.2 h, 𝑡= 6.2 when 𝑛= 59.17, 𝑛= 246.58 (see dotted line on graph). 6.12 = 6.27 −1.71 sin(0.0172𝑛+ 2.083) 𝑡< 6.2 when 𝑛≤59, 𝑛≥247. Hence awake days 1 through 59 and 247 through 365, which is 178 days. Specific behaviours  indicates 6: 12 am →6.2 h,  solves for 𝑡= 6.2  indicates correct intervals of days  correct number of days, allow 177 if used 6",
