    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-192-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 13 (7 marks) In a random sample of 315 cats, it was found that 107 of the cats were males with green- coloured eyes, and 92 of the 148 females had green-coloured eyes. (a) Complete all the regions of the table below to represent this situation. (2 marks) Gender Eye Colour Green Not Green Total Male Female Total 315 (b) Determine the probability that a randomly selected cat from the sample (i) is female. (1 mark) (ii) is female or does not have green-coloured eyes. (2 marks) (iii) is female given that it has green-coloured eyes. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-192-4 Question 13 (7 marks) In a random sample of 315 cats, it was found that 107 of the cats were males with green- coloured eyes, and 92 of the 148 females had green-coloured eyes. (a) Complete all the regions in the Venn diagram to represent this situation. (2 marks) Gender Eye Colour Green Not Green Total Male 107 60 167 Female 92 56 148 Total 199 116 315 (b) Determine the probability that a randomly selected cat from the sample (i) is female. (1 mark) (ii) is female or does not have green-coloured eyes. (2 marks) (iii) is female given that it has green-coloured eyes. (2 marks) Solution Specific behaviours  107 and 92 correct  all correct Solution 𝑃(𝐹) = 148 315 ≈0.4698 Specific behaviours  correct probability Solution 𝑃(𝐹∪𝐺̅) = 𝑃(𝐹) + 𝑃(𝐹̅ ∩𝐺̅) = 148 + 60 315 = 208 315 ≈0.6603 Specific behaviours  correct numerator  correct probability Solution 𝑃(𝐹|𝐺) = 𝑃(𝐹∩𝐺) 𝑃(𝐺) = 92 92 + 107 = 92 199 ≈0.4623 Specific behaviours  correct denominator 199  correct numerator 92",
