    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-192-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 14 (9 marks) A function defined by 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑎 𝑥+ 𝑏 , where 𝑎 and 𝑏 are constants, passes through the points (−8, 0.2) and (2, −0.6). (a) Determine the value of 𝑎 and the value of 𝑏. (3 marks) (b) Draw the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) on the axes below, clearly indicating the coordinates of all axes intercepts and equations of any asymptotes. (4 marks) (c) State the equations of all asymptotes of the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(2𝑥) −3. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-192-4 Question 14 (9 marks) A function defined by 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑎 𝑥+ 𝑏 , where 𝑎 and 𝑏 are constants, passes through the points (−8, 0.2) and (2, −0.6). (a) Determine the value of 𝑎 and the value of 𝑏. (3 marks) (b) Draw the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) on the axes below, clearly indicating the coordinates of all axes intercepts and equations of any asymptotes. (4 marks) (c) State the equations of all asymptotes of the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(2𝑥) −3. (2 marks) Solution 0.2 = 𝑎 −8 + 𝑏, −0.6 = 𝑎 2 + 𝑏 Solve simultaneously using CAS: 𝑎= −1.5, 𝑏= 0.5 Specific behaviours  uses points to form two equations  value of 𝑎  value of 𝑏 Solution See graph Specific behaviours  location of intercept  equations of both asymptotes  LHS, smooth curve, thru' (−2, 1)  RHS, smooth curve, thru' (1, −1) Solution 𝑦= 0 −3 →𝑦= −3, 𝑥= −1 2 ÷ 2 →𝑥= −1 4 Specific behaviours  equations of horizontal asymptote  equations of vertical asymptote",
