    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-192-4 Question 15 (7 marks) Let 𝑓(𝑥) = √𝑥+ 9 −4. (a) Sketch the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) on the axes below. (3 marks) (b) State the domain and range of (i) 𝑓(3𝑥) −3. (2 marks) (ii) 4𝑓(𝑥−4). (2 marks) Solution Horizontal dilation scale factor 1 3: 𝐷𝑓= {𝑥: 𝑥∈ℝ, 𝑥≥−3} Vertical translation 3 units downwards: 𝑅𝑓= {𝑦: 𝑦∈ℝ, 𝑦≥−7} Specific behaviours  correct domain  correct range just inequalities is OK but -1 once if not referred as domain or range Solution See graph. Specific behaviours  correctly locates endpoint at (−9, −4)  axes intercepts  smooth curve, no inflections Solution Horizontal translation 4 units right: 𝐷𝑓= {𝑥: 𝑥∈ℝ, 𝑥≥−5} Vertical dilation scale factor 4: 𝑅𝑓= {𝑦: 𝑦∈ℝ, 𝑦≥−16} Specific behaviours  correct domain  correct range",
