    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-192-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 17 (7 marks) A block of land 𝑃𝑄𝑅𝑆 is bounded by four straight sides, with 𝑃 the most westerly corner. The lengths of sides 𝑃𝑆 and 𝑄𝑅 are 136 m and 155 m respectively and 𝑄 lies 255 m due north of 𝑆. Diagonal 𝑃𝑅 makes an angle of 54° with 𝑃𝑆 and 30° with 𝑅𝑆. (a) Sketch a diagram of the block, showing all the above information. (2 marks) (b) Determine the length of side 𝑅𝑆. (2 marks) (c) Determine the bearing of 𝑅 from 𝑄. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-192-4 Question 17 (7 marks) A block of land 𝑃𝑄𝑅𝑆 is bounded by four straight sides, with 𝑃 the most westerly corner. The lengths of sides 𝑃𝑆 and 𝑄𝑅 are 136 m and 155 m respectively and 𝑄 lies 255 m due north of 𝑆. Diagonal 𝑃𝑅 makes an angle of 54° with 𝑃𝑆 and 30° with 𝑅𝑆. (a) Sketch a diagram of the block, showing all the above information. (2 marks) (b) Determine the length of side 𝑅𝑆. (2 marks) (c) Determine the bearing of 𝑅 from 𝑄. (3 marks) Solution Specific behaviours  correct orientation of sides  shows neatly three side lengths and two angles Solution In triangle 𝑄𝑅𝑆: 𝑅𝑆 sin 54° = 136 sin30° →𝑅𝑆= 220.1 m Specific behaviours  correct use of a trigonometric rule  correct length Solution In triangle 𝑄𝑅𝑆: cos ∠𝑆𝑄𝑅= 1552 + 2552 −220.12 2(155)(255) ∠𝑆𝑄𝑅= 59.1° Hence bearing is 180° −59° = 121° Specific behaviours  correct use of a trigonometric rule  correct angle  correct bearing",
