    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-192-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 18 (7 marks) Researchers found that 10% of rock lobsters were carriers of a newly detected shell disease. The researchers trialed a test to detect whether or not a lobster was a carrier of the disease. It was found that the test returned a positive result in 90% of the lobsters who were carriers of the disease but unfortunately incorrectly returned a negative result in the other 10%. When the test was administered with lobsters that were known not to be carriers of the disease, 95% came back as a negative result but for the other 5% an incorrect positive result was returned. (a) Complete the tree diagram below showing all probabilities and outcomes. (3 marks) (b) What is the probability that the test will return a correct result? (2 marks) (c) If a lobster returns a positive result, what is the probability that they are a carrier? (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-192-4 Question 18 (7 marks) Researchers found that 10% of rock lobsters were carriers of a newly detected shell disease. The researchers trialed a test to detect whether or not a lobster was a carrier of the disease. It was found that the test returned a positive result in 90% of the lobsters who were carriers of the disease but unfortunately incorrectly returned a negative result in the other 10%. When the test was administered with lobsters that were known not to be carriers of the disease, 95% came back as a negative result but for the other 5% an incorrect positive result was returned. (a) Complete the tree diagram below showing all probabilities and outcomes. (3 marks) (b) What is the probability that the test will return a correct result? (2 marks) Solution P(Correct) = 0.1 x 0.9 + 0.9 x 0.95 = 0.945 Specific behaviours  correct prob for carrier and pos 0.1 x 0.9  correct answer (c) If a lobster returns a positive result, what is the probability that they are a carrier? (2 marks) Solution P(carr/pos) = 0.1 x 0.9 0.1 x 0.9 + 0.9 x 0.05 = 0.09 0.135 = 2 3 Specific behaviours  correct denominator  correct answer Soluti",
