    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-192-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 19 (10 marks) The graph of the cubic polynomial 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) passes through the points (−1, 0), (0, 9) and has a minimum turning point at (3, 0). (a) Use only the above information to sketch the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) on the axes below. (3 marks) Let 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑥3 + 𝑏𝑥2 + 𝑐𝑥+ 𝑑, where 𝑏, 𝑐 and 𝑑 are constants. (b) Determine the value of each of the constants 𝑏, 𝑐 and 𝑑. (3 marks) CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 METHODS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-192-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF (c) Another cubic polynomial is defined by 𝑔(𝑥) = 𝑥3 −6𝑥2 + 𝑎𝑥+ 5. Determine the value(s) of the constant 𝑎 so that the graphs of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) and 𝑦= 𝑔(𝑥) do not intersect. (4 marks) © 2022 WA Exam Papers. Rossmoyne Senior High School has a non-exclusive licence to copy and communicate this document for non-commercial, educational use within the school. No other copying, communication or use is permitted without the express written permission of WA Exam Papers. SN085-192-2.",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of questions SN085-192-4 Question 19 (10 marks) The graph of the cubic polynomial 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) passes through the points (−1, 0), (0, 9) and has a minimum turning point at (3, 0). (a) Use only the above information to sketch the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) on the axes below. (3 marks) Let 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑥3 + 𝑏𝑥2 + 𝑐𝑥+ 𝑑, where 𝑏, 𝑐 and 𝑑 are constants. (b) Determine the value of each of the constants 𝑏, 𝑐 and 𝑑. (3 marks) Solution See graph Specific behaviours  smooth cubic curve  graph tangent to x-axis at x=3  locates both other intercepts Solution Factored form of cubic is 𝑓(𝑥) = (𝑥−3)2(𝑥+ 1) Hence 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑥3 −5𝑥2 + 3𝑥+ 9 And so 𝑏= −5, 𝑐= 3, 𝑑= 9 Specific behaviours  correct factored form of cubic  expands cubic  correct value for each constant",
