    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 3 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Section Two: Calculator-assumed 65% (101 Marks) This section has twelve questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 8 (7 marks) (a) Given that 𝑓(𝑥) = 4𝑥2 + 3𝑥+ 1, determine 𝑓(− 1 3 ). (1 mark) (b) State the natural domain and range for the following functions. (i) 𝑓(𝑥) = 3 𝑥+ 4 . (2 marks) (ii) 𝑔(𝑥) = 5 −√𝑥−2. (2 marks) (c) Determine the range of the function 𝑓(𝑥) = (𝑥−1)2 −3 for the domain 0 ≤𝑥≤4. (2 marks) Solution 𝑓(−1 3) = 4 9 Specific behaviours ✓ correct value Solution The domain is 𝑥≠−4 and the range is 𝑦≠0. Specific behaviours ✓ correct domain ✓ correct range Solution The domain is 𝑥≥2 and the range is 𝑦≤5. Specific behaviours ✓ correct domain ✓ correct range Solution 𝑓 has a minimum at (1, −3), 𝑓(0) = −2 and 𝑓(4) = 6. Hence range is −3 ≤𝑦≤6. Specific behaviours ✓ once correct bound of range ✓ correct range",
