    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 9 (7 marks) The diagram below shows the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥), where 𝑓 is a function with domain −6 ≤𝑥≤13. Determine the coordinates of the following point(s): (a) the 𝑦-axis intercept of the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥−4). (1 mark) (b) the roots of the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) + 1. (2 marks) (c) the maximum of the graph of 𝑦= −4𝑓(𝑥). (2 marks) (d) the minimum of the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥 2) −7. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 9 (7 marks) The diagram below shows the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥), where 𝑓 is a function with domain −6 ≤𝑥≤13. Determine the coordinates of the following point(s): (a) the 𝑦-axis intercept of the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥−4). (1 mark) (b) the roots of the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) + 1. (2 marks) (c) the maximum of the graph of 𝑦= −4𝑓(𝑥). (2 marks) (d) the minimum of the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥 2) −7. (2 marks) Solution Graph is translated 4 units right: (0, −1). Specific behaviours ✓ correct coordinates Solution Graph is translated 1 units upwards: (−4, 0), (2, 0) and (12, 0). Specific behaviours ✓ any correct root ✓ three correct roots Solution Vertical dilation factor −4, min of 𝑓(𝑥) transformed to max of −4𝑓(𝑥): (−2, 20). Specific behaviours ✓ vertical dilation of any of the four points by factor −4 ✓ correct coordinates of minimum Solution Horizontal dilation factor 2 and translation 7 down: (−4, −12). Specific behaviours ✓ correct 𝑥-coordinate ✓ correct 𝑦-coordinate",
