    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 10 (8 marks) The vertical height ℎ, in metres, of the tip of a wind turbine blade above its centre of rotation at time 𝑡 seconds, 𝑡≥0, is shown in the graph below. (a) State the amplitude and period of the trigonometric function ℎ. (2 marks) A similar function for a second wind turbine blade is given by ℎ2 = 60 sin(2𝜋𝑡 3 ) , 𝑡≥0. (b) State the period of this second function and hence determine how many revolutions per minute this blade is rotating at. (2 marks) (c) Add the graph of function ℎ2 to the axes above. (3 marks) (d) At what time does the tip of the second blade first reach its maximum height? (1 mark)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 10 (8 marks) The vertical height ℎ, in metres, of the tip of a wind turbine blade above its centre of rotation at time 𝑡 seconds, 𝑡≥0, is shown in the graph below. (a) State the amplitude and period of the trigonometric function ℎ. (2 marks) A similar function for a second wind turbine blade is given by ℎ2 = 60 sin(2𝜋𝑡 3 ) , 𝑡≥0. (b) State the period of this second function and hence determine how many revolutions per minute this blade is rotating at. (2 marks) (c) Add the graph of function ℎ2 to the axes above. (3 marks) (d) At what time does the tip of the second blade first reach its maximum height? (1 mark) Solution (c) See graph Specific behaviours ✓ turning points ✓ roots ✓ smooth curve Solution Amplitude: 50 m. Period: 8 seconds. Specific behaviours ✓ amplitude ✓ period Solution Period: 𝜔= 2𝜋÷ 2𝜋 3 = 3 seconds. Rotating at 60 ÷ 3 = 20 rpm. Specific behaviours ✓ period ✓ rotational speed Solution First maximum of graph at 3 ÷ 4 = 0.75 seconds. Specific behaviours ✓ correct time",
