    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 11 (9 marks) A dodecahedral dice has 12 sides, each numbered with a different integer between 1 and 12 inclusive. When the dice is rolled once, event 𝐴 occurs if the number is even, event 𝐵 occurs if the number is less than 8 and event 𝐶 occurs if the number is a multiple of 3. (a) List the sets A, B, and C when the dice is thrown once. (1 mark) (b) Write a brief word description of the numbers in the outcome set 𝐵∩ 𝐴. (1 mark) (c) List the following sets of outcomes: (i) 𝐵∪𝐶 (2 marks) (ii) 𝐴∩𝐵. (1 mark) (iii) 𝐴∪𝐵∪𝐶. (1 mark) (iv) 𝐴∩𝐵∩𝐶. (1 mark) (d) Determine P( 𝐴∩𝐵∩𝐶). (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 11 (9 marks) A dodecahedral dice has 12 sides, each numbered with a different integer between 1 and 12 inclusive. When the dice is rolled once, event 𝐴 occurs if the number is even, event 𝐵 occurs if the number is less than 8 and event 𝐶 occurs if the number is a multiple of 3. (a) List the sets A, B, and C when the dice is thrown once. (1 mark) (b) Write a brief word description of the numbers in the outcome set 𝐵∩ 𝐴. (1 mark) (c) List the following sets of outcomes: (i) 𝐵∪𝐶 (2 marks) (ii) 𝐴∩𝐵. (1 mark) (iii) 𝐴∪𝐵∪𝐶. (1 mark) (iv) 𝐴∩𝐵∩𝐶. (1 mark) (d) Determine P( 𝐴∩𝐵∩𝐶). (2 marks) Solution A = {2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12} B = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7} C = {3, 6, 9, 12} Specific behaviours ✓ correct description Solution Odd numbers less than 8 Specific behaviours ✓ correct description Solution 𝐵∪𝐶= {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 12} Specific behaviours ✓ correct elements ✓ use of curly brackets (penalise once in question) Solution 𝐴∩𝐵= {8, 10, 12} Specific behaviours ✓ correct set Solution 𝐴∪𝐵∪𝐶= {11} Specific behaviours ✓ correct set Solution 𝐴∩𝐵∩𝐶= {6} Specific behaviours ✓ correct",
