    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 14 (7 marks) The table below shows the results of a random survey of 200 customers who recently bought a new TV from a large store. The customers were asked which brand of TV they bought and whether they would buy the same brand again. Buy same brand again TV Brand Sense Sunny GL Other Yes 14 31 19 24 No 11 15 8 30 Unsure 7 6 10 25 A customer who recently bought a TV from the store is selected at random. Use the above data to determine a point estimate for the probability that (a) the TV they bought was a Sunny and that they would not buy the same brand again. (1 mark) (b) they are unsure whether they would buy the same brand of TV again. (1 mark) (c) the brand of TV they bought was not GL. (1 mark) (d) they would not buy the same brand of TV again, given that the brand they bought was not ‘Other’. (2 marks) CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF (e) the brand of TV they bought was Sense or GL, given that they would buy the same brand again. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 14 (7 marks) The table below shows the results of a random survey of 200 customers who recently bought a new TV from a large store. The customers were asked which brand of TV they bought and whether they would buy the same brand again. Buy same brand again TV Brand Sense Sunny GL Other Yes 14 31 19 24 No 11 15 8 30 Unsure 7 6 10 25 A customer who recently bought a TV from the store is selected at random. Use the above data to determine a point estimate for the probability that (a) the TV they bought was a Sunny and that they would not buy the same brand again. (1 mark) (b) they are unsure whether they would buy the same brand of TV again. (1 mark) (c) the brand of TV they bought was not GL. (1 mark) (d) they would not buy the same brand of TV again, given that the brand they bought was not ‘Other’. (2 marks) Solution 𝑃= 15 200 (= 3 40 = 0.075) Specific behaviours ✓ correct probability Solution 𝑃= 7 + 6 + 10 + 25 200 = 48 200 (= 6 25 = 0.24) Specific behaviours ✓ correct probability Solution 𝑃= 200 −(19 + 8 + 10) 200 = 200 −37 200 = 163 200 (= 0.815) Specific behav",
