    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 15 (10 marks) (a) Determine the area of triangle 𝑂𝑃𝑄 when ∠𝑃𝑂𝑄= 134°, 𝑂𝑃= 19 cm and 𝑂𝑄= 24 cm. (2 marks) (b) Triangle 𝑂𝑋𝑌 has an area of 175 cm2 and has sides 𝑂𝑋= 43 cm and 𝑂𝑌= 25 cm. Determine the size of angle ∠𝑂𝑋𝑌, giving your answer(s) in degrees correct to one decimal place. (8 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 15 (10 marks) (a) Determine the area of triangle 𝑂𝑃𝑄 when ∠𝑃𝑂𝑄= 134°, 𝑂𝑃= 19 cm and 𝑂𝑄= 24 cm. (2 marks) (b) Triangle 𝑂𝑋𝑌 has an area of 175 cm2 and has sides 𝑂𝑋= 43 cm and 𝑂𝑌= 25 cm. Determine the size of angle ∠𝑂𝑋𝑌, giving your answer(s) in degrees correct to one decimal place. (8 marks) Solution 𝐴= 1 2 (19)(24) sin134° = 164 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ correct use of area formula ✓ correct area Solution 175 = 1 2 (43)(25) sin ∠𝑋𝑂𝑌 ∠𝑋𝑂𝑌= 19° or 180° −19° = 161° 𝑋𝑌2 = 432 + 252 −2(43)(25) cos ∠𝑋𝑂𝑌 When ∠𝑋𝑂𝑌= 19°, 𝑋𝑌= 21.0 cm and when ∠𝑋𝑂𝑌= 161°, 𝑋𝑌= 67.13 cm. sin ∠𝑂𝑋𝑌 25 = sin 19° 21.0 ⇒∠𝑂𝑋𝑌= 22.8° sin ∠𝑂𝑋𝑌 25 = sin 161° 67.13 ⇒∠𝑂𝑋𝑌= 7.0° Hence ∠𝑂𝑋𝑌= 22.8° or 7.0°. Specific behaviours ✓ correct equation for ∠𝑋𝑂𝑌 ✓✓ two correct values for ∠𝑋𝑂𝑌 ✓ correct equation for 𝑋𝑌 ✓ at least one correct value for 𝑋𝑌 ✓ correct equation for ∠𝑂𝑋𝑌 ✓✓ two correct values for ∠𝑂𝑋𝑌",
