    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 16 (9 marks) Records kept by a café on an industrial estate show that 74% of its customers work in transport and the remainder in other jobs. 45% of the customers who work in transport order chips with their meal, whilst for other customers the figure is 30%. (a) Determine the probability that a customer who arrives at random at the café (i) does not work in transport and orders chips with their meal. (2 marks) (ii) does not order chips with their meal. (3 marks) (iii) works in transport given that they order chips with their meal. (2 marks) (b) Explain whether the records kept by the café indicate that working in transport and ordering chips with a meal are independent events for their customers. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 16 (9 marks) Records kept by a café on an industrial estate show that 74% of its customers work in transport and the remainder in other jobs. 45% of the customers who work in transport order chips with their meal, whilst for other customers the figure is 30%. (a) Determine the probability that a customer who arrives at random at the café (i) does not work in transport and orders chips with their meal. (2 marks) (ii) does not order chips with their meal. (3 marks) (iii) works in transport given that they order chips with their meal. (2 marks) (b) Explain whether the records kept by the café indicate that working in transport and ordering chips with a meal are independent events for their customers. (2 marks) Solution P( 𝑇∩𝐶) = (1 −0.74) × 0.3 = 0.26 × 0.3 = 0.078 (= 39 500) Specific behaviours ✓ shows correct use of probability rule ✓ correct probability Solution P( 𝐶) = P(𝑇∩𝐶) + P( 𝑇∩𝐶) = 0.74 × (1 −0.45) + 0.26 × (1 −0.3) = 0.74 × 0.55 + 0.26 × 0.7 = 0.407 + 0.182 = 0.589 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates correct probability for 𝑇∩𝐶 ✓ indicates correct probability ",
