    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 17 (9 marks) A newsagent has a stock of 36 greeting cards, all different to each other, of which 10 are birthday, 11 are anniversary and the remainder are blank cards. (a) Determine the number of different selections of three blank cards that could be made from the newsagent. (2 marks) (b) Determine the number of different selections of six cards that could be made from the birthday and anniversary cards stocked by the newsagent. (2 marks) (c) The newsagent just sold two of the 36 greeting cards. (i) Determine the number of different selections of two cards that could be sold. (1 mark) (ii) Determine the probability that both were birthday cards. (2 marks) (iii) Determine the probability that at least one of them was an anniversary card. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 17 (9 marks) A newsagent has a stock of 36 greeting cards, all different to each other, of which 10 are birthday, 11 are anniversary and the remainder are blank cards. (a) Determine the number of different selections of three blank cards that could be made from the newsagent. (2 marks) (b) Determine the number of different selections of six cards that could be made from the birthday and anniversary cards stocked by the newsagent. (2 marks) (c) The newsagent just sold two of the 36 greeting cards. (i) Determine the number of different selections of two cards that could be sold. (1 mark) (ii) Determine the probability that both were birthday cards. (2 marks) (iii) Determine the probability that at least one of them was an anniversary card. (2 marks) Solution There are 36 −10 −11 = 15 blank cards and (15 3 ) = 455 selections. Specific behaviours ✓ reasonable attempt to use combination formula ✓ correct number Solution There are 10 + 11 = 21 cards to choose from and (21 6 ) = 54 264 selections. Specific behaviours ✓ reasonable attempt to use combination formula ✓ corr",
