    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 19 (11 marks) The figure shown in the diagram consists of sector 𝑂𝐴𝐵 of circle with centre 𝑂 and a semi-circle with diameter 𝑂𝐵. Let 𝑂𝐴= 𝑂𝐵= 𝑥 and ∠𝐴𝑂𝐵= 𝛽 radians. (a) Let 𝑥= 12 cm and the area of the semi-circle be three times the area of the sector. (i) Show algebraically that 𝛽 is equal to 𝜋 12. (3 marks) (ii) Determine the perimeter of the figure. (3 marks) CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 METHODS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF (b) By first determining a new value for 𝛽, determine the area of the figure when the area of the semi-circle is five times the area of the sector and the new perimeter of the figure is 77.2 cm. (5 marks) © 2023 WA Exam Papers. Rossmoyne Senior High School has a non-exclusive licence to copy and communicate this document for non-commercial, educational use within the school. No other copying, communication or use is permitted without the express written permission of WA Exam Papers. SN085-212-2.",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-212-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 19 (11 marks) The figure shown in the diagram consists of sector 𝑂𝐴𝐵 of circle with centre 𝑂 and a semi-circle with diameter 𝑂𝐵. Let 𝑂𝐴= 𝑂𝐵= 𝑥 and ∠𝐴𝑂𝐵= 𝛽 radians. (a) Let 𝑥= 12 cm and the area of the semi-circle be three times the area of the sector. (i) Show algebraically that 𝛽 is equal to 𝜋 12. (3 marks) (ii) Determine the perimeter of the figure. (3 marks) Solution Let area of sector be 𝐴𝑆 and of semi-circle be 𝐴𝐶. 𝐴𝑆= 1 2 × 122𝛽= 72𝛽, 𝐴𝐶= 1 2 𝜋(12 2 ) 2 = 18𝜋 3𝐴𝑠= 𝐴𝐶 3 × 72𝛽= 18𝜋 𝛽= 18𝜋 3 × 72 = 𝜋 12 Specific behaviours ✓ expressions for area of sector and semi-circle ✓ forms equation using ratio of areas ✓ correct value of 𝛽 in terms of 𝜋 Solution 𝑃= 𝑂𝐴+ 𝐴𝐵+ 𝐵𝑂 = 𝑥+ 𝑥𝛽+ 1 2 𝜋𝑥 = 12 + 12 × 𝜋 12 + 1 2 𝜋× 12 = 12 + 7𝜋 cm ≈33.99 cm Specific behaviours ✓ Sets up equation ✓ correct arc length 𝐴𝐵 ✓ correct perimeter",
