    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 9 (7 marks) (a) State the equation of the line of symmetry of the graph of 𝑦= 4𝑥2 −32𝑥+ 51. (1 mark) (b) State the roots of the graph of 𝑦= −2(𝑥+ 1)(𝑥−3)(𝑥−8). (1 mark) (c) Let 𝑓(𝑥) = 2√𝑥+ 4 for 0 ≤𝑥< 32. Determine the range of 𝑓(𝑥). (2 marks) (d) The function 𝑔(𝑥) = 𝑎𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 𝑐 has a turning point at (5, −8) and passes through the point (2, 10). Determine the value of each of the constants 𝑎, 𝑏 and 𝑐. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-252-4 Question 9 (7 marks) (a) State the equation of the line of symmetry of the graph of 𝑦= 4𝑥2 −32𝑥+ 51. (1 mark) (b) State the roots of the graph of 𝑦= −2(𝑥+ 1)(𝑥−3)(𝑥−8). (1 mark) (c) Let 𝑓(𝑥) = 2√𝑥+ 4 for 0 ≤𝑥< 32. Determine the range of 𝑓(𝑥). (2 marks) (d) The function 𝑔(𝑥) = 𝑎𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 𝑐 has a turning point at (5, −8) and passes through the point (2, 10). Determine the value of each of the constants 𝑎, 𝑏 and 𝑐. (3 marks) Solution Turning point form: 𝑦= 𝑎(𝑥−5)2 −8 Using (2, 10): 10 = 𝑎(2 −5)2 −8 ⇒9𝑎= 18 ⇒𝑎= 2 Expanding: 𝑦= 2(𝑥−5)2 −8 = 2𝑥2 −20𝑥+ 42 𝑎= 2, 𝑏= −20, 𝑐= 42 Specific behaviours ✓ correct turning point form of equation, with constant ✓ correct value of 𝑎 ✓ correct values for 𝑏 and 𝑐 Solution 𝑓(0) = 4, 𝑓(32) = 12 Range is 4 ≤𝑦< 12 or 𝑦∈[4,12). Specific behaviours ✓ correct lower bound and inequality ✓ correct upper bound and inequality Solution 𝑥= −−32 2(4) →𝑥= 4 Specific behaviours ✓ correct equation Solution 𝑥= −1, 𝑥= 3, 𝑥= 8 Specific behaviours ✓ correct roots",
