    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 7 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 12 (9 marks) (a) Evaluate the number of combinations given by (33 3 ). (1 mark) (b) State the value(s) of 𝑛 and the value(s) of 𝑟 when (𝑛 𝑟) = 𝑛! 8! 5! . (2 marks) Sophia can only fit 3 desserts on a single plate at a buffet. So, Sophia selects 3 desserts from 13 desserts offered at the buffet, 7 of which are hot and the remainder cold. (c) How many different selections are possible? (2 marks) (d) How many different selections are possible if they must all be cold? (2 marks) (e) If the selection is made at random, determine the probability that all the desserts chosen are hot. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 METHODS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-252-4 Question 12 (9 marks) (a) Evaluate the number of combinations given by (33 3 ). (1 mark) (b) State the value(s) of 𝑛 and the value(s) of 𝑟 when (𝑛 𝑟) = 𝑛! 8! 5! . (2 marks) Sophia can only fit 3 desserts on a single plate at a buffet. So, Sophia selects 3 desserts from 13 desserts offered at the buffet, 7 of which are hot and the remainder cold. (c) How many different selections are possible? (2 marks) (d) How many different selections are possible if they must all be cold? (2 marks) (e) If the selection is made at random, determine the probability that all the desserts chosen are hot. (2 marks) Solution (13 3 ) = 286 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates use of combination formula ✓ correct number Solution 𝑛= 8 + 5 = 13 𝑟= 5 or 𝑟= 8 Specific behaviours ✓ value of 𝑛 ✓ values of 𝑟 Solution (33 3 ) = 5456 Specific behaviours ✓ correct value Solution (13 −7 3 ) = (6 3) = 20 Specific behaviours ✓ use of combination formula with restriction ✓ correct number Solution (7 3) = 35 P(All hot) = 35 286 ≈0.1224 Specific behaviours ✓ correct number ✓ correct probability AO ok",
