    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-252-4 Question 13 (7 marks) The function defined by 𝑃(𝑥) = 33 −47𝑥+ 15𝑥2 −𝑥3 for 0 ≤𝑥≤11 was used to model the monthly profit 𝑃, in thousands of dollars, when a factory set the production rate of a chemical to 𝑥 thousand litres per day. The graph of 𝑦= 𝑃(𝑥) is shown. (a) Determine 𝑃(2.7) and interpret your answer in the context of the question. (2 marks) (b) Express 𝑃(𝑥) in factored form. (1 mark) (c) State the range of the function for the given domain of 0 ≤𝑥≤11. (1 mark) (d) By only considering production rates in the interval 0 ≤𝑥≤8, determine the change in the production rate required to increase the monthly profit by $30 000 from its value when the factory is producing 4400 litres per day. (3 marks) Solution 𝑃(𝑥) = −(𝑥−1)(𝑥−3)(𝑥−11) Specific behaviours ✓ correct factored form Solution 𝑃(2.7) = −4.233 When the rate of production is 2700 litres per day, the factory will make a loss of $4233 per month. Specific behaviours ✓ correct value of function ✓ correct interpretation Solution 𝑃(4.4) = 31.416 𝑃(𝑥) = 31.416 + 30 = 61.416 ⇒𝑥= 5.483 The rate must increase by 5483 −4400 = 1083 litres per day. Specific behaviours ✓ evaluat",
