    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 METHODS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-252-4 Question 14 (8 marks) The diagram shows a circle with a hole through the middle. ∠𝐴𝑂𝐷= 5 radians and 𝐴𝐵= 𝐵𝑂= 𝑂𝐶= 𝐶𝐷= 3.3 cm (a) Determine the perimeter of the shaded region to 2d.p. (4 marks) (b) Determine the area of the shaded region to 2d.p. (4 marks) Solution Big circle area 𝜋× 6.62 = 136.848 Small circle area 𝜋× 3.32 = 34.212 Area of small circle minor segment 1 2 (3.3)2((2𝜋−5) −sin(2𝜋−5)) = 1.7656 Area is 136.848 −34.212 + 1.7656 ≈ 104.40𝑐𝑚2 Big circle area 𝜋× 6.62 = 136.848 Area of small circle major sector 1 2 (3.3)2 × 5 = 27.225 Area of ∆𝑂𝐵𝐶 1 2 (3.3)2 × sin(2𝜋−5) = 5.221 Area is 136.848 −27.225 −5.221 ≈ 104.40𝑐𝑚2 Specific behaviours ✓ correct expression for big circle area ✓ correct expression for small circle area ✓ correct expression for small circle minor segment ✓ correct shaded area ✓ correct expression for big circle area ✓ correct expression for small circle major sector ✓ correct expression for ∆𝑂𝐵𝐶 ✓ correct shaded area Solution Circumference of bigger circle 2𝜋(6.6) = 41.47 Major arc length of smaller circle 5 × 3.3 = 16.5 𝐵𝐶= √3.32 + 3.32 −2 × 3.3 × 3.3 × cos(2𝜋−5) = 3.95 Perimeter is 41.47 + 16.5",
