    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 15 (9 marks) A group of Rossmoyne students are asked whether they study Economics or History. Analysis of the 399 responses showed that 57 study both, 190 study neither and 171 study Economics. (a) Determine how many of these students study History but not Economics. (2 marks) (b) One of the students is chosen at random. Determine the probability that they (i) study Economics or History. (2 marks) (ii) study History given that they study Economics. (2 marks) (c) For these students, are the events studying Economics and studying History independent? Justify your answer. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-252-4 Question 15 (9 marks) A group of Rossmoyne students are asked whether they study Economics or History. Analysis of the 399 responses showed that 57 study both, 190 study neither and 171 study Economics. (a) Determine how many of these students study History but not Economics. (2 marks) (b) One of the students is chosen at random. Determine the probability that they (i) study Economics or History. (2 marks) (ii) study History given that they study Economics. (2 marks) (c) For these students, are the events studying Economics and studying History independent? Justify your answer. (3 marks) Solution P(𝐻|𝐸) = 57 171 = 1 3 = 0. 3̅ Specific behaviours ✓ correct numerator ✓ correct probability Solution 𝑛(𝐸∪𝐻) = 399 −190 = 209 P(𝐸∪𝐻) = 209 399 = 11 21 ≈0.5238 Specific behaviours ✓ correct 𝑛(𝐸∪𝐻) ✓ correct probability Solution 𝑛(𝐻∩𝐸̅) = 399 −171 −190 = 38 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates any correct method ✓ correct number Solution 𝑛(𝐻) = 38 + 57 = 95 P(𝐻) = 95 399 = 5 21 ≈0.2381 𝑃(𝐻) ≉𝑃(𝐻|𝐸) 0.2381 ≉0. 3̅ 𝑛(𝐸) = 171 𝑃(𝐸) = 171 399 = 3 7 ≈0.4286 𝑃(𝐸) ≉𝑃(𝐸|𝐻) 0.4286 ≉0.6 𝑃(𝐸∩𝐻) = 57 399 = 1 7 171 399 × 95 399 = 5 49 ≈0.1020 𝑃(𝐸) ×",
