    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-252-4 Question 18 (7 marks) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥), where 𝑓 is a cubic polynomial, has a turning point at (−5 2 ⁄ , 0) and passes through the points with coordinates (0, −200) and (4 3 ⁄ , 0). (a) Sketch the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) on the axes below. (3 marks) (b) Determine 𝑓(𝑥) in expanded form 𝑎𝑥3 + 𝑏𝑥2 + 𝑐𝑥+ 𝑑 where 𝑎, 𝑏, 𝑐 and 𝑑 are constants. (4 marks) Solution Using roots: 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑎(𝑥+ 5 2) 2 (𝑥−4 3) 𝑓(0) = 𝑎(0 + 5 2) 2 (0 −4 3) = −200 ⇒𝑎= 24 𝑓(𝑥) = 24 (𝑥+ 5 2) 2 (𝑥−4 3) = 24𝑥3 + 88𝑥2 −10𝑥−200 Specific behaviours ✓ attempts to use roots and constant to form 𝑓 ✓ uses repeated root as quadratic factor ✓ uses 𝑦-intercept to evaluate 𝑎 ✓ correct 𝑓(𝑥) in expanded form Solution See graph Specific behaviours ✓ indicates scale on each axis ✓ all intercepts ✓ cubic curve through points",
