    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 8 (12 marks) A thin metal plate 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴, as shown in the diagram (not to scale), consists of sector 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂 of a circle with radius 4.2 cm and centre 𝑂𝑂 joined to triangle 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂 so that 𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴𝐴 is a straight line and 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂= 5.4 cm. The size of ∠𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂= 0.65 radians and 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵 is the longest side of triangle 𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂𝑂. (a) Use the sine rule and consideration of the ambiguous case to show that the size of ∠𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 1.60 radians, correct to 2 decimal places. (4 marks) (b) Use the cosine rule to show that 𝐵𝐵𝐵𝐵= 6.94 cm, correct to 2 decimal places. (2 marks) CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF (c) Determine the perimeter of the metal plate. (3 marks) (d) Determine the area of the metal plate. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 8 (12 marks) A thin metal plate 𝐴𝐵𝐶, as shown in the diagram (not to scale), consists of sector 𝑂𝐴𝐵 of a circle with radius 4.2 cm and centre 𝑂 joined to triangle 𝑂𝐵𝐶 so that 𝐴𝑂𝐶 is a straight line and 𝑂𝐶= 5.4 cm. The size of ∠𝑂𝐶𝐵= 0.65 radians and 𝐵𝐶 is the longest side of triangle 𝑂𝐵𝐶. (a) Use the sine rule and consideration of the ambiguous case to show that the size of ∠𝐵𝑂𝐶= 1.60 radians, correct to 2 decimal places. (4 marks) Solution sin(∠𝑂𝐵𝐶) 5.4 = sin(0.65) 4.2 ✓ ∠𝑂𝐵𝐶= 0.892 or 2.25 radians. ✓ Given 𝐵𝐶 is the longest side, ∠𝑂𝐵𝐶 must be acute (< 1.57𝑟) and so ∠𝑂𝐵𝐶= 0.892. ✓ ∠𝐵𝑂𝐶= 𝜋−0.65 −0.892 = 1.59996 = 1.60 radians (2dp✓) Specific behaviours ✓ shows correct expression using sine rule and ∠𝑂𝐵𝐶 ✓ evaluates both possible values for ∠𝑂𝐵𝐶 ✓ rejects obtuse angle with some justification ( opp longest side) ✓ correct value for ∠𝐵𝑂𝐶 (b) Use the cosine rule to show that 𝐵𝐶= 6.94 cm, correct to 2 decimal places. (2 marks) Solution 𝐵𝐶= √5.42 + 4.22 −2(5.4)(4.2) cos(1.60) ✓ = 6.937 = 6.94 cm (2dp)✓ Specific behaviours ✓ correct expression for 𝐵𝐶 ✓ evaluates and rounds",
