    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 11 (5 marks) A screening test for malaria is carried out in a population in which 2% of people have malaria. The test returns one of two results - a person has the disease, or they do not. It has a sensitivity of 87% (i.e., the test indicates that people with malaria have the disease in 87% of cases) and a specificity of 94% (i.e., the test indicates that people free of malaria do not have the disease in 94% of cases). A person is randomly chosen from the population and tested. (a) Determine the probability that the person has malaria and that the test indicates they have the disease. (1 mark) (b) Determine the probability that the person has malaria, given that the test indicates that they have malaria. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 11 (5 marks) A screening test for malaria is carried out in a population in which 2% of people have malaria. The test returns one of two results - a person has the disease, or they do not. It has a sensitivity of 87% (i.e., the test indicates that people with malaria have the disease in 87% of cases) and a specificity of 94% (i.e., the test indicates that people free of malaria do not have the disease in 94% of cases). A person is randomly chosen from the population and tested. (a) Determine the probability that the person has malaria and that the test indicates they have the disease. (1 mark) Solution 𝑝= 0.02 × 0.87 = 87 5000 = 0.0174✓ Specific behaviours ✓ correct probability (b) Determine the probability that the person has malaria, given that the test indicates that they have malaria. (4 marks) Solution They do not have malaria but test indicates they do: 𝑝= 0.98 × 0.06 = 0.0588✓ Test indicates they have malaria: 𝑝= 0.0174 + 0.0588 = 0.0762✓ They have malaria, given that the test indicates they do: ✓ 𝑝",
