    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 12 (6 marks) A bridge crossed a tidal inlet so that the clearance height ℎ metres between the water surface and the bottom of the bridge varied with time 𝑡𝑡 (the number of hours after low tide at 5 am) according to the rule ℎ(𝑡𝑡) = 5.4 + 1.7 cos൬𝜋𝜋𝜋𝜋 6 ൰, 0 ≤𝑡𝑡≤24. (a) Determine what the clearance height was at (i) 5 am. (1 mark) (ii) 8: 45 am. (1 mark) (b) At what time was the clearance first a minimum and what was the clearance at this time? (2 marks) (c) A fishing boat required a clearance of at least 4.6 m to pass beneath the bridge. What was the latest time, to the nearest minute, that it could pass beneath the bridge in the morning? (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 12 (6 marks) A bridge crossed a tidal inlet so that the clearance height ℎ metres between the water surface and the bottom of the bridge varied with time 𝑡 (the number of hours after low tide at 5 am) according to the rule ℎ(𝑡) = 5.4 + 1.7 cos (𝜋𝑡 6 ) , 0 ≤𝑡≤24. (a) Determine what the clearance height was at (i) 5 am. (1 mark) (ii) 8:45 am. (1 mark) (b) At what time was the clearance first a minimum and what was the clearance at this time? (2 marks) (c) A fishing boat required a clearance of at least 4.6 m to pass beneath the bridge. What was the latest time, to the nearest minute, that it could pass beneath the bridge in the morning? (2 marks) Solution ℎ(0) = 7.1 m✓ Solution ℎ(3.75) = 4.75 m✓ Solution Minimum when cos (𝜋𝑡 6 ) = −1 ⇒𝑡= 6. At 11 am.✓ Minimum clearance will be 5.4 −1.7 = 3.7 m.✓ Specific behaviours ✓ correct time ✓ correct clearance Solution ℎ(𝑡) = 4.6 ⇒𝑡= 3.9357✓ Latest time will be at 5 + 3 56′ which is 8: 56 am.✓ Specific behaviours ✓ solves ℎ(𝑡) = 4.6 ✓ correct time, to nearest minute",
