    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 13 (6 marks) A company has placed 400 vouchers into identical unmarked envelopes as part of a promotion it is running. Each voucher admits 1, 2, 3 or 4 people to one of three sporting events as shown in the table below: Voucher admits 1 person 2 people 3 people 4 people Basketball 50 35 25 40 Football 27 17 21 45 Soccer 48 20 42 30 One envelope is selected at random from the 400. Determine the probability that the voucher in the envelope (a) is for soccer and admits 2 people. (1 mark) (b) is for basketball. (1 mark) (c) admits no more than 3 people. (1 mark) (d) admits one person or is for basketball. (1 mark) (e) admits an odd number of people given soccer is excluded (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF SN085-232-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 13 (6 marks) A company has placed 400 vouchers into identical unmarked envelopes as part of a promotion it is running. Each voucher admits 1, 2, 3 or 4 people to one of three sporting events as shown in the table below: Voucher admits 1 person 2 people 3 people 4 people Basketball 50 35 25 40 Football 27 17 21 45 Soccer 48 20 42 30 One envelope is selected at random from the 400. Determine the probability that the voucher in the envelope (a) is for soccer and admits 2 people. (1 mark) (b) is for basketball. (1 mark) (c) admits no more than 3 people. (1 mark) Solution P = 400 −(40 + 45 + 30) 400 = 285 400 = 57 80 = 0.7125✓ Specific behaviours ✓ correct probability (d) admits one person or is for basketball. (1 mark) Solution P = 50 + 27 + 48 + 35 + 25 + 40 400 = 225 400 = 9 16 = 0.5625✓ Specific behaviours ✓ correct probability (e) admits an odd number of people given soccer is excluded (2 marks) Solution P = 77 + 46 260 = 123✓ 260✓= 0.473 Specific behaviours ✓ denominator ✓numerator and/or correct answer ",
