    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-112-2 Question 11 (6 marks) A thin post stands vertically in the middle of a level playing ground. From point 𝐴 on the ground, the angle of elevation to the top of the post, 𝑇, is 21º. From point 𝐵, also on the ground but 3.25 metres further from the foot of the post than 𝐴, the angle of elevation to the top of the post is 14º. (a) Draw a sketch to represent this information. (1 mark) (b) Showing use of trigonometry, determine the height of the post. (5 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-112-4 Question 11 (6 marks) A thin post stands vertically in the middle of a level playing ground. From point 𝐴 on the ground, the angle of elevation to the top of the post, 𝑇, is 21º. From point 𝐵, also on the ground but 3.25 metres further from the foot of the post than 𝐴, the angle of elevation to the top of the post is 14º. (a) Draw a sketch to represent this information. (1 mark) (b) Showing use of trigonometry, determine the height of the post. (5 marks) Solution Specific behaviours  sketch with right-angle, two given angles and distance AB Solution 𝐴𝑇 sin 14 = 3.255 sin 7 ⇒𝐴𝑇= 6.45 ℎ= 6.45 × sin21 = 2.31 m Specific behaviours  angle 𝐵𝑇𝐴  equation using sine rule  solves for AT  use of trig in right triangle  determines h",
