    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN085-112-4 Question 13 (10 marks) A logo with triangular outline 𝐴𝐵𝐶 contains a shaded segment bounded by the straight line 𝑃𝑀 and the circular arc 𝑃𝑀 with centre 𝐵 and radius 𝐵𝑀= 25 cm, as shown below. Given that ∠𝐴𝐵𝐶= 7𝜋 12, ∠𝐵𝐶𝐴= 4∠𝐵𝐴𝐶 and 𝑀 is the midpoint of 𝐵𝐶, determine (a) the size of ∠𝐴𝐵𝐶 in degrees. (1 mark) (b) the area of the shaded segment. (2 marks) (c) the perimeter of the shaded segment. (3 marks) Solution 𝐴= 1 2 (25)2 (7𝜋 12 −sin(7𝜋 12)) ≈270.8 cm2 Specific behaviours  indicates substitution into segment area formula  evaluates area Solution 𝑃𝑀𝑎𝑟𝑐= 25 × 7𝜋 12 = 175𝜋 12 ≈45.81 𝑏= √252 + 252 −2(25)(25) cos 105 ≈39.67 Perimeter = 45.81 + 39.67 ≈85.5 cm Specific behaviours  calculates arc length  indicates use of cosine rule to find 𝑃𝑀  evaluates 𝑃𝑀 and states perimeter Solution 7𝜋 12 × 180 𝜋 = 105° Specific behaviours  converts angle",
