    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 METHODS UNIT 1 End of questions SN085-112-4 Question 21 (7 marks) Consider the points with coordinates (𝑝, 𝑞) and (𝑟, 𝑠) that lie in the first and second quadrants respectively of the unit circles shown below, where 𝜆 and 𝜃 are acute angles. Determine the following in terms of 𝑝, 𝑞, 𝑟 and 𝑠, simplifying your answers where possible. (a) sin 𝜃. (1 mark) (b) tan 𝜃. (1 mark) (c) cos(𝜋+ 𝜆). (1 mark) (d) sin(90° −𝜆). (1 mark) (e) cos(𝜃+ 𝜆). (3 marks) Solution cos(𝜃+ 𝜆) = cos 𝜃cos𝜆−sin 𝜃sin 𝜆 = (−𝑟)(𝑝) −(𝑠)(𝑞) = −𝑝𝑟−𝑞𝑠 Specific behaviours  uses identity  at least two correct trig values  correct expression Solutions (i) 𝑠 (ii) 𝑠 𝑟 (iii) −𝑝 (iv) 𝑝 Specific behaviours  each correct response",
