    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-112-8 Question 12 (6 marks) (a) Determine the equation of the axis of symmetry for the graph of 𝑦= 4𝑥2 −20𝑥−51. (2 marks) (b) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 27 passes through the points (3, 6) and (−4, −57). Determine the values of the constants 𝑎 and 𝑏. (4 marks) Solution 6 = (3)2𝑎+ 3𝑏+ 27 6 = 9𝑎+ 3𝑏+ 27 −57 = (−4)2𝑎−4𝑏+ 27 −57 = 16𝑎−4𝑏+ 27 Solve simultaneously using CAS 𝑎= −4, 𝑏= 5 Specific behaviours  substitutes first point  substitutes second point  solves for 𝑎  solves for 𝑏 Solution 𝑥= −𝑏 2𝑎= −−20 2 × 4 = 2.5 𝑥= 2.5 Specific behaviours  indicates use of formula  correct equation",
