    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-112-6 Question 17 (9 marks) The wind speed at a weather station, 𝑣 metres per second, 𝑡 hours after recording began, can be modelled by the function 𝑣= 10 + 5.7𝑡−0.7𝑡2 + 0.02𝑡3, 0 ≤𝑡≤24 (a) Calculate the wind speed when 𝑡= 3. (1 mark) (b) Sketch the graph of wind speed against time on the axes below. (4 marks) (c) During the 24-hour period, determine (i) the time at which the wind speed was least. (1 mark) (ii) the maximum wind speed. (1 mark) (iii) the length of time, in hours and minutes, that the wind speed was decreasing. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-112-8 Question 17 (9 marks) The wind speed at a weather station, 𝑣 metres per second, 𝑡 hours after recording began, can be modelled by the function 𝑣= 10 + 5.7𝑡−0.7𝑡2 + 0.02𝑡3, 0 ≤𝑡≤24 (a) Calculate the wind speed when 𝑡= 3. (1 mark) (b) Sketch the graph of wind speed against time on the axes below. (4 marks) (c) During the 24-hour period, determine (i) the time at which the wind speed was least. (1 mark) (ii) the maximum wind speed. (1 mark) (iii) the length of time, in hours and minutes, that the wind speed was decreasing. (2 marks) Solution 𝑣(3) = 21.34 m/s Specific behaviours  value Solution 𝑡= 18.1 h Specific behaviours  value (at least 1dp) Solution 𝑣𝑀𝐼𝑁= 23.5 m/s Specific behaviours  value (at least 1 dp) Solution 18.078 −5.255 = 12.823 = 12 h 49 min Specific behaviours  interval in hours  interval in hours and minutes Solution See graph Specific behaviours  (0, 10) and (24, 20)  min at ≈(18, 2.5)  max at ≈(5, 23.5)  reasonable curve",
