    "questionText": "METHODS UNIT 1 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-112-6 Question 20 (9 marks) (a) Use your calculator to (i) determine the exact value of cos 36°. (1 mark) (ii) determine the exact value of sin 105°. (1 mark) (iii) solve cos(𝑥+ 60°) = sin 𝑥 for −270° ≤𝑥≤270°. (2 marks) (b) Using suitable exact values of acute angles and an angle sum and difference identity, justify your above value of sin105°. (5 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-112-8 Question 20 (9 marks) (a) Use your calculator to (i) determine the exact value of cos 36°. (1 mark) (ii) determine the exact value of sin 105°. (1 mark) (iii) solve cos(𝑥+ 60°) = sin 𝑥 for −270° ≤𝑥≤270°. (2 marks) (b) Using suitable exact values of acute angles and an angle sum and difference identity, justify your above value of sin105°. (5 marks) Solution sin(105) = sin(45 + 60) = sin45 cos 60 + cos45 sin60 = √2 2 × 1 2 + √2 2 × √3 2 = √2(1 + √3) 4 Specific behaviours  chooses suitable pair of angles  chooses correct identity  first pair of exact values  second pair of exact values  simplifies to match previous answer Solution (i) √5 + 1 4 (ii) √2(√3 + 1) 4 Specific behaviours  each exact value Solution 𝑥= −165°, 𝑥= 15°, 𝑥= 195° Specific behaviours  two correct solutions  all three correct NB Graphical or numerical solve quickest - use of exact solve slow",
