    "questionText": "Applecross SHS Semester 1, 2019 Section 2 Mathematics Methods Unit 1&2 4 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS SECTION AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF. Question 10 (8 marks) (a) The variables 𝐶 and 𝑥 are directly proportional and when 𝑥= 5, 𝐶= 60. (i) Determine an equation for the relationship between 𝐶 and 𝑥. (2 marks) (ii) State the value of 𝐶 when 𝑥= 15. (1 mark) (b) The time, 𝑡 minutes, that a car takes to travel one kilometre at a constant speed of 𝑠 kmh-1 is given by the formula = 𝑘 𝑠 . (i) Determine the value of the constant 𝑘, given that when 𝑠= 40, 𝑡= 90. (1 mark) (ii) Determine the value of 𝑡 when 𝑠= 30. (1 mark) (iii) On the axes below, draw a graph to show how 𝑠 varies with 𝑡. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN002-132-4 Question 10 (8 marks) (a) The variables 𝐶 and 𝑥 are directly proportional and when 𝑥= 5, 𝐶= 60. (i) Determine an equation for the relationship between 𝐶 and 𝑥. (2 marks) (ii) State the value of 𝐶 when 𝑥= 15. (1 mark) (b) The time, 𝑡 minutes, that a car takes to travel one kilometre at a constant speed of 𝑠 kmh-1 is given by the formula = 𝑘 𝑠 . (i) Determine the value of the constant 𝑘, given that when 𝑠= 40, 𝑡= 90. (1 mark) (ii) Determine the value of 𝑡 when 𝑠= 30. (1 mark) (iii) On the axes below, draw a graph to show how 𝑠 varies with 𝑡. (3 marks) Solution 𝐶= 𝑚𝑥, 𝑚= 60 5 = 12 ⇒𝐶= 12𝑥 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates use of line through origin ✓ correct relationship Solution 𝐶= 12(15) = 180 Specific behaviours ✓ correct value Solution 𝑡= 3600 ÷ 30 = 120 Specific behaviours ✓ correct value Solution 90 = 𝑘 40 ⇒𝑘= 3600 Specific behaviours ✓ correct value Solution See graph. Key points: (20, 180), (30, 120), (40, 90), (60, 60), (90, 40), (120, 30) Specific behaviours ✓ plots at least 3 key points ✓ plots all key points ✓ smooth curve",
