    "questionText": "Applecross SHS Semester 1, 2019 Section 2 Mathematics Methods Unit 1&2 6 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS SECTION AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF. Question 12 (8 marks) (a) A function is given by 3 ( ) 2 1 f x x = + + . (i) State the natural domain and corresponding range of f . (2 marks) (ii) The graph of ( ) f x is dilated vertically by a scale factor of 2. Determine the coordinates of the y -axis intercept. (2 marks) (iii) The graph of ( ) f x is translated 3 units to the right. Determine the equation of the translated function. (1 mark) (b) The graph of the cubic function 𝑦= 𝑔(𝑥) is shown below. Determine 𝑔(10). (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN002-132-4 Question 12 (8 marks) (a) A function is given by 3 ( ) 2 1 f x x = + + . (i) State the natural domain and corresponding range of f . (2 marks) (ii) The graph of ( ) f x is dilated vertically by a scale factor of 2. Determine the coordinates of the y -axis intercept. (2 marks) (iii) The graph of ( ) f x is translated 3 units to the right. Determine the equation of the translated function. (1 mark) (b) The graph of the cubic function 𝑦= 𝑔(𝑥) is shown below. Determine 𝑔(10). (3 marks) Solution Domain: {𝑥: 𝑥 ≠−1} Range: {𝑦: ≠2} Specific behaviours ✓ Domain ✓ Range Solution Y intercept is (0, 10) Specific behaviours ✓ ✓ correct coordinates Solution (𝑥−3) 𝑟𝑒𝑝𝑙𝑎𝑐𝑒𝑠 𝑥 𝑖𝑛 𝑓(𝑥) 𝑓(𝑥−3) = 3 𝑥−2 + 2 Specific behaviours ✓ writes correct equation Solution 𝑔(𝑥) = 𝑎(𝑥+ 1)(𝑥−2)(𝑥−5) 20 = 𝑎(1)(−2)(−5) ⇒𝑎= 2 𝑔(10) = 2(11)(8)(5) = 880 Specific behaviours ✓ cubic in factored form ✓ correct value of 𝑎 ✓ required value",
