    "calculator": "Unlabelled",
    "questionText": "Applecross SHS Semester 1, 2019 Section 2 Mathematics Methods Unit 1&2 7 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS SECTION AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF. Question 13 (8 marks) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) is shown below where 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑐 𝑎−𝑥 . (a) State the value of the constant 𝑎 and the value of the constant 𝑐. (3 marks) (b) The hyperbola shown above has two asymptotes. State their equations. (2 marks) (c) Describe the transformation required to transform the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) to obtain the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥−3) and state the domain and range of the transformed function. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN002-132-4 Question 13 (8 marks) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) is shown below where 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑐 𝑎−𝑥 . (a) State the value of the constant 𝑎 and the value of the constant 𝑐. (3 marks) (b) The hyperbola shown above has two asymptotes. State their equations. (2 marks) (c) Describe the transformation required to transform the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) to obtain the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥−3) and state the domain and range of the transformed function.(3 marks) Solution 𝑥= 4, 𝑦= 0 Specific behaviours ✓ vertical asymptote ✓ horizontal asymptote Solution Translate the graph 3 unit to the right. Domain: 𝑥≠7 Range: 𝑦≠0 Specific behaviours ✓ transformation ✓ domain ✓ range Solution 𝑎= 4 Using (3, 3) ⇒3 = 𝑐÷ 1 ⇒𝑐= 3 Specific behaviours ✓ value of 𝑎 ✓ uses point on curve ✓ value of 𝑐",
