    "questionText": "Applecross SHS Semester 1, 2019 Section 2 Mathematics Methods Unit 1&2 8 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS SECTION AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF. Question 14 (8 marks) (a) Convert, giving an exact answer (i) 16° to radians. (1 mark) (ii) 0.4 radians to degrees. (1 mark) (b) Calculate, to the nearest degree, the acute angle between the line 𝑦= 1.5𝑥−4 and the line 𝑦= −0.5𝑥+ 4. (3 marks) (c) The sides adjacent to the right-angle in a right triangle have lengths 65 cm and 72 cm. If the smallest angle in the triangle is 𝛼, determine an exact value for (i) tan 𝛼. (1 mark) (ii) sin(90° −𝛼). (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNIT 1 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN002-132-4 Question 14 (8 marks) (a) Convert, giving an exact answer (i) 16° to radians. (1 mark) (ii) 0.4 radians to degrees. (1 mark) (b) Calculate, to the nearest degree, the acute angle between the line 𝑦= 1.5𝑥−4 and the line 𝑦= −0.5𝑥+ 4. (3 marks) (c) The sides adjacent to the right-angle in a right triangle have lengths 65 cm and 72 cm. If the smallest angle in the triangle is 𝛼, determine an exact value for (i) tan 𝛼. (1 mark) (ii) sin(90° −𝛼). (2 marks) Solution 4𝜋 45 Specific behaviours ✓ exact value Solution 72 𝜋 Specific behaviours ✓ exact value Solution 𝜃1 = tan−1 1.5 = 56.3 𝜃2 = tan−1(−0.5) = −26.6 𝜃2 −𝜃1 = 83° 𝑁𝑜𝑡 97° Specific behaviours ✓ indicates use of tan−1 𝑚 ✓ one correct angle with 𝑥-axis ✓ correct angle between lines Solution tan 𝛼= 65 72 Specific behaviours ✓ correct ratio Solution √652 + 722 = 97 sin(90° −𝛼) = 72 97 Specific behaviours ✓ calculates length of hypotenuse ✓ correct ratio for small",
