    "questionText": "Applecross SHS Semester 1, 2019 Section 2 Mathematics Methods Unit 1&2 11 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS SECTION AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF. Question 17 (7 marks) In shape 𝑂𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷 below, ∠𝐴𝑂𝐵= 126° and 𝐴𝐶, 𝐵𝐷 are diameters of the circle with centre 𝑂 and radius 35 cm. (a) Calculate the perimeter of 𝑂𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. (4 marks) (b) Calculate the area of 𝑂𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN002-132-4 Question 17 (7 marks) In shape 𝑂𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷 below, ∠𝐴𝑂𝐵= 126° and 𝐴𝐶, 𝐵𝐷 are diameters of the circle with centre 𝑂 and radius 35 cm. (a) Calculate the perimeter of 𝑂𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. (4 marks) (b) Calculate the area of 𝑂𝐴𝐵𝐶𝐷. (3 marks) Solution 126° = 7𝜋 10 , 𝜋−7𝜋 10 = 3𝜋 10 = 54° 𝐴𝐵, 𝐷𝐶: 35 × 7𝜋 10 = 49𝜋 2 ≈76.97 𝐵𝐶2 = 352 + 352 −2(35)(35) cos 54 𝐵𝐶≈31.78 𝑃𝑇𝑂𝑇𝐴𝐿= 2(35) + 2(76.97) + 31.78 ≈256 cm Specific behaviours ✓ indicates length of arc 𝐴𝐵 ✓ indicates use of cosine rule for 𝐵𝐶 ✓ correct length 𝐵𝐶 ✓ correct total perimeter Solution 𝐴𝑂𝐵+ 𝐷𝑂𝐶: 2 × 1 2 × 352 × 7𝜋 10 = 1715𝜋 2 ≈2694 𝐵𝑂𝐶: 1 2 (35)(35) sin54 ≈496 𝐴𝑇𝑂𝑇𝐴𝐿= 2694 + 496 = 3 190 cm2 Specific behaviours ✓ sector area 𝐴𝑂𝐵 ✓ triangle area 𝐵𝑂𝐶 ✓ correct total area",
    "questionImage": "generated/resource-previews/docx-pdf-cache-year-11-mathematics-methods-section-2-semeste-p011-question-b315fb9ff1.jpg",
