    "calculator": "Unlabelled",
    "questionText": "Applecross SHS Semester 1, 2019 Section 2 Mathematics Methods Unit 1&2 13 See next page DO NOT WRITE IN THIS SECTION AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF. Question 19 (8 marks) (a) The equation of the axis of symmetry for the graph of 𝑦= 3𝑥2 + 6𝑥+ 7 is 𝑥= 𝑘. Determine the value of 𝑘, using a method that does not refer to the graph of the parabola. (2 marks) (b) A parabola with equation 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 𝑐 has a turning point at (6, −5) and passes through the point (−2, −37). Determine the value of 𝑎, the value of 𝑏 and the value of 𝑐. (3 marks) (c) Determine the value of the discriminant for the quadratic equation 16𝑥2 −24𝑥+ 9 = 0 and use it to explain how many solutions the equation (𝑥+ 1)(16𝑥2 −24𝑥+ 9) = 0 will have. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNIT 1 See next page SN002-132-4 Question 19 (8 marks) (a) The equation of the axis of symmetry for the graph of 𝑦= 3𝑥2 + 6𝑥+ 7 is 𝑥= 𝑘. Determine the value of 𝑘, using a method that does not refer to the graph of the parabola. (2 marks) (b) A parabola with equation 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 𝑐 has a turning point at (6, −5) and passes through the point (−2, −37). Determine the value of 𝑎, the value of 𝑏 and the value of 𝑐. (3 marks) (c) Determine the value of the discriminant for the quadratic equation 16𝑥2 −24𝑥+ 9 = 0 and use it to explain how many solutions the equation (𝑥+ 1)(16𝑥2 −24𝑥+ 9) = 0 will have. (3 marks) Solution 𝑥= − 6 2 × 3 = −1 𝑘= −1 𝑦= 3(𝑥+ 1)2 + 𝑐 ∴𝑘= −1 Specific behaviours ✓ uses 𝑥= −𝑏÷ (2𝑎) or partially completes the square ✓ value of 𝑘 Solution 𝑑= (−24)2 −4(16)(9) = 0 When 𝑑= 0, quadratic will have one solution. Hence equation will have two solutions - one from linear factor and one from quadratic factor. Specific behaviours ✓ value of discriminant ✓ uses discriminant to say quadratic will have one solution ✓ explains why equation has two solutions Solution 𝑦= 𝑎(𝑥−6)2 −5 −37 = 𝑎(−2 −6)2 −5 ⇒𝑎= −0.5 𝑦= −0.5(𝑥−6)2 −5 = −0.5𝑥2 + 6𝑥−23 𝑎= −0.5, 𝑏= ",
