    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page Question 11 (6 marks) A mobile phone retailer classified recent sales of 375 phones by the age of customer and if the phone was bought outright or on a plan. A summary of the data is shown in the table below. (a) Determine the values of 𝑝, 𝑞 and 𝑟 shown in the table. (3 marks) (b) A recent sale is selected at random from those recorded above. Event 𝐴 occurs if the customer was aged under 30 and event 𝐵 occurs if the phone was bought outright. Determine the following probabilities: (i) 𝑃(𝐴∪𝐵). (1 mark) (ii) 𝑃(𝐴̅ |𝐵V ). (2 marks) Aged under 30 Aged 30 or over Total Bought outright 𝑝 94 𝑟 Bought on a plan 115 𝑞 224 Total 375 Solution 𝑃(𝐴∪𝐵) = 375 −109 375 = 266 375 (= 0.7093V) Specific behaviours ü correct probability Solution 𝑞= 224 −115 = 109 𝑟= 375 −224 = 151 𝑝= 151 −94 = 57 Specific behaviours ü each correct value Solution 𝑃(𝐴̅ |𝐵V ) = 109 224 (≈0.487) Specific behaviours ü numerator ü denominator",
