    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page Question 18 (6 marks) A small body moves in a straight line so that its displacement 𝑥 from a fixed point 𝑂 after 𝑡 seconds is given by 𝑥= 𝑎𝑡< + 𝑏𝑡+ 𝑐 metres. The position-time graph of the body is shown below. (a) Determine the values of the constants 𝑎, 𝑏 and 𝑐. (3 marks) (b) Determine the displacement of the body when its velocity is 24 ms-1. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page Question 18 (6 marks) A small body moves in a straight line so that its displacement 𝑥 from a fixed point 𝑂 after 𝑡 seconds is given by 𝑥= 𝑎𝑡D + 𝑏𝑡+ 𝑐 metres. The position-time graph of the body is shown below. (a) Determine the values of the constants 𝑎, 𝑏 and 𝑐. (3 marks) (b) Determine the displacement of the body when its velocity is 24 ms-1. (3 marks) Solution 𝑣= 4𝑡−20 4𝑡−20 = 24 ⇒𝑡= 11 𝑥(11) = 2(11 −2)(11 −8) = 54 m Specific behaviours ü equation for velocity ü solves for time ü substitutes for displacement Solution 𝑥= 𝑎(𝑡−2)(𝑡−8) 32 = 𝑎(−2)(−8) ⇒𝑎= 2 𝑥= 2(𝑡D −10𝑡+ 16) = 2𝑡D −20𝑡+ 32 𝑎= 2, 𝑏= −20, 𝑐= 32 Specific behaviours ü writes equation using roots ü uses 𝑦-intercept to find 𝑎 ü expands and states three values",
