    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page Question 19 (8 marks) The height, ℎ metres, above level ground of a seat on a steadily rotating giant viewing wheel at the Perth Show, 𝑡 seconds after observations began was given by ℎ= 5.5 sine𝜋𝑡 15f + 7, 𝑡≥0. (a) Draw the graph of the height of the seat against time on the axes below. (4 marks) (b) How long did the Ferris wheel take to complete one revolution? (1 mark) (c) At what time, when the seat was rising, did it first reach a height of 5 metres? (1 mark) (d) Determine the change in height of the seat between 𝑡= 95 and 𝑡= 96, giving your answer rounded to the nearest cm. (2 marks)",
