    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions SN018-142-1 Question 8 (7 marks) An arithmetic sequence has a recursive definition given by 𝑇𝑇𝑛𝑛+1 = 𝑇𝑇𝑛𝑛+ 𝑑𝑑, 𝑇𝑇1 = 𝑎𝑎. It has fourth term of 50 and tenth term of 20. (a) Determine the value of the constant 𝑎𝑎 and the constant 𝑑𝑑. (2 marks) (b) Determine 𝑇𝑇2019. (2 marks) (c) The sum of the first 𝑚𝑚 terms of the sequence is 350. Determine the value(s) of the integer constant 𝑚𝑚. (3 marks) © 2019 WA Exam Papers. Christ Church Grammar School has a non-exclusive licence to copy and communicate this document for non-commercial, educational use within the school. No other copying, communication or use is permitted without the express written permission of WA Exam Papers. SN018-142-1. Mathematics Department Year 11 Mathematics Methods Semester 2 Examination, 2019 Question/Answer booklet MATHEMATICS METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 Section Two: Calculator-assumed Student name: _____________________________________ Time allowed for this section Reading time before commencing work: ten minutes Working time: one hundred minutes Materials required/recommended for this section To be provided by the supervisor This Question/Answer booklet Formula sheet (retained from Section One) To be provided by the candidate Standard items: pens (blue/black preferred), pencils (including coloured), sharpener, correction fluid/tape, eraser, ruler, highlighters Special items: drawing instruments, templates, notes on two unfolded sheets of A4 paper, and up to three calculators approved for use in this examination Important note to candidates No other items may be taken into the examination room. It is your responsibility to ensure that you do not have any unauthorised material. If you have any unauthorised material with you, hand it to the supervisor before reading any further. Fix student label here",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 10 CALCULATOR-FREE End of questions SN018-142-3 Question 8 (7 marks) An arithmetic sequence has a recursive definition given by 𝑇𝑇𝑛𝑛+1 = 𝑇𝑇𝑛𝑛+ 𝑑𝑑, 𝑇𝑇1 = 𝑎𝑎. It has fourth term of 50 and tenth term of 20. (a) Determine the value of the constant 𝑎𝑎 and the constant 𝑑𝑑. (2 marks) (b) Determine 𝑇𝑇2019. (2 marks) (c) The sum of the first 𝑚𝑚 terms of the sequence is 350. Determine the value(s) of the integer constant 𝑚𝑚. (3 marks) Solution (10 −4)𝑑𝑑= 20 −50 6𝑑𝑑= −30 𝑑𝑑= −5 𝑎𝑎= 50 −3(−5) = 65 Specific behaviours  value of 𝑑𝑑  value of 𝑎𝑎 Solution 350 = 𝑚𝑚 2 ൫2(65) + (𝑚𝑚−1)(−5)൯ 700 = 𝑚𝑚(130 −5𝑚𝑚+ 5) 5𝑚𝑚2 −135𝑚𝑚+ 700 = 0 𝑚𝑚2 −27𝑚𝑚+ 140 = 0 (𝑚𝑚−7)(𝑚𝑚−20) = 0 𝑚𝑚= 7, 𝑚𝑚= 20 Specific behaviours  substitutes into sum formula  simplifies and equates quadratic to zero  both correct solutions Solution 𝑇𝑇𝑛𝑛= 65 + (𝑛𝑛−1)(−5) 𝑇𝑇301 = 65 + 2018(−5) = −10 025 Specific behaviours  indicates rule for general term  correct value",
