    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 3 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN018-142-2 Section Two: Calculator-assumed 65% (98 Marks) This section has thirteen (13) questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Supplementary pages for planning/continuing your answers to questions are provided at the end of this Question/Answer booklet. If you use these pages to continue an answer, indicate at the original answer where the answer is continued, i.e. give the page number. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 9 (6 marks) (a) Convert 108° to an exact radian measure. (1 mark) (b) A segment of a circle of radius 28 cm is shown below, where 𝜃𝜃= 108°. (i) Determine the area of the segment. (2 marks) (ii) Determine the perimeter of the segment. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 3 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN018-142-4 Section Two: Calculator-assumed 65% (98 Marks) This section has thirteen (13) questions. Answer all questions. Write your answers in the spaces provided. Working time: 100 minutes. Question 9 (6 marks) (a) Convert 108° to an exact radian measure. (1 mark) (b) A segment of a circle of radius 28 cm is shown below, where 𝜃𝜃= 108°. (i) Determine the area of the segment. (2 marks) (ii) Determine the perimeter of the segment. (3 marks) Solution 108 × 𝜋𝜋 180 = 3𝜋𝜋 5 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution Arc length is 𝐿𝐿 and chord length is 𝐶𝐶. 𝐿𝐿= 28 × 3𝜋𝜋 5 ≈52.78 𝐶𝐶2 = 282 + 282 −2(28)(28) cos 108° or 𝐶𝐶= 2𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟( 𝜃𝜃 2) 𝐶𝐶≈45.3 𝑃𝑃≈52.78 + 45.3 ≈98.08 cm Alternatively: 𝐶𝐶= 2𝑅𝑅𝑅𝑅𝑅𝑅𝑅𝑅 𝜃𝜃 2 = 45.3 Specific behaviours  arc length  uses cosine rule (or 𝐶𝐶= 2𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟𝑟( 𝜃𝜃 2)) to calculate chord length  correct perimeter Solution 𝐴𝐴= 1 2 (28)2 ൬3𝜋𝜋 5 −sin 3𝜋𝜋 5 ൰ ≈366.09 cm2 Specific behaviours  indicates correct use of formula  correct area",
