    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN018-142-2 Question 12 (10 marks) When a manufacturer makes 𝑥𝑥 litres of a chemical using process 𝑋𝑋, the cost in dollars per litre 𝐶𝐶(𝑥𝑥) varies according to the rule 𝐶𝐶(𝑥𝑥) = 240 𝑥𝑥+ 15 , 5 ≤𝑥𝑥≤45. (a) Determine (i) the cost per litre when 35 L is made. (1 mark) (ii) the total cost of making 17 L of the chemical. (2 marks) (b) Graph the cost per litre over the given domain on the axes below. (3 marks) CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN018-142-2 (c) State the range of 𝐶𝐶(𝑥𝑥). (1 mark) (d) When the manufacturer uses process 𝑍𝑍, the cost in dollars per litre 𝐾𝐾(𝑥𝑥) is modelled by 𝐾𝐾(𝑥𝑥) = 10.5 −𝑥𝑥 6 , 5 ≤𝑥𝑥≤45. (i) Add this function 𝐾𝐾(𝑥𝑥) to the graph. (1 mark) (ii) determine the production quantities for which process 𝑋𝑋 is cheaper than process 𝑍𝑍. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN018-142-4 Question 12 (10 marks) When a manufacturer makes 𝑥𝑥 litres of a chemical using process 𝑋𝑋, the cost in dollars per litre 𝐶𝐶(𝑥𝑥) varies according to the rule 𝐶𝐶(𝑥𝑥) = 240 𝑥𝑥+ 15 , 5 ≤𝑥𝑥≤45. (a) Determine (i) the cost per litre when 35 L is made. (1 mark) (ii) the total cost of making 17 L of the chemical. (2 marks) (b) Graph the cost per litre over the given domain on the axes below. (3 marks) Solution (b) See graph Specific behaviours  LH endpoint (5, 12)  RH endpoint (45, 4)  smooth curve through (15, 8) and (25,6) Solution 𝐶𝐶(35) = 4.8 $/L Specific behaviours  correct cost per litre Solution 𝐶𝐶(17) = 7.5 𝑇𝑇= 7.5 × 17 = $127.50 Specific behaviours  cost per litre  correct total cost",
