    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN018-142-2 Question 13 (5 marks) A geometric sequence has a second term of −8.4 and a sum to infinity of 15. Determine the sum of the first 4 terms of the sequence.",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN018-142-4 Question 13 (5 marks) A geometric sequence has a second term of −8.4 and a sum to infinity of 15. Determine the sum of the first 4 terms of the sequence. Solution 𝑎𝑎𝑎𝑎= −8.4, 𝑎𝑎 1 −𝑟𝑟= 15 Solving simultaneously gives 𝑎𝑎= 21, 𝑟𝑟= −0.4 (ignore 𝑟𝑟= 1.4 since |𝑟𝑟| < 1 for sum to infinity) 𝑆𝑆4 = 21(1 −(−0.4)4) 1 −(−0.4) = 1827 125 = 14.616 Specific behaviours  equation using 𝑇𝑇2  equation using 𝑆𝑆∞  solves for 𝑎𝑎 and 𝑟𝑟  discards invalid solution  calculates 𝑆𝑆4",
