    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN018-142-2 Question 15 (7 marks) The amount of water in a tank, 𝑊𝑊 litres, varies with time 𝑡𝑡, in minutes, and can be modelled by the equation 𝑊𝑊= 200 −185(1.2)−𝑡𝑡, 𝑡𝑡≥0. (a) Determine amount of water in the tank (i) initially. (1 mark) (ii) after 15 minutes. (1 mark) (b) Graph 𝑊𝑊 against 𝑡𝑡 for 0 ≤𝑡𝑡≤45 on the axes below. (3 marks) (c) Over time, the amount of water in the tank approaches 𝑣𝑣 litres. State the value of 𝑣𝑣 and determine the time at which the amount of water in the tank reaches 99% of this value. (2 marks)",
