    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN018-142-2 Question 16 (7 marks) When a patient takes a painkilling drug 𝐴𝐴, the probability that they experience some side effects is known to be 0.1. (a) A doctor prescribes drug 𝐴𝐴 to two unrelated patients. Determine the probability that (i) neither patient experiences some side effects. (1 mark) (ii) one patient experiences some side effects and the other does not. (2 marks) Other painkilling drugs are available. Of those who take drug 𝐴𝐴, 88% of patients who suffer some side effects will switch to another drug whereas no patient who has no side effects will switch. (b) The doctor prescribes drug 𝐴𝐴 to a patient. Determine the probability that the patient does not switch to another drug. (2 marks) (c) The doctor prescribes drug 𝐴𝐴 to three unrelated patients. Determine the probability that at least one of these patients switch to another drug. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN018-142-4 Question 16 (7 marks) When a patient takes a painkilling drug 𝐴𝐴, the probability that they experience some side effects is known to be 0.1. (a) A doctor prescribes drug 𝐴𝐴 to two unrelated patients. Determine the probability that (i) neither patient experiences some side effects. (1 mark) (ii) one patient experiences some side effects and the other does not. (2 marks) Other painkilling drugs are available. Of those who take drug 𝐴𝐴, 88% of patients who suffer some side effects will switch to another drug whereas no patient who has no side effects will switch. (b) The doctor prescribes drug 𝐴𝐴 to a patient. Determine the probability that the patient does not switch to another drug. (2 marks) (c) The doctor prescribes drug 𝐴𝐴 to three unrelated patients. Determine the probability that at least one of these patients switch to another drug. (2 marks) Solution 𝑃𝑃= (0.9)2 = 0.81 Specific behaviours  correct probability Solution 𝑃𝑃= 0.1 × 0.9 × 2 = 0.18 Specific behaviours  calculates 𝑝𝑝(1 −𝑝𝑝)  doubles to obtain correct probability Solution 𝑃𝑃= 0.9 + 0.1 × 0.12 = 0.9 + 0.012 = 0.912 Specific behaviours  probabilit",
