    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN018-142-2 Question 17 (12 marks) The function 𝑓𝑓 is defined by 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = 𝑥𝑥3 + 𝑎𝑎𝑥𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑏𝑏𝑏+ 𝑐𝑐, where 𝑎𝑎, 𝑏𝑏 and 𝑐𝑐 are constants. The graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) has the following features: • passes through (0, −27) and (3, 0) • has a local maximum at (−3, 0) (a) Determine the value of 𝑎𝑎, the value of 𝑏𝑏 and the value of 𝑐𝑐. (3 marks) (b) Sketch the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) on the axes below. (3 marks) CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN018-142-2 (c) Use a calculus method to determine the exact coordinates of the local minimum of the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥). (3 marks) (d) Determine the coordinates of the point where the tangent to 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) at (0, −27) intersects the curve 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥), other than at the point of tangency. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN018-142-4 Question 17 (12 marks) The function 𝑓𝑓 is defined by 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = 𝑥𝑥3 + 𝑎𝑎𝑥𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑏𝑏𝑏+ 𝑐𝑐, where 𝑎𝑎, 𝑏𝑏 and 𝑐𝑐 are constants. The graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) has the following features: • passes through (0, −27) and (3, 0) • has a local maximum at (−3, 0) (a) Determine the value of 𝑎𝑎, the value of 𝑏𝑏 and the value of 𝑐𝑐. (3 marks) Solution 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = (𝑥𝑥−3)(𝑥𝑥+ 3)2 = 𝑥𝑥3 + 3𝑥𝑥2 −9𝑥𝑥−27 𝑎𝑎= 3, 𝑏𝑏= −9, 𝑐𝑐= −27 Specific behaviours  writes in factored form  expands  states all three values (b) Sketch the graph of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) on the axes below. (3 marks) Solution See graph Specific behaviours  local maximum  y-intercept and root  smooth curve",
