    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN018-142-2 Question 19 (8 marks) Two events 𝐴𝐴 and 𝐵𝐵 are such that 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴∩𝐵𝐵ത) = 𝑥𝑥, 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴) = 0.2 and 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴̅ ∩𝐵𝐵) = 0.6. (a) Determine 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴∩𝐵𝐵) when 𝑥𝑥= 0.12. (2 marks) (b) Determine an expression for 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴∩𝐵𝐵) in terms of 𝑥𝑥. (1 mark) (c) Determine the value of 𝑥𝑥 when (i) 𝐴𝐴 and 𝐵𝐵 are mutually exclusive. (1 mark) (ii) 𝐴𝐴 and 𝐵𝐵 are independent. (2 marks) (iii) 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴|𝐵𝐵) = 0.04. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN018-142-4 Question 19 (8 marks) Two events 𝐴𝐴 and 𝐵𝐵 are such that 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴∩𝐵𝐵ത) = 𝑥𝑥, 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴) = 0.2 and 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴̅ ∩𝐵𝐵) = 0.6. (a) Determine 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴∩𝐵𝐵) when 𝑥𝑥= 0.12. (2 marks) (b) Determine an expression for 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴∩𝐵𝐵) in terms of 𝑥𝑥. (1 mark) (c) Determine the value of 𝑥𝑥 when (i) 𝐴𝐴 and 𝐵𝐵 are mutually exclusive. (1 mark) (ii) 𝐴𝐴 and 𝐵𝐵 are independent. (2 marks) (iii) 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴|𝐵𝐵) = 0.04. (2 marks) Solution 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴∩𝐵𝐵) = 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴) −𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴∩𝐵𝐵ത) = 0.2 −0.12 = 0.08 Specific behaviours  use of Venn diagram or other method  correct probability Solution 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴∩𝐵𝐵) = 0.2 −𝑥𝑥 Specific behaviours  correct expression Solution 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴∩𝐵𝐵) = 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴) × 𝑃𝑃(𝐵𝐵) 0.2 −𝑥𝑥= 0.2 × (0.6 + 0.2 −𝑥𝑥) 𝑥𝑥= 0.05 Specific behaviours  uses rule for independence  correct value Solution 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴∩𝐵𝐵) = 0.2 −𝑥𝑥= 0 ⇒𝑥𝑥= 0.2 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴|𝐵𝐵) = 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴∩𝐵𝐵) 𝑃𝑃(𝐵𝐵) 0.04 = 0.2 −𝑥𝑥 0.6 + 0.2 −𝑥𝑥 𝑥𝑥= 0.175 Specific behaviours  uses conditional probability rule  correct value",
