    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN018-142-2 Question 20 (8 marks) A fair six-sided dice numbered 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 is thrown 𝑛𝑛 times until it lands on a 6. (a) Show that the probability that 𝑛𝑛= 3 is 25 216 . (1 mark) (b) Determine the probability that 𝑛𝑛= 5. (1 mark) (c) Write an expression in terms of 𝑛𝑛 for the probability that the first 6 is thrown on the 𝑛𝑛th throw and explain why the probabilities form a geometric sequence. (2 marks) (d) Determine the probability that the first 6 is thrown in 12 or less attempts. (2 marks) (e) The probability that the first 6 is thrown in 𝑘𝑘 or less attempts must be at least 99%. Determine the least value of integer 𝑘𝑘. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN018-142-4 Question 20 (8 marks) A fair six-sided dice numbered 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6 is thrown 𝑛𝑛 times until it lands on a 6. (a) Show that the probability that 𝑛𝑛= 3 is 25 216 . (1 mark) (b) Determine the probability that 𝑛𝑛= 5. (1 mark) (c) Write an expression in terms of 𝑛𝑛 for the probability that the first 6 is thrown on the 𝑛𝑛th throw and explain why the probabilities form a geometric sequence. (2 marks) (d) Determine the probability that the first 6 is thrown in 12 or less attempts. (2 marks) (e) The probability that the first 6 is thrown in 𝑘𝑘 or less attempts must be at least 99%. Determine the least value of integer 𝑘𝑘. (2 marks) Solution 𝑃𝑃(𝑛𝑛= 3) = 5 6 × 5 6 × 1 6 = 25 216 Specific behaviours  shows product of three fractions Solution 0.99 = 1 6 ൬1 −ቀ5 6ቁ 𝑛𝑛 ൰ 1 −5 6 ⇒𝑛𝑛= 25.3 𝑘𝑘= 26 Specific behaviours  solves for 𝑛𝑛  correct value of 𝑘𝑘 Solution 𝑃𝑃(𝑛𝑛= 5) = ൬5 6൰ 4 × 1 6 = 625 7776 ≈0.0804 Specific behaviours  correct probability Solution 𝑃𝑃= 1 6 ൬5 6൰ 𝑛𝑛−1 The expression takes the form of the 𝑛𝑛th term of a GP - 𝑎𝑎(𝑟𝑟)𝑛𝑛−1 or There exists a common ratio ( 5 6). Specific behaviours  correct expression  c",
