    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 End of questions SN018-142-2 Question 21 (6 marks) The graphs of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) and 𝑦𝑦= 𝑔𝑔(𝑥𝑥) are shown below where 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = 1 + 4𝑥𝑥−2𝑥𝑥2 and 𝑔𝑔(𝑥𝑥) = 2𝑥𝑥+ 𝑘𝑘. Determine the value(s) of the constant 𝑘𝑘 so that the equation 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = 𝑔𝑔(𝑥𝑥) has (a) one solution. (5 marks) (b) no solutions. (1 mark) © 2019 WA Exam Papers. Christ Church Grammar School has a non-exclusive licence to copy and communicate this document for non-commercial, educational use within the school. No other copying, communication or use is permitted without the express written permission of WA Exam Papers. SN018-142-2.",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 End of questions SN018-142-4 Question 21 (6 marks) The graphs of 𝑦𝑦= 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) and 𝑦𝑦= 𝑔𝑔(𝑥𝑥) are shown below where 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = 1 + 4𝑥𝑥−2𝑥𝑥2 and 𝑔𝑔(𝑥𝑥) = 2𝑥𝑥+ 𝑘𝑘. Determine the value(s) of the constant 𝑘𝑘 so that the equation 𝑓𝑓(𝑥𝑥) = 𝑔𝑔(𝑥𝑥) has (a) one solution. (5 marks) (b) no solutions. (1 mark) Solutions 𝑔𝑔 must be a tangent to 𝑓𝑓: 𝑓𝑓′(𝑥𝑥) = 4 −4𝑥𝑥 = 2 when 𝑥𝑥= 1 2 𝑦𝑦-coordinate of point of tangency: 𝑓𝑓൬1 2൰= 1 + 4 ൬1 2൰−2 ൬1 2൰ 2 = 5 2 Equation of tangent: 𝑦𝑦−5 2 = 2 ൬𝑥𝑥−1 2൰ 𝑦𝑦= 2𝑥𝑥+ 3 2 Hence 𝑘𝑘= 3 2 = 1.5 1 + 4𝑥𝑥−2𝑥𝑥2 = 2𝑥𝑥+ 𝑘𝑘 2𝑥𝑥2 −2𝑥𝑥+ (𝑘𝑘−1) = 0 For one solution, ∆= 0 𝑏𝑏2 −4𝑎𝑎𝑎𝑎= 0 4 −4(2)(𝑘𝑘−1) = 0 𝑘𝑘−1 = 0.5 ∴𝑘𝑘= 1.5 Specific behaviours  indicates tangent required  determines 𝑥𝑥-coordinate of point of tangency  determines 𝑦𝑦-coordinate of point of tangency  equation of tangent  states correct value of 𝑘𝑘  equates f(x) and g(x)  generates quadratic equation with RHS being 0  states discriminant = 0  sets up equation in k  solves for k Solution 𝑘𝑘> 1.5 ∆< 0 4 −8(𝑘𝑘−1) < 0 ∴𝑘𝑘> 1.5 Specific behaviours  correct inequality",
