    "topicLabel": "Topic 1.2 · Functions & Graphs",
    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN245-142-3 D O N O T W RI TE IN TH IS A R EA Question 12 (10 marks) When a manufacturer makes 𝑥 litres of a chemical using process 𝑋, the cost in dollars per litre 𝐶(𝑥) varies according to the rule 𝐶(𝑥) = 240 𝑥+ 15 , 5 ≤𝑥≤45. (a) Determine (i) the cost per litre when 35 L is made. (1 mark) (ii) the total cost of making 17 L of the chemical. (2 marks) (b) Graph the cost per litre over the given domain on the axes below. (3 marks) METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 8 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-142-3 D O N O T W RI TE IN TH IS A R EA (c) State the range of 𝐶(𝑥). (1 mark) When the manufacturer uses process 𝑍, the cost in dollars per litre 𝐾(𝑥) is modelled by 𝐾(𝑥) = 10.5 −𝑥 6 , 5 ≤𝑥≤45. (d) Add this function to the graph and hence, or otherwise, determine the production quantities for which process 𝑋 is cheaper than process 𝑍. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN245-142-4 Question 12 (10 marks) When a manufacturer makes 𝑥 litres of a chemical using process 𝑋, the cost in dollars per litre 𝐶(𝑥) varies according to the rule 𝐶(𝑥) = 240 𝑥+ 15 , 5 ≤𝑥≤45. (a) Determine (i) the cost per litre when 35 L is made. (1 mark) Solution 𝐶(35) = 4.8 $/𝐿 Specific behaviours ✔ correct cost per litre (ii) the total cost of making 17 L of the chemical. (2 marks) Solution 𝐶(17) = 7.5𝑇= 7.5 × 17 = $127.50 Specific behaviours ✔ cost per litre ✔ correct total cost (b) Graph the cost per litre over the given domain on the axes below. (3 marks) Solution (b) See graph Specific behaviours ✔ LH endpoint (5, 12) ✔ RH endpoint (45, 4) ✔ smooth curve through (15, 8) and (25,6)",
    "questionImage": "generated/resource-previews/docx-pdf-cache-kennedy-2019-yr11-meth-u12-s2-b1d62eaf40-p007-question-88f6694ec8.jpg",
