    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 9 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN245-142-3 D O N O T W RI TE IN TH IS A R EA Question 13 (7 marks) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) is shown below, where 𝑓(𝑥) = 3𝑥, together with the secant to the curve through the points 𝑃 and 𝑄. 𝑃 has coordinates (1, 3) and 𝑄 has coordinates (1 + ℎ, 𝑓(1 + ℎ)) where 0 < ℎ≤1. (a) Complete the second column in the table below, rounding values to 4 decimal places where necessary. (4 marks) ℎ 𝑓(1 + ℎ) −𝑓(1) ℎ 1 0.1 0.01 0.001 (b) Name the feature of the graph above that the values you calculated in part (a) represent. (1 mark) (c) Determine an estimate, correct to 3 decimal places, for the value that 𝑓(1 + ℎ) − 𝑓(1) ℎ approaches as ℎ becomes closer and closer to 0 and state what this value represents. (2 marks)",
