    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-142-3 D O N O T W RI TE IN TH IS A R EA Question 14 (5 marks) A geometric sequence has a second term of −2.5 and a sum to infinity of 8. Determine the sum of the first 3 terms of the sequence.",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-142-4 Question 14 (5 marks) A geometric sequence has a second term of −2.5 and a sum to infinity of 8. Determine the sum of the first 3 terms of the sequence. Solution 𝑎𝑟= −2.5, 𝑎 1 −𝑟= 8 Solving simultaneously gives 𝑎= 10, 𝑟= −0.25 (ignore 𝑟= 1.25 since |𝑟| < 1 for sum to infinity) 𝑆3 = 10 + (−2.5) + (−2.5 × −0.25) = 65 8 = 8.125 Specific behaviours ✔ equation using 𝑇2 ✔ equation using 𝑆∞ ✔ solves for 𝑎 and 𝑟 ✔ discards invalid solution ✔ calculates 𝑆3",
