    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-142-3 D O N O T W RI TE IN TH IS A R EA Question 17 (7 marks) The amount of water in a tank, 𝑊 litres, varies with time 𝑡, in minutes, and can be modelled by the equation 𝑊= 200 −185(1.2)−𝑡, 𝑡≥0. (a) Determine amount of water in the tank (i) initially. (1 mark) (ii) after 15 minutes. (1 mark) (b) Graph 𝑊 against 𝑡 for 0 ≤𝑡≤45 on the axes below. (3 marks) (c) Over time, the amount of water in the tank approaches 𝑣 litres. State the value of 𝑣 and determine the time at which the amount of water in the tank reaches 99% of this value. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 21 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN245-142-4 Question 17 (7 marks) The amount of water in a tank, 𝑊 litres, varies with time 𝑡, in minutes, and can be modelled by the equation 𝑊= 200 −185(1.2)−𝑡, 𝑡≥0. (a) Determine amount of water in the tank Solution 𝑊(0) = 15 𝐿 Specific behaviours ✔ correct value (i) initially. (1 mark) Solution 𝑊(15) = 188 𝐿 Specific behaviours ✔ correct value (ii) after 15 minutes. (1 mark) (b) Graph 𝑊 against 𝑡 for 0 ≤𝑡≤45 on the axes below. (3 marks) Solution See graph Specific behaviours ✔ 𝑦-intercept and (15, 188) ✔ asymptotic behaviour ✔ smooth curve",
