    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN245-142-3 D O N O T W RI TE IN TH IS A R EA Question 18 (8 marks) Two events 𝐴 and 𝐵 are such that 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) = 0.2, 𝑃(𝐵) = 0.5 and 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) = 𝑥. (a) Determine 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) when 𝑥= 0.15. (2 marks) (b) Determine an expression for 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) in terms of 𝑥. (1 mark) (c) Determine the value of 𝑥 when (i) 𝐴 and 𝐵 are independent. (2 marks) (ii) 𝐴 and 𝐵 are mutually exclusive. (1 mark) (iii) 𝑃(𝐴) = 0.6. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 23 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN245-142-4 Question 18 (8 marks) Two events 𝐴 and 𝐵 are such that 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) = 0.2, 𝑃(𝐵) = 0.5 and 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) = 𝑥. (a) Determine 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) when 𝑥= 0.15. (2 marks) Solution 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) = 𝑃(𝐵) −𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) = 0.5 −0.15 = 0.35 Specific behaviours ✔ use of Venn diagram or other method ✔ correct probability (b) Determine an expression for 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) in terms of 𝑥. (1 mark) Solution 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) = 0.5 −𝑥 Specific behaviours ✔ correct expression (c) Determine the value of 𝑥 when (i) 𝐴 and 𝐵 are independent. (2 marks) Solution 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) = 𝑃(𝐴) × 𝑃(𝐵)0.5 −𝑥 = (0.2 + 0.5 −𝑥) × 0.5𝑥= 0.3 Specific behaviours ✔ uses rule for independence ✔ correct value",
