    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN245-142-3 D O N O T W RI TE IN TH IS A R EA Question 19 (7 marks) A right circular cone of base radius 10 cm and height 25 cm stands on a horizontal surface. A cylinder of radius 𝑥 cm and volume 𝑉 cm3 stands inside the cone with its axis coincident with that of the cone and such that the cylinder touches the curved surface of the cone as shown. (a) Show that 𝑉= 25𝜋𝑥2 −2.5𝜋𝑥3. (3 marks) (b) Given that 𝑥 can vary, use a calculus method to determine the maximum value of 𝑉. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 25 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN245-142-4 Question 19 (7 marks) A right circular cone of base radius 10 cm and height 25 cm stands on a horizontal surface. A cylinder of radius 𝑥 cm and volume 𝑉 cm3 stands inside the cone with its axis coincident with that of the cone and such that the cylinder touches the curved surface of the cone as shown. (a) Show that 𝑉= 25𝜋𝑥2 −2.5𝜋𝑥3. (3 marks) Solution From similar triangles ℎ 10 −𝑥= 25 10 ⇒ℎ= 25 −2.5𝑥 Hence 𝑉= 𝜋𝑟2ℎ𝑉= 𝜋𝑥2(25 −2.5𝑥) = 25𝜋𝑥2 −2.5𝜋𝑥3 Specific behaviours ✔ relation between 𝑥 and ℎ using similar triangles ✔ expresses ℎ in terms of 𝑥 ✔ substitutes into cylinder volume formula (b) Given that 𝑥 can vary, use a calculus method to determine the maximum value of 𝑉. Solution 𝑑𝑉 𝑑𝑥= 50𝜋𝑥−7.5𝜋𝑥2 𝑑𝑉 𝑑𝑥= 0 𝑤ℎ𝑒𝑛 𝑥= 0, 𝑥= 20 3 𝑥= 0 ⇒𝑉= 0 (𝑚𝑎𝑥𝑖𝑚𝑢𝑚)",
