    "questionText": "MATHEMATICS 5 CALCULATOR ASSUMED Question 8 (12 marks) The line AB, 27 3 = + y x cuts both of the lines OP and CD. OP and CD are parallel to each other. OP is represented by the equation x y 3 = . 5 - 5 10 20 Y x A B x + 3 y = 27 O - 9 P D C y = 3 x Angle V H (a) Write the equation of the line CD. (2 marks) Solution 𝑦= 3𝑥−9 (b) Find the vertical intercept at V and the horizontal intercept at H. (2 marks) Solution 𝑎𝑡 𝑥= 0 →𝑦= 9 𝑎𝑡 𝑦= 0 →𝑥= 27 ∴𝑉= (0,9) 𝑎𝑛𝑑 𝐻= (27,0) (c) Using (b), find the angle (in degrees), to 1 decimal place, the line AB makes with the horizontal axis as shown in the diagram. (2 marks) Solution 𝜃= tan−1( 9 27) 𝜃= 18.40 MATHEMATICS 6 CALCULATOR ASSUMED (d) Find the coordinates of both points where the line AB intersects the lines OP and CD. (4 marks) Solution 𝐿𝑖𝑛𝑒 𝐴𝐵: 𝑦= 27 −𝑥 3 𝐿𝑖𝑛𝑒 𝑂𝑃: 𝑦= 3𝑥 𝐿𝑖𝑛𝑒 𝐶𝐷: 𝑦= 3𝑥−9 27−𝑥 3 = 3𝑥 and 27−𝑥 3 = 3𝑥−9 𝑥= 2.7 → 𝑦= 8.1 𝑥= 5.4 → 𝑦= 7.2 ∴ (2.7, 8.1) 𝑎𝑛𝑑 (5.4, 7.2) ✔ equating line AB and OP ✔ equating line AB and CD ✔✔ two coordinates (e) Find the length of the sloping side VH to 2 decimal places. (2 marks) Solution 92 + 272 = 𝑉𝐻2 28.46 𝑢𝑛𝑖𝑡𝑠= 𝑉𝐻",
