    "questionText": "MATHEMATICS 15 CALCULATOR ASSUMED Question 15 (9 marks) (a) Integrate (𝑥+1)(2𝑥−1) 2𝑥5 with respect to x. Express your answer with exactly 4 terms and without any negative exponents. (3 marks) Solution ∫(𝑥+ 1)(2𝑥−1) 2𝑥5 𝑑𝑥= ∫2𝑥2 + 𝑥−1 2𝑥5 𝑑𝑥 = ∫𝑥−3 + 𝑥−4 2 −𝑥−5 2 𝑑𝑥 = −𝑥−2 2 − 𝑥−3 6 + 𝑥−4 8 +C = − 1 2𝑥2 − 1 6𝑥3 + 1 8𝑥4 + 𝑐 ✔ correct antiderivative ✔ positive exponents ✔ C (b) Justify the relevance of adding an arbitrary constant 𝐶 in finding the antiderivatives of functions. (1 mark) Solution Adding a constant C, accounts for the fact that there are families of curves which will have the same derivative. Unless we are given a point in the function, we can only write a general form for the antiderivative. MATHEMATICS 16 CALCULATOR ASSUMED (c) The figure below shows the curve 𝐶 which meets the coordinate axes at the points 𝑃, 𝑄 and 𝑅. The gradient function of 𝐶 is given by 𝑓′(𝑥) = 3 −4𝑥 and that 𝑓(1) = 2𝑓(2), determine the coordinates of the points 𝑃, 𝑄 and 𝑅. (5 marks) Solution 𝑓′(𝑥) = 3 −4𝑥 → 𝑓(𝑥) = 3𝑥−2𝑥2 + 𝑐 3 −2 + 𝑐= 2(6 −8 + 𝑐) 𝑐= 5 𝑓(𝑥) = −2𝑥2 + 3𝑥+ 5 → 𝑓(0) = 5 → 0 = −2𝑥2 + 3𝑥+ 5 0 = (𝑥+ 1)(2𝑥−5) →𝑥= −1, 5 2 ∴ 𝑄 𝑖𝑠 (0,5), 𝑃 𝑖𝑠 (−1,0) 𝑎𝑛𝑑 𝑅 𝑖𝑠 (5 2 , 0). ✔ finding the function ✔ correct value for c ✔✔✔ coordinates for 𝑃, 𝑄 𝑎𝑛𝑑 𝑅 MATHEMATICS 17 CALCULATOR ASSUMED END OF SECTION 2 MATHEMATICS 18 CALCULATOR ASSUMED Additional working space Question number: _____________________________ MATHEMATICS 19 CALCULATOR ASSUMED Additional working space Question number: _____________________________ MATHEMATICS 20 CALCULATOR ASSUMED Additional working space Question number: _____________________________",
