    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-162-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 10 (5 marks) For the events 𝐴 and 𝐵, 𝑃(𝐴) = 0.52 and 𝑃(𝐵) = 0.25. Determine 𝑃(𝐴∪𝐵) when (a) 𝐴 and 𝐵 are mutually exclusive. (1 mark) (b) 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵̅) = 0.33. (1 mark) (c) 𝑃(𝐴̅ ∩𝐵̅) = 0.33. (1 mark) (d) 𝐴 and 𝐵 are independent. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-162-4 Question 10 (5 marks) For the events 𝐴 and 𝐵, 𝑃(𝐴) = 0.52 and 𝑃(𝐵) = 0.25. Determine 𝑃(𝐴∪𝐵) when (a) 𝐴 and 𝐵 are mutually exclusive. (1 mark) (b) 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵̅) = 0.33. (1 mark) (c) 𝑃(𝐴̅ ∩𝐵̅) = 0.33. (1 mark) (d) 𝐴 and 𝐵 are independent. (2 marks) Solution 𝑃(𝐴∪𝐵) = 0.52 + 0.25 = 0.77 Specific behaviours  correct probability Solution 𝑃(𝐴∪𝐵) = 0.33 + 0.25 = 0.58 Specific behaviours  correct probability Solution 𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵) = 0.52 × 0.25 = 0.13 𝑃(𝐴∪𝐵) = 0.52 + 0.25 −0.13 = 0.64 Specific behaviours  𝑃(𝐴∩𝐵)  correct probability Solution 𝑃(𝐴∪𝐵) = 1 −0.33 = 0.67 Specific behaviours  correct probability",
