    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-162-4 Question 12 (8 marks) Part of the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) is shown below, where 𝑓(𝑥) = 5𝑥 2𝑥+ 1. Points 𝐴 and 𝐵 lie on the curve and have 𝑥-coordinates of 0.5 and 2 respectively. (a) Draw the chord to the curve between 𝐴 and 𝐵 on the axes above and determine the gradient of this chord. (3 marks) Point 𝐶, with an 𝑥-coordinate of 0.5 + ℎ, lies on the curve between 𝐴 and 𝐵. The gradient of the chord 𝐴𝐶 is 𝑚𝐴𝐶. (b) Calculate 𝑚𝐴𝐶 for the values of ℎ shown in the table below, recording the gradients in the table to 3 decimal places. (3 marks) ℎ 1 0.5 0.1 0.05 0.01 𝑚𝐴𝐶 0.625 𝟎. 𝟖𝟑𝟑 𝟏. 𝟏𝟑𝟔 𝟏. 𝟏𝟗𝟎 𝟏. 𝟐𝟑𝟖 Solution See table Specific behaviours  one correct gradient  at least three correct gradients  all correct gradients ( just comment on incorrect rounding) Solution 𝑚= 𝑓(2) −𝑓(0.5) 2 −0.5 = 2 −1.25 1.5 = 0.5 Specific behaviours  draws chord on graph  correct 𝑦-values  correct gradient",
