    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-162-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 15 (6 marks) A farmer was treating a large area of land for an invasive weed. The area treated on the first day was 275 m2. Over the following months more resources were utilised so that the area treated each day was 7.5% more than the previous day. (a) Determine the area treated on the 28th day. (2 marks) The cost of the treatment was 35.8 cents per square metre. (b) On which day did the cost of the days treatment first exceed $10 000? (2 marks) (c) Determine the total cost of the first 15 days of treatment. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-162-4 Question 15 (6 marks) A farmer was treating a large area of land for an invasive weed. The area treated on the first day was 275 m2. Over the following months more resources were utilised so that the area treated each day was 7.5% more than the previous day. (a) Determine the area treated on the 28th day. (2 marks) The cost of the treatment was 35.8 cents per square metre. (b) On which day did the cost of the days treatment first exceed $10 000? (2 marks) (c) Determine the total cost of the first 15 days of treatment. (2 marks) Solution 𝐶𝑛= 0.358 × 275(1.075)(𝑛−1) = 98.45(1.075)(𝑛−1) 98.45(1.075)(𝑛−1) ≥10 000 𝑛≥65 On day 65. Specific behaviours  adjusts sequence/indicates equation to solve  correct day Solution 𝐶𝑜𝑠𝑡= $10 000 / 0.358 = $27932.96 Uses table recursive on CAS On day 65. Specific behaviours  correct cost  correct day Solution 𝑆15 = 98.45(1 −1.07515) 1 −1.075 = $2 571.35 Specific behaviours  indicates use of sum formula  total cost Solution Uses table recursive on CAS 𝑆15 = 7182.55 Cost = 7182.55 x 0.358 = $2571.35 Specific behaviours  correct 𝑆15  correct cost Solution 𝑇28 = 275(1.075)(28−1) = 1 9",
