    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN085-162-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 16 (6 marks) When an alternating current is used to power a light globe, the intensity of light emitted from the globe, 𝐼 lumens, varies with time 𝑡 milliseconds and can be modelled by the formula 𝐼= 240 + 110 cos(0.08𝜋𝑡). (a) Draw the graph of 𝐼 against 𝑡 on the axes below for 0 ≤𝑡≤50. (3 marks) (b) State the period of 𝐼. (1 mark) (c) Determine the percentage (to the nearest percent) of each cycle that the intensity of light is below 175 lumen. (2 marks)",
