    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 12 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-162-4 Question 17 (9 marks) (a) Point 𝐴(11, −5) lies on the circumference of a circle with centre (−4, 3). Determine the equation of the circle. (3 marks) (b) The graph of 𝑦= 1 + 𝑎 𝑥+ 𝑏 passes through the points (1, −2) and (3, 4). (i) Determine the value of each of the integer constants 𝑎 and 𝑏. (3 marks) Solution (𝑥+ 4)2 + (𝑦−3)2 = 𝑘 Using given point: 152 + (−8)2 = 𝑘⇒𝑘= 289 (= 172) Equation: (𝑥+ 4)2 + (𝑦−3)2 = 289 Specific behaviours  forms equation using centre  uses points to find k value or correct radius  correct equation (any form) Solution −2 = 1 + 𝑎 1 + 𝑏, 4 = 1 + 𝑎 3 + 𝑏 Solve simultaneously for 𝑎= 3, 𝑏= −2. Specific behaviours  uses points to form two equations  correct 𝑎  correct 𝑏",
