    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-162-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 18 (13 marks) A small body is moving in a straight line. Relative to a fixed point 𝑂, it has a displacement of 𝑥 cm at time 𝑡 seconds given by 𝑥(𝑡) = 2𝑡3 −19𝑡2 + 52𝑡−35, 0 ≤𝑡≤6. (a) Obtain an expression for the velocity of the body in the form 𝑣(𝑡) = (𝑎𝑡+ 𝑏)(𝑐𝑡+ 𝑑), where 𝑎, 𝑏, 𝑐 and 𝑑 are integer constants. (3 marks) (b) Determine (i) the initial velocity of the body. (1 mark) (ii) the displacement of the body at the instant(s) that it is stationary. (3 marks) CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 METHODS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN085-162-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF (c) Use the axes below to sketch the displacement of the body over the given domain. (3 marks) (d) State the number of times the body passed through 𝑂 and determine the minimum speed and maximum speed of the body as it passed through this point. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-162-4 Question 18 (13 marks) A small body is moving in a straight line. Relative to a fixed point 𝑂, it has a displacement of 𝑥 cm at time 𝑡 seconds given by 𝑥(𝑡) = 2𝑡3 −19𝑡2 + 52𝑡−35, 0 ≤𝑡≤6. (a) Obtain an expression for the velocity of the body in the form 𝑣(𝑡) = (𝑎𝑡+ 𝑏)(𝑐𝑡+ 𝑑), where 𝑎, 𝑏, 𝑐 and 𝑑 are integer constants. (3 marks) (b) Determine (i) the initial velocity of the body. (1 mark) (ii) the displacement of the body at the instant(s) that it is stationary. (3 marks) Solution 𝑣(𝑡) = 𝑑𝑥 𝑑𝑡 = 6𝑡2 −38𝑡+ 52 = 2(𝑡−2)(3𝑡−13) = (2𝑡−4)(3𝑡−13) (or = (𝑡−2)(6𝑡−26)) Specific behaviours  uses derivative of 𝑥(𝑡) to find 𝑣(𝑡)  correct derivative  factors into required form Solution 𝑣(0) = 52 cm/s Specific behaviours  correct velocity Solution 𝑣(𝑡) = 0 ⇒𝑡= 2, 𝑡= 13 3 𝑥(2) = 9 cm 𝑥(13 3 ) = −100 27 ≈−3.70 cm Specific behaviours  times when stationary  one correct displacement  both correct, with units",
