    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 METHODS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN085-162-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 20 (9 marks) The shaded region 𝐴𝐵𝑀 in the diagram is a canvas awning and is part of a sector of circle 𝑂𝐴𝐵 with centre 𝑂 and radius 4.2 m. 𝐵𝑀 is a straight line from 𝐵 to 𝑀, the midpoint of 𝑂𝐴. The size of ∠𝐴𝑂𝐵 is 0.9 radians. (a) Determine the area of sector 𝑂𝐴𝐵. (2 mark) (b) Determine the area of the canvas awning. (3 marks) (c) The edge of the canvas is to be reinforced with thin wire. Determine the length of wire required. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 METHODS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN085-162-4 Question 20 (9 marks) The shaded region 𝐴𝐵𝑀 in the diagram is a canvas awning and is part of a sector of circle 𝑂𝐴𝐵 with centre 𝑂 and radius 4.2 m. 𝐵𝑀 is a straight line from 𝐵 to 𝑀, the midpoint of 𝑂𝐴. The size of ∠𝐴𝑂𝐵 is 0.9 radians. (a) Determine the area of sector 𝑂𝐴𝐵. (2 mark) (b) Determine the area of the canvas awning. (3 marks) (c) The edge of the canvas is to be reinforced with thin wire. Determine the length of wire required. (4 marks) (or Arc𝐴𝐵=4.2 x 0.9 =3.78) Solution 𝐴𝑂𝐴𝐵= 0.5(4.2)2 × 0.9 = 7.938 m2 Specific behaviours  shows use of area formula  correct sector area Solution 𝐴𝑂𝑀𝐵= 0.5(4.2)(2.1) sin(0.9) = 3.454 𝐴𝐴𝐵𝑀= 𝐴𝑂𝐴𝐵−𝐴𝑂𝑀𝐵 = 7.938 −3.454 = 4.484 m2 Specific behaviours  indicates use of difference of areas  area of triangle  correct area Solution 𝐵𝑀2 = 4.22 + 2.12 −2(4.2)(2.1) cos(0.9) 𝐵𝑀= 3.329 Arc𝐴𝐵= 3.2 × 1.3 = 3.78 𝐿= 2.1 + 3.329 + 3.78 = 9.21 m Specific behaviours  uses cosine rule for 𝐵𝑀  length of 𝐵𝑀  arc length 𝐴𝐵  correct length",
