    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN085-102-3 Question 11 (6 marks) Line 𝐿1 has equation 5𝑥−2𝑦= 20. (a) Sketch the graph of 𝐿1. (2 marks) (b) Determine the equation of line 𝐿2 that is parallel to 𝐿1 and passes through the point with coordinates (−3, −11). (2 marks) (c) Determine the equation of line 𝐿3 that is perpendicular to 𝐿1 and has the same 𝑦-intercept as 𝐿1. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 5 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN085-102-4 Question 11 (6 marks) Line 𝐿1 has equation 5𝑥−2𝑦= 20. (a) Sketch the graph of 𝐿1. (2 marks) (b) Determine the equation of line 𝐿2 that is parallel to 𝐿1 and passes through the point with coordinates (−3, −11). (2 marks) (c) Determine the equation of line 𝐿3 that is perpendicular to 𝐿1 and has the same 𝑦-intercept as 𝐿1. (2 marks) Solution 5(−3) −2(−11) = −15 + 22 = 7 5𝑥−2𝑦= 5 (or 𝑦= 5 2 𝑥−7 2) Specific behaviours ✓ uses correct gradient ✓ states equation Solution 2𝑥+ 5𝑦= 𝑘 2(0) + 5(−10) = −50 2𝑥+ 5𝑦= −50 (or 𝑦= −2 5 𝑥−10) Specific behaviours ✓ uses correct gradient ✓ states equation Solution See graph Specific behaviours ✓ labelled intercepts ✓ straight line",
