    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN085-102-4 Question 13 (6 marks) The quadratic function 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑎𝑥2 + 𝑏𝑥+ 𝑐 passes through 𝑃(5, 9) and has roots at 𝑥= −4 and 𝑥= 7. (a) Determine the values of the constants 𝑎, 𝑏 and 𝑐. (3 marks) (b) State the location of the 𝑦-intercept of the graph 𝑦= −3𝑓(𝑥). (1 mark) (c) State the location of the roots of the graph 𝑦= 𝑓(4𝑥). (2 marks) Solution 𝑦= −3(14) = −42 Specific behaviours ✓ correct 𝑦-value Solution 𝑥= 1 4 (−4) = −1 𝑥= 1 4 (7) = 7 4 = 1.75 Specific behaviours ✓ uses correct horizontal dilation ✓ correct 𝑥-values Solution 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑎(𝑥+ 4)(𝑥−7) 𝑓(5) = 9 = 𝑎(9)(−2) 𝑎= −1 2 𝑓(𝑥) = −1 2 (𝑥+ 4)(𝑥−7) = −1 2 𝑥2 + 3𝑥 2 + 14 𝑎= −1 2 = −0.5, 𝑏= 3 2 = 1.5, 𝑐= 14 Specific behaviours ✓ writes in factored form ✓ uses given point to determine 𝑎 ✓ expands and clearly states all values",
