    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-102-3 Question 16 (8 marks) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥 is shown below, where 𝑎 is a positive constant. (a) On the same axes, sketch and label the graphs of (i) 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥−3. (2 marks) (ii) 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥−2. (2 marks) (b) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥−3 intersects the graph of 𝑦= 1.2𝑥 when 𝑥= 2.1. Determine, giving your answers to 3 significant figures, (i) the 𝑦-coordinate of the point of intersection. (1 mark) (ii) the value of the constant 𝑎. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 10 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-102-4 Question 16 (8 marks) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥 is shown below, where 𝑎 is a positive constant. (a) On the same axes, sketch and label the graphs of (i) 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥−3. (2 marks) (ii) 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥−2. (2 marks) (b) The graph of 𝑦= 𝑎𝑥−3 intersects the graph of 𝑦= 1.2𝑥 when 𝑥= 2.1. Determine, giving your answers to 3 significant figures, (i) the 𝑦-coordinate of the point of intersection. (1 mark) (ii) the value of the constant 𝑎. (3 marks) Solution See graph Specific behaviours (i) ✓ y-int close to (0, 5); ✓ touches x-axis close to (9, 0) (ii) ✓ y-int at (0, -1); ✓ clear asymptote at 𝑦= −2 Solution 𝑦= 1.22.1 = 1.466495 … ≈1.47 (3sf) Specific behaviours ✓ value that rounds to 1.47 Solution 𝑎2.1−3 = 1.22.1 𝑎= 0.653497 … 𝑎≈0.653 (3sf) Specific behaviours ✓ writes equation ✓ writes solution to equation ✓ rounds answers to (b)(i) & (ii) correctly",
