    "calculator": "Calculator-assumed",
    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN085-102-3 Question 17 (8 marks) A particle is moving along a straight line so that its displacement, 𝑥 metres, from a fixed point 𝑂 after 𝑡 seconds is given by 𝑥= 5 −18𝑡 5 + 12𝑡2 5 −2𝑡3 5 ⁡. (a) Sketch the displacement of the particle on the axes below for 0 ≤𝑡≤5. (3 marks) (b) Determine the velocity dx dt of the particle when 𝑡= 0.5. (2 marks) (c) For how long during the first five seconds is the particle is moving towards 𝑂? (1 mark) (d) Circle the point on the graph where the particle is moving with the maximum velocity and explain what feature of the graph you used to choose this point. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 See next page SN085-102-4 Question 17 (8 marks) A particle is moving along a straight line so that its displacement, 𝑥 metres, from a fixed point 𝑂 after 𝑡 seconds is given by 𝑥= 5 −18𝑡 5 + 12𝑡2 5 −2𝑡3 5 . (a) Sketch the displacement of the particle on the axes below for 0 ≤𝑡≤5. (3 marks) (b) Determine the velocity of the particle when 𝑡= 0.5. (2 marks) (c) For how long during the first five seconds is the particle is moving towards 𝑂? (1 mark) (d) Circle the point on the graph where the particle is moving with the maximum velocity and explain what feature of the graph you used to choose this point. (2 marks) Solution See graph. Velocity is maximum at point where curve has greatest positive slope. Specific behaviours ✓ indicates point of inflection ✓ explanation Solution 3 seconds (for 0 < 𝑡< 1 and 3 < 𝑡< 5). Specific behaviours ✓ correct time Solution 𝑣= −(6𝑡2 −24𝑡+ 18) 5 𝑣(0.5) = −3 2 = −1.5 m/s Specific behaviours ✓ differentiates displacement ✓ states velocity Solution (a) See graph Specific behaviours ✓ through (0, 5) & (5, -3) ✓ turning points located correctly ✓ smooth curve",
