    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of questions SN085-102-3 Question 21 (8 marks) A composite solid is made from a cone and a cylinder, both of height ℎ cm and radius 𝑟 cm, as shown below. The dimensions are such that the sum of ℎ and 3𝑟 is 36 cm. (a) Show that the volume of the solid is given by 𝑉= 48𝜋𝑟2 −4𝜋𝑟3. (3 marks) (b) Use differentiation to determine the values of 𝑟 and ℎ that will maximise the volume of the solid, and state this maximum volume. (5 marks) CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 Additional working space Question number: _________ METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED Additional working space Question number: _________ CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 19 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 Additional working space Question number: _________",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of questions SN085-102-4 Question 21 (8 marks) A composite solid is made from a cone and a cylinder, both of height ℎ cm and radius 𝑟 cm, as shown below. The dimensions are such that the sum of ℎ and 3𝑟 is 36 cm. (a) Show that the volume of the solid is given by 𝑉= 48𝜋𝑟2 −4𝜋𝑟3. (3 marks) (b) Use differentiation to determine the values of 𝑟 and ℎ that will maximise the volume of the solid, and state this maximum volume. (5 marks) Solution ℎ+ 3𝑟= 36 ⇒ℎ= 36 −3𝑟 𝑉= 1 3 𝜋𝑟2ℎ+ 𝜋𝑟2ℎ = 4 3 𝜋𝑟2ℎ = 4 3 𝜋𝑟2(36 −3𝑟) = 48𝜋𝑟2 −4𝜋𝑟3 Specific behaviours ✓ writes ℎ in terms of 𝑟 ✓ substitutes into sum of cone and cylinder volumes ✓ simplifies Solution 𝑑𝑉 𝑑𝑟= 96𝜋𝑟−12𝜋𝑟2 = 0 when 𝑟= 0, 8 Optimum value of 𝑟= 8 cm ℎ= 36 −3(8) = 12 cm 𝑉(8) = 1024𝜋 cm3 (≈3217) Specific behaviours ✓ differentiates ✓ determines root of derivative ✓ states optimum value of 𝑟 ✓ calculates height ℎ ✓ calculates volume 𝑉",
    "questionImage": "generated/resource-previews/docx-pdf-cache-waep-2017-yr11-meth-u12-s2-c22364a999-p016-question-33e91739ee.jpg",
