    "answerText": "D (c) At what time, when the seat was rising, did it first reach a height of 11 metres? (1 mark) Solution \u0000\u0000 = 41.3 s Specific behaviours ✓ time that rounds to 41 s (d) Determine the change in height of the seat between \u0000\u0000 = 130 and \u0000\u0000 = 131, giving your answer rounded to the nearest cm. (2 marks) Solution ℎ(130) = 2.74, ℎ(131) = 3.26 \u0000\u0000ℎ = 3.26 − 2.74 = 0.52 m Specific behaviours ✓ determines both heights ✓ states difference to nearest cm See next page SN078-122-4 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 13 METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 Question 19 (7 marks) (a) Part of the circle \u0000\u00002 + \u0000\u00002 = \u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000 + \u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000 + \u0000\u0000 is shown below. Determine the values of the constants \u0000\u0000, \u0000\u0000 and \u0000\u0000. (4 marks) Solution (\u0000\u0000 − 3)2 + (\u0000\u0000 + 2)2 = 62 \u0000\u00002 + \u0000\u00002 = 6\u0000\u0000 − 4\u0000\u0000 + 23 \u0000\u0000 = 6, \u0000\u0000 = −4, \u0000\u0000 = 23 Specific behaviours ✓ circle in factored form ✓ correct radius and centre ✓ expands into required form ✓ correct values of \u0000\u0000, \u0000\u0000 and \u0000\u0000",
