    "questionText": "D O N O T W R I T E I N T H I S (b) The graph of a power function \u0000\u0000 = \u0000\u0000(\u0000\u0000) is shown below. A R E A A S I T W I L L B E C U T O F F (i) Draw the tangent to the curve when \u0000\u0000 = −0.5. (1 mark) (ii) Use the tangent to estimate \u0000\u0000′(−0.5). (2 marks) SN078-122-3 See next page METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED Question 20 (8 marks) A diagnostic test for a disease has a 97% chance of giving the correct outcome and it is known that 0.5% of all sheep on a station have the disease. It can be assumed that the correct outcome of the test is independent of whether a sheep has the disease. (a) A sheep is randomly selected for the test from those on the station. Determine the probability that (i) the sheep has the disease, but the test indicates that it does not. (2 marks) F F O T (ii) the sheep actually has the disease if the test indicates that it does. (4 marks) U C E B L L I W T I S A A E R A S I H T N I E T I R W T O N O D (b) Two sheep are randomly selected for the test from those on the station. Determine the probability that just one of the sheep is diagnosed correctly. (2 marks) See next page SN078-122-3",
    "answerText": "(ii) Use the tangent to estimate \u0000\u0000′(−0.5). (2 marks) Solution \u0000\u0000′(−0.5) ≈ −1.62≈ −0.8 Specific behaviours ✓ uses gradient of tangent ✓ value −1 ≤ \u0000\u0000 ≤ −0.7 SN078-122-4 See next page METHODS UNITS 1 AND 2 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED Question 20 (8 marks) A diagnostic test for a disease has a 97% chance of giving the correct outcome and it is known that 0.5% of all sheep on a station have the disease. It can be assumed that the correct outcome of the test is independent of whether a sheep has the disease. (a) A sheep is randomly selected for the test from those on the station. Determine the probability that (i) the sheep has the disease, but the test indicates that it does not. (2 marks) Solution \u0000\u0000 = 0.005 × 0.03 =3 20 000 = 0.000 15 Specific behaviours ✓ indicates multiplication of correct probabilities ✓ correct probability F F O T (ii) the sheep actually has the disease if the test indicates that it does. (4 marks) U C E Solution \u0000\u0000(\u0000\u0000 ∩ \u0000\u0000) = 0.005 × 0.97 = 0.00485 \u0000\u0000(\u0000\u0000̅ ∩ \u0000\u0000) = 0.995 × 0.03 = 0.02985 \u0000\u0000(\u0000\u0000) = 0.00485 + 0.02985 = 0.0347 \u0000\u0000(\u0000\u0000|\u0000\u0000) =0.00485 0.0347 =97 694 ≈ 0.140 Specific behaviours",
