    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 6 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-182-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 11 (9 marks) A function is defined by 𝑓(𝑥) = 𝑥4 −6𝑥2 + 8𝑥+ 13. (a) Use calculus to determine the coordinates of all stationary points of the graph 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥), and then use the sign test to determine their nature. (5 marks) (b) Sketch the graph of 𝑦= 𝑓(𝑥) on the axes below for −3 ≤𝑥≤3. (4 marks)",
