    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 METHODS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN085-182-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 12 (8 marks) Data from repairs to 405 smartphones showed that 274 of them were Android. The type of repair was classified as battery or other, and of the 136 smartphones that required battery repairs, 98 were Android. (a) Complete the missing entries in the table below. (3 marks) Battery Other Total Android Not Android Total 136 405 (b) Determine the probability that a randomly selected smartphone from those repaired (i) did not require a battery repair. (1 marks) (ii) was an Android smartphone or required battery repairs. (2 marks) (iii) did not require a battery repair given that it was an Android smartphone. (2 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 7 METHODS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN085-182-4 Question 12 (8 marks) Data from repairs to 405 smartphones showed that 274 of them were Android. The type of repair was classified as battery or other, and of the 136 smartphones that required battery repairs, 98 were Android. (a) Complete the missing entries in the table below. (3 marks) Battery Other Total Android 98 176 274 Not Android 38 93 131 Total 136 269 405 (b) Determine the probability that a randomly selected smartphone from those repaired (i) did not require a battery repair. (1 marks) * Part (b) allow follow through from (a), No need to simplify fraction for probability. If rounded to 2dp -1 mark once. Solution 𝑃(𝐵̅) = 269 405 ≈0.664 Specific behaviours  correct probability (ii) was an Android smartphone or required battery repairs. (2 marks) (iii) did not require a battery repair given that it was an Android smartphone. (2 marks) Specific behaviours records 98 correctly  274 and 131 correct  all correct in table Solution 274 + 136 −98 = 312 𝑃(𝐴∪𝐵) = 312 405 = 104 135 ≈0.770 Specific behaviours  calculates numerator  correct probability Solution 274 −98 = 176 𝑃(𝐵̅|𝐴) = 176 274 = 88 137 ≈0.642 Specif",
