    "questionText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN085-182-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 16 (5 marks) The sum of the first 𝑛 terms of a sequence is given by 𝑆𝑛= 4𝑛2 + 7𝑛. (a) Determine 𝑆4. (1 mark) (b) Determine 𝑇4, where 𝑇𝑛 is the 𝑛th term of the sequence. (1 mark) (c) Determine a simplified rule for the 𝑛th term of the sequence. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 11 METHODS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN085-182-4 Question 16 (5 marks) The sum of the first 𝑛 terms of a sequence is given by 𝑆𝑛= 4𝑛2 + 7𝑛. (a) Determine 𝑆4. (1 mark) (b) Determine 𝑇4, where 𝑇𝑛 is the 𝑛th term of the sequence. (1 mark) (c) Determine a simplified rule for the 𝑛th term of the sequence. (3 marks) Alternative Solution 𝑇𝑛= 𝑆𝑛−𝑆𝑛−1 = 4𝑛2 + 7𝑛−(4(𝑛−1)2 + 7(𝑛−1)) =4𝑛2 + 7𝑛−4𝑛2 + 8𝑛−4 −7𝑛 + 7 𝑇𝑛= 8𝑛+ 3 Specific behaviours  forms equation  expands and simplifies  correct rule simplified Solution 𝑆4 = 4(4)2 + 7(4) = 92 Specific behaviours  correct value Solution 𝑆3 = 4(3)2 + 7(3) = 57 𝑇4 = 𝑆4 −𝑆3 = 92 −57 = 35 Specific behaviours  calculates 𝑇4 Solution 𝑇1 = 𝑆1 = 11 𝑇2 = 𝑆2 −𝑇1 = 30 −11 = 19 𝑑= 𝑇2 −𝑇1 = 19 −11 = 8 𝑇𝑛= 11 + (𝑛−1)(8) = 8𝑛+ 3 Specific behaviours  𝑇1 = 11  calculates common difference  correct rule simplified",
