    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-182-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 19 (10 marks) The graph of the hyperbola 𝑦= 𝑎 𝑥+ 𝑏 is shown below, where 𝑎 and 𝑏 are constants. (a) State the equations of all asymptotes of the hyperbola. (2 marks) (b) Determine the value of 𝑎 and the value of 𝑏. (2 marks) CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 15 METHODS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN085-182-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF (c) Add the line 𝑦= 2𝑥+ 3 to the graph of the hyperbola and state the number of points of intersection it will have with the hyperbola. (2 marks) (d) The line 𝑦= 𝑚𝑥+ 3 is tangential to the hyperbola, where 𝑚 is a constant. Use an algebraic method to determine all possible values of 𝑚. (4 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 14 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-182-4 Question 19 (10 marks) The graph of the hyperbola 𝑦= 𝑎 𝑥+ 𝑏 is shown below, where 𝑎 and 𝑏 are constants. (a) State the equations of all asymptotes of the hyperbola. (2 marks) (b) Determine the value of 𝑎 and the value of 𝑏. (2 marks) Solution Horizontal: 𝑦= 0 Vertical: 𝑥= 3. Specific behaviours  equation for horizontal asymptote  equation for vertical asymptote Solution From asymptote, 𝑏= −3. Using (0, −1): −1 = 𝑎 0 −3 ⇒𝑎= 3 Specific behaviours  value of 𝑎  value of 𝑏",
