    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-182-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 20 (9 marks) Three small weights 𝐴, 𝐵 and 𝐶, each attached to a spring, are oscillating vertically above level ground. The height, ℎ cm, above the ground of each weight at time 𝑡 seconds, 𝑡≥0, is given by ℎ𝐴= 16 cos (3𝜋𝑡 4 ) + 20, ℎ𝐵= 12 sin(3𝜋𝑡 4 ) + 25, ℎ𝐶= 12 cos(5𝜋𝑡 4 ) + 20. (a) State which two weights are oscillating with the same amplitude, and state what this common amplitude is. (1 mark) (b) State which two weights are oscillating with the same period, and state what this common period is. (2 marks) (c) State which of the weights reaches furthest above the ground, state this height and find the time at which it first reaches this position. (3 marks) CALCULATOR-ASSUMED 17 METHODS UNITS 1&2 See next page SN085-182-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF (d) Determine the length of time during the first 3 seconds for which ℎ𝐶> ℎ𝐴> ℎ𝐵, correct to 3 decimal places. (3 marks)",
    "answerText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 16 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED See next page SN085-182-4 Question 20 (9 marks) Three small weights 𝐴, 𝐵 and 𝐶, each attached to a spring, are oscillating vertically above level ground. The height, ℎ cm, above the ground of each weight at time 𝑡 seconds, 𝑡≥0, is given by ℎ𝐴= 16 cos (3𝜋𝑡 4 ) + 20, ℎ𝐵= 12 sin(3𝜋𝑡 4 ) + 25, ℎ𝐶= 12 cos(5𝜋𝑡 4 ) + 20. (a) State which two weights are oscillating with the same amplitude, and state what this common amplitude is. (1 mark) (b) State which two weights are oscillating with the same period, and state what this common period is. (2 marks) (c) State which of the weights reaches furthest above the ground, state this height and find the time at which it first reaches this position. (3 marks) Solution Weights 𝐵 and 𝐶 - their amplitude is 12 cm. Specific behaviours  correct weights and amplitude Solution ℎ𝐴= 20 + 16 = 36, ℎ𝐵= 25 + 12 = 37, ℎ𝐶= 20 + 12 = 32 Hence weight 𝐵 reaches furthest above the ground with a height of 37 cm. When: sin(3𝜋𝑡 4 ) = 1 ⇒3𝜋𝑡 4 = 𝜋 2 ⇒𝑡= 2 3 This first occurs when 𝑡= 2 3 s. Specific behaviours  states correct weight  states this height (with units)  states correct time (with units) Solution Weights 𝐴 and 𝐵 - th",
