    "questionText": "METHODS UNITS 1&2 18 CALCULATOR-ASSUMED End of Questions SN085-182-2 DO NOT WRITE IN THIS AREA AS IT WILL BE CUT OFF Question 21 (7 marks) A length of wire 72 cm long is cut into two pieces. One piece is bent into a right triangle with sides of length 3𝑥, 4𝑥 and 5𝑥 cm and the other piece is bent into a square of side 𝑦 cm. (a) Show that the combined area of the triangle and square in terms of 𝑥 is 𝐴= 15𝑥2 −108 𝑥+ 324 (3 marks) (b) Use a calculus method to determine the value of 𝑥 that minimises this combined area and state this minimum area. (4 marks) © 2021 WA Exam Papers. Rossmoyne Senior High School has a non-exclusive licence to copy and communicate this document for non-commercial, educational use within the school. No other copying, communication or use is permitted without the express written permission of WA Exam Papers. SN085-182-2.",
    "answerText": "Question 21 (7 marks) A length of wire 72 cm long is cut into two pieces. One piece is bent into a right triangle with sides of length 3𝑥, 4𝑥 and 5𝑥 cm and the other piece is bent into a square of side 𝑦 cm. (a) Show that the combined area of the triangle and square in terms of 𝑥 is 𝐴= 15𝑥2 −108 𝑥+ 324 (3 marks) Solution 12𝑥+ 4𝑦= 72 ⇒𝑦= 18 −3𝑥 𝐴= 1 2 (4𝑥)(3𝑥) + 𝑦2 = 6𝑥2 + (18 −3𝑥)2 = 15𝑥2 −108𝑥+ 324 Specific behaviours  equation relating 𝑥 and 𝑦  total area in terms of 𝑥 and 𝑦  total area in terms of 𝑥 (a) Use a calculus method to determine the value of 𝑥 that minimises this combined area and find this minimum area. (4 marks) Solution 𝑑𝐴 𝑑𝑥= 30𝑥−108 30𝑥−108 = 0 𝑥= 18 5 = 3.6 𝐴(3.6) = 15(3.6)2 −108(3.6) + 324 = 648 5 = 129.6 The minimum total area is 129.6 cm2. Specific behaviours  derivative  equates derivative to 0  optimum value of 𝑥  calculates and states minimum area",
