    "answerText": "Page 2 of 4 Question 3. [6 marks: 3, 3] Solve for 𝑥𝑥 in each of the following, showing all working: (a) 252𝑥𝑥+1 = √125 (b) 32𝑥𝑥+1 = 8(3𝑥𝑥) + 3 Question 4. [4 marks: 2, 2] The first three terms of an arithmetic progression are 𝑥𝑥, 5𝑥𝑥 - 8 and 3𝑥𝑥 + 8 respectively. (a) Show that 𝑥𝑥 = 4 (b) Find the value of 21st term in this sequence? 52(2𝑥𝑥+1) = 5 3 2 4𝑥𝑥+ 2 = 3 2 𝑥𝑥= −1 8 3(3𝑥𝑥)(3𝑥𝑥) −8(3𝑥𝑥) −3 = 0 (3 × 3𝑥𝑥+ 1)(3𝑥𝑥−3) = 0 3𝑥𝑥= −1 3 (𝑛𝑛𝑛𝑛 𝑠𝑠𝑠𝑠𝑠𝑠𝑠𝑠𝑠𝑠𝑠𝑠𝑠𝑠𝑠𝑠)𝑜𝑜𝑜𝑜 3𝑥𝑥= 3 X = 1, (5𝑥𝑥 - 8) - (𝑥𝑥) = (3𝑥𝑥 + 8)-(5𝑥𝑥 - 8) => 4𝑥𝑥 -8 = -2𝑥𝑥 +16 => 6𝑥𝑥 = 24 => 𝑥𝑥 = 4 a= 4, d = 8 21th term = 4 + 20 x 8 = 164",
