    "questionText": "Page 2 of 4 Question 8. [ 6 marks: 1, 1, 2, 2 ] Maths department at Rossmoyne Senior High School purchased a new photocopier for $3 250. Its value depreciates at a rate of 4.5 cents per copy. Let 𝑉𝑛 be the value of the photocopier in dollars after 𝑛 copies have been made, where 𝑉𝑛= 𝑎+ 𝑏𝑛. (a) State the value of the constant 𝑎 and the value of the constant 𝑏. (b) Calculate the value of the photocopier after 44 000 copies have been made. (c) Determine 𝑛 when 𝑉𝑛= 2647. (d) The photocopier will be replaced as soon as its value falls below $350. Determine the number of copies the photocopier will make before it is replaced.",
    "answerText": "Page 2 of 4 Question 8. [6 marks: 1, 1, 2, 2 ] Maths department at Rossmoyne Senior High School purchased a new photocopier for $3 250. Its value depreciates at a rate of 4.5 cents per copy. Let 𝑉𝑉𝑛𝑛 be the value of the photocopier in dollars after 𝑛𝑛 copies have been made, where 𝑉𝑉𝑛𝑛= 𝑎𝑎+ 𝑏𝑏𝑏𝑏. (a) State the value of the constant 𝑎𝑎 and the value of the constant 𝑏𝑏. (b) Calculate the value of the photocopier after 44 000 copies have been made. (c) Determine 𝑛𝑛 when 𝑉𝑉𝑛𝑛= 2647. (d) The photocopier will be replaced as soon as its value falls below $350. Determine the number of copies the photocopier will make before it is replaced. a=3250 b=-0.045 350 = 3250 – 0.045 n n=64444.4444444 n = 64445 2647 = 3250 – 0.045 n n=13400 𝑉𝑉44000 = 3250 −0,045 × 44000=$1270",
