    "calculator": "Unlabelled",
    "questionText": "Page 3 of 4 Question 9. [ 7 marks: 2, 1, 2, 2 ] Water collected from Serpentine River contained microorganisms. In the laboratory, a chemical cocktail was added to the water to aid in the proliferation of the microorganisms. The total bacteria (B) in the sample was measured in thousands for 28 days and was found to relate to time, t (days) by the formula, 𝐵= 𝑎(𝑘𝑡). The accompanying graph contains data points from the data logger. (a) Use an appropriate method to find the values of a and k. Give the value of a to the nearest 1000 and the values of k to 3 decimal places. (b) Predict the population after 40 days. (c) How many days will it take for the total bacteria count to reach 150 000? (d) A water sample from the Swan River was mixed with the same chemical cocktail and studied over the same time period and its total bacteria count, C, is given as 𝐶= 80(0.95)𝑡. Determine when the two total bacteria counts are equal?",
    "answerText": "Page 3 of 4 Question 9. [7 marks: 2, 1, 2, 2] Water collected from Serpentine River contained microorganisms. In the laboratory, a chemical cocktail was added to the water to aid in the proliferation of the microorganisms. The total bacteria (B) in the sample was measured in thousands for 28 days and was found to relate to time, t (days) by the formula, 𝐵𝐵= 𝑎𝑎(𝑘𝑘𝑡𝑡). The accompanying graph contains data points from the data logger. (a) Use an appropriate method to find the values of a and k. Give the value of a to the nearest 100 and the values of k to 3 decimal places. (b) Predict the population after 40 days. 261.33 (c) How many days will it take for the total bacteria count to reach 150 000? (d) Water sample from the Swan River was mixed with the same chemical cocktail and studied over the same time period and its total bacteria count, C, is given as 𝐶𝐶= 80(0.95)𝑡𝑡. Determine when the two total bacteria counts are equal? Use (0,10) (10, 22.61) to solve a and k a = 10, k = 1.085 B=10 x 1.085^40=261.33 150=10 x 1.085^t t=33.195 days or round to 34 days 80 x 0.95^t=10 x 1.085^t t = 15.65 days",
