    "questionText": "Page 4 of 4 Question 10. [ 7 marks: 1, 2, 2, 2 ] The events A and B are such that P(A) = 0.4 and P(B) = 0.5. Determine P(A ∪ B) in each of the following cases: (a) A and B are mutually exclusive. (b) P ( A ∪ B’ ) = 0.75 (c) A and B are independent. (d) P ( B | A’ ) = 𝟕 𝟏𝟐",
    "answerText": "Page 4 of 4 Question 10. [7 marks: 1, 2, 2, 2 ] The events 𝐴𝐴 and 𝐵𝐵 are such that 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴) = 0.4 and 𝑃𝑃(𝐵𝐵) = 0.5. Determine 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴 ∪ 𝐵𝐵) in each of the following cases: (a) 𝐴𝐴 and 𝐵𝐵 are mutually exclusive. (b) 𝑃𝑃( 𝐴𝐴 ∪ 𝐵𝐵’ ) = 0.75. (c) 𝐴𝐴 and 𝐵𝐵 are independent. (d) 𝑃𝑃( B | A’ ) = 𝟕𝟕 𝟏𝟏𝟏𝟏 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴 ∪ 𝐵𝐵) = 0.4 + 0.5 = 0.9 𝑃𝑃(𝐵𝐵 ∩ 𝐴𝐴̅) = 1 − 0.75 = 0.25 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴 ∪ 𝐵𝐵) = 0.4 + 0.25 = 0.65 = 13 20 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴 ∩ 𝐵𝐵) = 0.4 × 0.5 = 0.2 𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴 ∪ 𝐵𝐵) = 0.4 + 0.5 − 0.2 = 0.7 𝑃𝑃 (𝐵𝐵|𝐴𝐴̅) =𝑃𝑃(𝐵𝐵 ∩ 𝐴𝐴̅)/𝑃𝑃(𝐴𝐴̅) 𝑃𝑃 (𝐵𝐵 ∩ 𝐴𝐴̅) = (1 − 0.4) × 𝟕𝟕 𝟏𝟏𝟏𝟏= 0.35 𝑃𝑃 (𝐴𝐴 ∪ 𝐵𝐵) = 0.4 + 0.35 = 0.75",
