    "answerText": "Question 3 (1.1.14) (2, 2, 2 = 6 marks) A rectangular hyperbola has asymptotes with equation 𝑥= −2 and 𝑦= 4. a) Write two possible equations for this function Solution 𝑦= 𝑎 𝑥+2 + 4 so a could be any number eg 𝑦= 1 𝑥+2 + 4 and 𝑦= −1 𝑥+2 + 4 Specific behaviours ✓✓ two possible equations b) Write the equation of this function if it has a y-intercept at (0,5) Solution 5 = 𝑎 0+2 + 4 so a=2 Specific behaviours ✓ substitutes correctly into equation ✓a=2 c) Write the equation of this function if it passes through the point (3,5) Solution 5 = 𝑎 3+2 + 4 so a=5 therefore y= 5 𝑥+2 + 4 Specific behaviours ✓ substitutes correctly into equation ✓ states equation",
