    "questionText": "Mathematics Department Perth Modern 3 | P a g e Question 3 [8 marks – 1, 2, 2, 3] (2.3.7, 12-15, 22) a) Differentiate the following: i) 𝑓(𝑥) = 4𝑥5 −9𝑥4 ii) 𝑦= (2𝑥+ 3)(6𝑥−7) b) Anti-differentiate the following: i) 𝑑𝑦 𝑑𝑥= 24𝑥3 + 27𝑥2 ii) 𝑓′(𝑥) = 12𝑥5 − 9𝑥2 6𝑥2",
    "answerText": "Mathematics Department Perth Modern 3 | P a g e Question 3 [8 marks – 1, 2, 2, 3] (2.3.7, 12-15, 22) a) Differentiate the following: i) 𝑓(𝑥) = 4𝑥5 −9𝑥4 Solution 𝑓′(𝑥) = 20𝑥4 −36𝑥3 Specific behaviours ✓ Differentiates ii) 𝑦= (2𝑥+ 3)(6𝑥−7) Solution 𝑦 = 12𝑥2 + 4𝑥−21 𝑑𝑦 𝑑𝑥 = 24𝑥+ 4 Specific behaviours ✓ Expands ✓ Differentiates Award full marks if product rule is used correctly b) Anti-differentiate the following: i) 𝑑𝑦 𝑑𝑥= 24𝑥3 + 27𝑥2 Solution 𝑦 = ∫(24𝑥3 + 27𝑥2)𝑑𝑥 = 6𝑥4 + 9𝑥3 + 𝑐 Specific behaviours ✓ Anti-differentiates ✓ Adds constant Penalise once only for missing constant ii) 𝑓′(𝑥) = 12𝑥5 − 9𝑥2 6𝑥2 Solution 𝑓(𝑥) = ∫(12𝑥5 − 9𝑥2 6𝑥2 ) 𝑑𝑥 = ∫(2𝑥3 −3 2) 𝑑𝑥, 𝑥≠0 = 1 2 𝑥4 −3 2 𝑥+ 𝑐, 𝑥≠0 Specific behaviours ✓ Rearranges (no need to state 𝑥≠0) ✓ Anti-differentiates ✓ Adds constant",
